            "text": "[{\"description\":\"Mondays // 13 January – 31 March* //  *No class 17 February // 2pm – 3:30pm, £20 per session, £198 for the 11 weeks // \\r\\n\\r\\nAlso available online Join Paula as she brilliantly tackles the news of the week. Topics are generated by you, and the issues of the day.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\" Current Affairs for Winter 2025 [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450002AGTKDLTPJKCNBKVNSKJBRTLNBMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The electric true story behind the rise of one of the most iconic singer-songwriters in history. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 141 Minutes \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. This may vary with specific screenings, and we always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":141,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/ef7bbdcc-c6ea-439a-91c0-3da7c530be37.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Complete Unknown\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 February-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/ef7bbdcc-c6ea-439a-91c0-3da7c530be37-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":\"completeunknown\",\"id\":\"476001APSDBVNKMJGPSRBPQGDVDRSCRLK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-02T19:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T10:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10:30am – 12noon // £192 for the 12 weeks only (can't book individual sessions) // Judaism and Christianity are two of the closest of the world’s religions. But differences in beliefs and rituals have historically led to significant divisions, often resulting in injustice and violence when political power was unequal. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn the modern era, however, relations have improved, fostering mutual appreciation. Angela will explore this evolving relationship, focusing on the modern period through historical case studies and diverse materials.\\r\\n\\r\\nAngela has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She is the author of over 40 books on aspects of religion and history, and is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Family Affair? The Story of Jewish-Christian Relations\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450801AQGCCNMRHQTGHCBTRHJDVQNTKQH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Angela Gluck\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £20, off site, meeting location provided after booking // This gentle stroll among the leafy streets of Swiss Cottage uncovers many and varied 20th century Jewish connections.  \\r\\n\\r\\nFocussing on the German/Austrian emigres of the 1930s including Freud and his family, stories also include the founding of Belsize Square Shul, a young refugee who became an award-winning author, the AJR, the Royal Family’s favourite sculptor, schlagsahne (whipped cream) at the Cosmo, and the Primrose Club for surviving children arriving post war. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A History of Jewish Hampstead\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 May-7 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492201AVPTHRSBJSDKKQVCHGPJKRLGMBM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-07T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-07T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Kolsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mismatched cousins David (Jesse Eisenberg) and Benji (Kieran Culkin) reunite for a tour through Poland to honor their beloved grandmother. The adventure takes a turn when the odd-couple's old tensions resurface against the backdrop of their family history.\\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 90 minutes \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/777d1612-49e9-4134-b8dd-b1ad89665ed9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Real Pain\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 January-20 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/777d1612-49e9-4134-b8dd-b1ad89665ed9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470801AVJSQCKVJBJPVSJRVCPVNDRKVQP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-12T18:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, building, £20 // Two nights before the Lord’s Test, Daniel Lightman returns by popular demand to regale us with the best of Jewish cricketing stories. Daniel will be joined by speakers including former England captain Mike Brearley OBE, and Roland Butcher, the first Black cricketer to play for England. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDaniel has co-curated the current (and first ever) exhibition at the MCC Museum on Jews and Cricket, and his articles in Wisden, The Cricketer and Nightwatchman have revealed hitherto unknown stories of the lives of Jewish (and Jew-ish) cricketers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Third Annual Evening of Cricket\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 July-8 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485603AHGSKKTHJPKQBGCDVLMQGSRDNKM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-08T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-08T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Daniel Lightman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.30pm, £17, in building // 18+ // ‘A Way Too Honest Confession About Motherhood’ is the true story of award-winning TV producer Danielle Lauren’s bumpy start to motherhood.\\r\\nTwo years ago, Danielle was living the dream—working with Hollywood A-listers and travelling around the world as a thought leader. Then she became a mum, and her entire world fell apart. What followed was an identity crisis of epic proportions, an emotional rollercoaster and a desperate search for the woman she used to be.\\r\\nIn this raw, funny* and poignant one-woman show, Danielle invites audiences to step into her motherhood journey as she openly explores the complexities, contradictions, and humour that come with claiming the title \\\"mother.\\\"\\r\\n* swearing included\\r\\nTrigger warning: This dynamic talk contains sensitive material related to maternal mental health and is suitable for audiences 18 plus.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Way Too Honest Confession About Motherhood\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-5 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491601ALRLGMLMVKMVKMKBRSTQRKSHQNM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Warren Schmidt has arrived at several of life's crossroads all at the same time. To begin with, he is retiring from a lifetime of service as an actuary for Woodmen of the World Insurance Company, and he feels utterly adrift. Furthermore, his only daughter Jeannie is about to marry a boob. And his wife Helen dies suddenly after 42 years of marriage. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 5m \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":125,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/2b3bc6b0-3bca-4057-bae2-971859f412ef.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"About Schmidt\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/2b3bc6b0-3bca-4057-bae2-971859f412ef-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481601ANHGJQGMDPNMQDDPBKRKCMGDHNC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-17T16:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T16:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays 1.30pm - 2.30pm, Come and join JW3s regular students who organise this weekly debate choosing the topics and debaters on each side. Hear their voices and add your own. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Abraham Debating Club\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 April-26 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"505601AQGCBQDHQQDKLRLKNRJKVRNLRJN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-26T13:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 16 January – 3 April, 1.30pm - 2.30pm, £7 \\r\\n\\r\\nStudents organise this weekly debate choosing the subjects and debaters on each side. Join them to hear their voices and your own. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Abraham Debating Club - Winter 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 January-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450201ASRPSCSQMHKPPVRRCBDBQHCSTVN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T13:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thu 22 May 2025 //\\r\\n7:00pm // \\r\\n£20 // Anthony Julius is Deputy Chairman at law firm Mishcon de Reya and holds the Chair in Law and Arts in the Faculty of Laws, UCL. As a lawyer, he is best known for his successful defence of historian Deborah Lipstadt in the libel case brought by David Irving.  As a scholar, he is the author of the widely praised Trials of the Diaspora: A History of Anti-Semitism in England, amongst other books.\\r\\n\\r\\nRabbi Michael Pollak is an educational consultant and Ethics & Religion teacher at Hendon School. He is also Director of Education at Yad Vashem UK.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbraham: The First Jew\\r\\nBy Anthony Julius\\r\\n\\r\\nPublished by Yale University Press\\r\\n\\r\\nThe story of Abraham, the first Jew, portrayed as two lives lived by one person, paralleling the contradictions in Judaism throughout its history. In this new biography of Abraham - Judaism’s foundational figure - Anthony Julius offers an account of the origins of a fundamental struggle within Judaism between scepticism and faith, critique and affirmation, thinking for oneself and thinking under the direction of another.\\r\\n\\r\\nJulius describes Abraham’s life as two separate lives, and as a version of the collective life of the Jewish people. Abraham’s first life is an early adulthood of questioning the polytheism of his home city of Ur Kasdim until its ruler, Nimrod, condemns him to death and he is rescued, he believes, by a miracle. In his second life, Abraham’s focus is no longer on critique but rather on conversion and on his leadership over his growing household, until God’s command that he sacrifice his son Isaac. This test, the Akedah (or “Binding”), ends with another miracle, as he believes, but as Julius argues, it is also a catastrophe for Abraham. The Akedah represents for him an unsurpassed horizon—and in Jewish life thereafter. This book focuses on Abraham as leader of the first Jewish project, Judaism, and the unresolvable, insurmountable crisis that the Akedah represents—both in his leadership and in Judaism itself.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Abraham: The First Jew\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 May-22 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"484001ALSBSMSJGLMTNCLTHVJMRPTVPMN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"English\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Anthony Julius and Rabbi Michael Pollak\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"For those wishing to add pizza to the film ticket for Young JW3 x Seret Film Festival: Pink Lady\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":0,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Add Pizza\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"505401ARJBPMQQPTMJTQKPNNGQBVRDKGJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wed 04 June 2025 //\\r\\n7:15pm //\\r\\n£20 // As the Barbican prepares to unveil “Encounters: Giacometti” from 8 May 2025 – 1 May 2026, we are delighted to welcome back Sophie Lachowsky to explore the work of Alberto Giacometti. \\r\\n\\r\\nBorn into a family of painters, sculptors, and architects, Giacometti devoted his career to the interplay between form and space. His elongated, solitary figures are among the most iconic sculptures of modern art. Shaped by the devastation of postwar Europe, his body of work offers a profound reflection on the human condition. Imbued with emotional intensity and a timeless quality, Giacometti’s art continues to inspire and resonate with contemporary artists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSophie Lachowsky is an art historian, lecturer, and writer with experience in the culture and heritage sectors. She has given talks at many leading cultural institutions, and bespoke guided tours of major collections. She writes and lectures on modern and contemporary art, with a focus on modernist sculptors.  She is a trustee of The Showroom, a non-profit contemporary art space, in London.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Alberto Giacometti: An encounter between Being and Nothingness\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 June-4 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485201AHGNGHNDNRMKKQCBHHCVNTSRJCD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-04T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-04T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sophie Lachowsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"12.30pm–1.45pm // £12 per session or £50 for the 5 weeks // Intergenerational Movement classes welcome adults of all ages, whether you’ve danced before or are stepping onto the floor for the first time.  //  Each session invites you to tune into your body, explore movement through playful imagery and build confidence alongside others. You’ll develop technical and creative skills while forging new social connections. // With gentle improvisations and simple exercises designed to suit everyone, especially those over 50, our classes are accessible, energising and full of joy. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"All Ages Movement Class\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489601AHLRMQQHSHDTBHVLLDBLSDCJSVB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T12:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Yael Flexer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"8pm-9.15pm, £25, in building // Join us for an intimate solo gig with treasured Australian singer-songwriter, Lior, for his only European date.  \\r\\n\\r\\nCelebrating 20 years since the ground-breaking album, Autumn Flow, as well as his original song for the Gladiator II soundtrack.\\r\\n\\r\\nRenowned for his beautiful voice and songs that radiate truth and sincerity, Lior burst on to the Australian music scene in 2005 with his debut album, Autumn Flow. It has become one of the most successful independent debut releases in Australian music history. That year Lior earned 3 ARIA nominations including ‘Best Male Artist’ as well as Triple J’s ‘J Award’ nomination for ‘Australian Album of the Year’. He has subsequently released five more albums whilst remaining a completely independent artist. He has earned a total of 7 ARIA nominations and is a 2-time ARIA award-winner.\\r\\n\\r\\nHe has toured extensively both in Australia and internationally. He has been a regular performer at arts festivals and WOMAD festivals internationally, including an entire season at the Edinburgh Festival.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An Evening with Lior\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 March-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483401AJKLDRQSGMQLCCQPDNTGVRVJVJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-23T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-23T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Lior\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.15-8.30pm, £20, building only // From the Bauhaus School in Weimar to Black Mountain College, Yale and their beloved Mexico, Anni and Josef Albers produced pivotal artworks and influential theories that defined the history of the 20th century. Their groundbreaking methods of teaching and making transcended architecture, craft, design and the visual arts.\\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover how these two pioneers transformed the way we see colour, forms, materials and the process of creation.\\r\\n\\r\\nSophie is a lecturer and writer with experience in the culture and heritage sectors. She has given talks at Kenwood House and the Courtauld Gallery and bespoke guided tours of the Wallace Collection.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Anni and Josef Albers: Iconic Couple of Modernism\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 March-12 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453601ATLTSMQPCQJLPGTMMRRLBDDRJSK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sophie Lachowsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // The Annual Spiro Tribute Lecture is sponsored by the Pears Foundation to celebrate the tremendous work of Robin (z\\\"l) and Nitza Spiro and their contribution to Jewish cultural life in Britain over the last 40+ years. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis year we are honoured to welcome David Quarry and Aldo Henriques. \\r\\n\\r\\nDavid was British Ambassador in Israel and is now the permanent British representative to NATO, based in Brussels. Aldo is an expert on Culture and worked for the British Council in Israel. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Annual Spiro Tribute 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455001ASRMHBCKSGHKCQQSLCKDBRNNMKC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\" David Quarry and Aldo Henriques\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Customers book with Bump and Baby Club, not us // \\r\\n£260 per couple for the course // Feel confident, prepared and excited for the arrival of your baby and gain a new set of friends to share the journey with.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur invaluable antenatal course for expectant parents covers everything you need to know about labour, birth and the early days of parenthood, including baby first aid.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Antenatal Classes with Bump and Baby Club\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 January-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"469002AKJKHRHQVNCCMDHBDSTRRGMBNMT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-09T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-17T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am – 12.15pm // £20 per session or £108 for the 6 weeks // Ever wondered how a constitutional monarchy differs from a Presidential system? Or realised that you had no idea why the French Assembly didn't have the power of the Knesset?  // Paula explores and examines different political systems of democracy - how they were created, why they were created in that way and what do those structures mean for the governance of a country. // \\r\\nEach session is a standalone class but with the common theme of how that country's political system works. Paula will looks at the USA, France, the UK, Russia, Italy, Germany and Israel. Never be confused by a Primary or a regional ballot again! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Are All Democracies Equal? [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489202AVKLHTGLBPDTVLNLDLRSKJJRKMJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-30T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am – 12.15pm // £20 per session or £108 for the 6 weeks // Ever wondered how a constitutional monarchy differs from a Presidential system? Or realised that you had no idea why the French Assembly didn't have the power of the Knesset? // Paula explores and examines different political systems of democracy - how they were created, why they were created in that way and what do those structures mean for the governance of a country. // Each session is a standalone class but with the common theme of how that country's political system works. Paula will looks at the USA, France, the UK, Russia, Italy, Germany and Israel. Never be confused by a Primary or a regional ballot again!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Are All Democracies Equal? [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489203AKNRRJHPGPTLVVQVDBTCSJTLQKK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-30T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The electric true story behind the rise of one of the most iconic singer-songwriters in history. Credits Rating: 15 Genre: Biography, Drama, Music Director: James Mangold Stars: Timothée Chalamet, Edward Norton, Elle Fanning\\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 21m\\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":199,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: A Complete Unknown\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-3 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"476201ARHTKHDDDPQTJBDJGPBBNVRNSLD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The Impressionists are the most popular group in art history – millions flock every year to marvel at their masterpieces. But, to begin with, they were scorned, penniless outsiders. 1874 was the year that changed everything; the first Impressionists, “hungry for independence”, broke the mould by holding their own exhibition outside official channels. Impressionism was born and the art world was changed forever. What led to that first groundbreaking show 150 years ago? Who were the maverick personalities that wielded their brushes in such a radical and provocative way? The spectacular Musée d’Orsay exhibition brings fresh eyes to this extraordinary tale of passion and rebellion. The story is told not only by historians and curators, but in the words of those who witnessed the dawn of Impressionism: the artists, press and people of Paris, 1874. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 30m  \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/33329e63-24a5-4180-a77f-de4b42e0b9c8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Exhibition on Screen: Dawn of Impressionism: Paris 1874\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-28 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/33329e63-24a5-4180-a77f-de4b42e0b9c8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499802AVCLDCJBNBLJQJRHLNMNKDNHPMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Reunited with Leigh for the first time since multiple Oscar-nominated Secrets and Lies, the astonishing Marianne Jean-Baptiste plays Pansy, a woman wracked by fear, tormented by afflictions, and prone to raging tirades against her husband, son, and anyone who looks her way. Meanwhile, her easy-going younger sister, played by Michele Austin (Another Year), is a single mother with a life as different from Pansy's as their clashing temperaments -- brimming with communal warmth from her salon clients and daughters alike. This expansive film from a master dramatist takes us into the intensities of kinship, duty, and the most enduring of human mysteries: that even through lifetimes of hurt and hardship, we still find ways to love those we call family. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rated: 12A, Duration: 1 hour 37 minutes\\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":97,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/380dec1b-6e8c-4a37-b546-ca384232d9ec.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Hard Truths\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 February-17 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/380dec1b-6e8c-4a37-b546-ca384232d9ec-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"475601ASDNHPPJDSPQGJLJPCHCKPNMLQR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-17T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-17T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Rachel Samstat (Meryl Streep), a New York food critic, beds Mark Forman (Jack Nicholson), a Washington, D.C., newspaper columnist. The two fall in love, and Rachel relinquishes her job and relocates to be with a man who views himself as unfit for marriage. They try to build a life together -- literally -- as they struggle with the construction crews renovating their home. When Rachel gets pregnant, Mark is enthusiastic, but then soon begins doubting whether he could be a family man. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 48m \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":108,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/0abb5b0a-6f73-4d11-a00f-0681f5af5453.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Heartburn\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 March-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/0abb5b0a-6f73-4d11-a00f-0681f5af5453-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"482601ALDLRRKDNDMRSPBDCLJQBPRHKDH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"124 // 15 // Maria Callas, the world's greatest opera singer, lives the last days of her life in 1970s Paris, as she confronts her identity and life.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Maria\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 January-27 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471801ALNNPRJDKSVCRVKDSRLVLTBLPKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Grace Pudel is a lonely misfit with an affinity for collecting ornamental snails and an intense love for books. At a young age, when Grace is separated from her fire-breathing twin brother Gilbert, she falls into a spiral of anxiety and angst. Despite a continued series of hardships, inspiration and hope emerge when she strikes up an enduring friendship with an elderly eccentric woman named Pinky, who is full of grit and lust for life | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 35m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/437bb655-2395-47be-891d-26f5ae6bb887.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Memoir of a Snail\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 March-3 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/437bb655-2395-47be-891d-26f5ae6bb887-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480401ACKBDMNTMQMHPDPGSBMMMQSDVQN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-03T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-03T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mr. Burton tells the true story of the relationship between Port Talbot schoolmaster Philip Burton and a wild young schoolboy called Richard Jenkins, the son of a wayward drunk. Richard dreamed of becoming an actor, but his ambitions were in danger of being derailed by a combination of family trouble, the pressure of war, and his own lack of discipline. Mr. Burton recognized the raw talent in his pupil, becoming his tutor, strict taskmaster and eventually his adoptive father. | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one. | Rating: 12A, Duration: 2h 4m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9e7bfee7-cc0c-4636-84cc-a35bdda73ab9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Mr Burton\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 May-19 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9e7bfee7-cc0c-4636-84cc-a35bdda73ab9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"508401ANLQLNJMHPNPRDGTDTCNLDGGHQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Set during the 1972 Munich Summer Olympics, the film follows an American Sports broadcasting team that quickly adapted from sports reporting to live coverage of the Israeli athletes taken hostage. Through this lens, \\\"September 5\\\" provides a fresh perspective on the live broadcast seen globally by an estimated one billion people at the time. At the heart of the story is Geoff (John Magaro), a young and ambitious producer striving to prove himself to his boss, the legendary TV executive Roone Arledge (Peter Sarsgaard). Together with German interpreter Marianne (Leonie Benesch) and his mentor Marvin Bader (Ben Chaplin), Geoff unexpectedly takes the helm of the live coverage. As narratives shift, time ticks away, and conflicting rumors spread, with the hostages' lives hanging in the balance, Geoff grapples with tough decisions while confronting his own moral compass.\\r\\nRated: 15 | 1 hour 35 minutes\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1fdadc56-469d-4d40-80fa-31d99e7e2d88.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: September 5\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 February-24 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1fdadc56-469d-4d40-80fa-31d99e7e2d88-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"475401AVBPMKKLJGQGMHHRJSKJHRSVTNG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-24T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-24T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A live-action musical reimagining of the classic 1937 film. Starring Rachel Zegler in the title role and Gal Gadot as her Stepmother, the Evil Queen, the magical music adventure journeys back to the timeless story with beloved characters Bashful, Doc, Dopey, Grumpy, Happy, Sleepy, and Sneezy. | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one. | Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 49m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":109,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/f6f92e78-51e2-47d5-a854-977fb08e2390.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Snow White\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 May-26 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/f6f92e78-51e2-47d5-a854-977fb08e2390-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"508601AKKNLSBBKHPDJNBLNMMVKSMQQSR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-26T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-26T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"124 // PG// During her family's move to the suburbs, a sullen 10-year-old girl wanders into a world ruled by gods, witches and spirits, and where humans are changed into beasts.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Spirited Away\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-6 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470201ADHPDMTLLSBMNQQCLQQLSBSHDPT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When the glittering Las Vegas revue she has headlined for decades announces it will soon close, glamorous showgirl Shelly (Pamela Anderson) must reconcile with the decisions she’s made and the life she has built as she plans her next act whilst also striving to repair the relationship with her daughter (Billie Lourd). With an outstanding ensemble cast that includes Jamie Lee Curtis, Dave Bautista, Brenda Song and Kiernan Shipka, The Last Showgirl is a joyous tribute to a long-gone Las Vegas – and all the women who made it glitter. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 28m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":88,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b9799b6f-cf04-47e9-9730-e8bf8297e33c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: The Last Showgirl\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 March-17 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b9799b6f-cf04-47e9-9730-e8bf8297e33c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481201ALJSVRSCMPSPLCHBLJGBMKSQDSQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-17T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-17T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"108 // 15 // An up-and-coming chef and a recent divorcée find their lives forever changed when a chance encounter brings them together, in a decade-spanning, deeply moving romance.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":108,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: We Live in Time\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 January-20 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471401ATMHGCKPVLCKPNJJLPGSRNJKMLK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-20T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-20T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6-8pm, age 13+, £10 // Get ready for an unforgettable night as the most talented young musicians hit the stage, delivering their best performances in our first Battle of the Bands competition, compered by Chlo Spinks.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWe are thrilled to announce the shortlisted bands: The Shambles, The Warriors, Unrelated, Infertile Crabs, Kto Tam?, The Souvenirs, and The Curlies. \\r\\n\\r\\nThese bands will go head-to-head, showcasing their skills and passion as they compete for the top spot, and judged by an esteemed panel of music industry professionals.\\r\\n\\r\\nWho will steal the show and take home the crown? Be there and witness the next big stars in the making! \\r\\n\\r\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; Show starts at 6pm.\\r\\n\\r\\nUnder 13s will need to be accompanied by an adult.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Battle of the Bands\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 April-6 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"469401AJCRLKJDQJSQMJLMPHLHCVKMBMN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-06T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-06T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"\\\"More than 70 years after the Holocaust, children of survivors and refugees will explore together how it has affected their lives.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis workshop will be led by Gaby Glassman, a psychologist and psychotherapist who has facilitated second generation groups since the 1980s. \\r\\nOnline only event. \\r\\nExclusively for those who are second generation.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Being Second Generation\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-27 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"457801APKKVKDVKVKLNCSJVJQQNTGDLKT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-27T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-27T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Gaby Glassman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"As the world teeters on the brink of annihilation, Dietrich Bonhoeffer is swept into the epicenter of a deadly plot to assassinate Hitler. With his faith and fate at stake, Bonhoeffer must choose between upholding his moral convictions or risking it all to save millions of Jews from genocide. Will his shift from preaching peace to plotting murder alter the course of history or cost him everything? | Rating: 12A, Duration: 2h 13m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":133,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/2f2c26c3-4576-46da-83ac-a321f843b911.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bonhoeffer \",\"instanceDates\":\"11 March-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/2f2c26c3-4576-46da-83ac-a321f843b911-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481001APGDPSVVVTSCHCCVRKLJRLPDGSC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T13:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"In Bridget Jones: Mad About the Boy, Bridget is alone once again, widowed and now a single mother to 9-year-old Billy and 4-year-old Mabel, and is stuck in a state of emotional limbo, raising her children with help from her loyal friends and even her former lover, Daniel Cleaver.  Encouraged to forge a new path toward life and love, Bridget goes back to work and even tries out the dating apps, where she’s soon pursued by a dreamy and enthusiastic younger man. Now juggling work, home and romance, Bridget grapples with the judgment of the perfect mums at school, worries about Billy as he struggles with the absence of his father, and engages in a series of awkward interactions with her son’s rational-to-a-fault science teacher. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 4m\\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/f011b1be-a4ad-48f7-a9dd-94a27707d883.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bridget Jones: Mad About the Boy\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 March-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/f011b1be-a4ad-48f7-a9dd-94a27707d883-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480203ABQDCSQHPMVLTPRQRPGDCLJPGPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-30T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T12:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"19:30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £30 adult £15 student, in-building // (Brodsky Quartet have replaced the Doric Quartet, who were no longer available on this date)  // Schubert Quartettsatz - approx 9 minutes // Haydn Opus 54 String Quartet No. 2 in C Major - 4 pieces approx 20 minutes total // Interval 20 minutes //\\r\\nBeethoven Opus 132 String Quartet No. 15 in A minor - 5 pieces approx 43 minutes total // Since its formation in 1972 the Brodsky Quartet has performed over 3,500 concerts on the major stages of the world and released more than 60 recordings.\\r\\n\\r\\nA natural curiosity and insatiable desire to explore has propelled the group in many artistic directions and continues to ensure them not only a place at the very forefront of the international chamber music scene but also a rich and varied musical existence. Their energy and craftsmanship have attracted numerous awards and accolades worldwide, while ongoing educational work provides a vehicle for passing on experience and staying in touch with the next generation. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Brodsky Quartet\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 January-23 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"397801ABLRBSPQMSTJDHRHTPBQTKVKNLS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-23T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-23T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, £15, building only // Join Israeli-American photo artist Loli Kantor as she explores her poignant photo-book Call Me Lola, a deeply personal journey through history, memory and loss. Rooted in an archive of family documents and photographs, the book reflects on her father’s life across Poland, Russia, post-war Germany, France, and Israel, while also capturing Kantor’s attempt to connect with the mother she never knew. \\r\\n\\r\\nLoli will be in conversation with her daughter, Danna Heller, a curator and contributor to the book. They will discuss preserving family memory and address the emotional legacy of grief and loss. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Call Me Lola\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453602ADJCQRVBVNQTNNJJSHKMKVLQQMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Nice guy Sandy and charming schemer Jonathan meet as college roommates in the late 1940s. Sandy woos and eventually marries the sweetly virginal Susan without knowing that she had cheated on him with Jonathan. Years later, his marriage faltering, Sandy attempts to mimic Jonathan's promiscuous womanizing, while the misogynistic Jonathan finally tries his hand at monogamy with the gorgeous but emotionally needy Bobbie.\\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 18, Duration: 1h 38m\\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":98,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/42340d1d-09dc-4553-863a-0f579e5541b9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Carnal Knowledge\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 April-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/42340d1d-09dc-4553-863a-0f579e5541b9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"498601AGKMJVKKMMQRSNQVVTMRQLPLPJQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-01T19:55:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T15:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, £20, building only // Take a journey through human history to explore how Carnival has served as a pressure valve for humanity. Discover the customs, practices and celebrations, ranging from the bizarre to the chilling and festive. Learn how this concept relates to Judaism, particularly the festival of Purim, and the rich tradition of humour that has always been central to the Jewish people. \\r\\n\\r\\nRobert has been teaching theatre and drama for twenty years. He runs the King Alfred Phoenix Theatre in London and has written stage plays that have awarded him Time Out Critics' Choice. He’s also written for Radio 4.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Carnival Cravings: Our Human Right to Break from the Norm\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 March-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453401ACCKCGCLNMQMDPSCNLTPVLVRLRH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-05T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Purim\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, hybrid // One of the most popular actors during Hollywood’s Golden Age, Cary was born into poverty but soon rose to star in such classic films as North By Northwest, Charade, The Bishop’s Wife and Arsenic and Old Lace. \\r\\n\\r\\nA private man in real life who married five times, George examines his life and career.\\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge has worked in the media for over 35 years, latterly at the BBC where he was responsible for all feature films and non-UK TV series. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cary Grant: Rise To Stardom\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 February-24 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453201APKHTTCBVHNQCBHTCLJSVLDLBGB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-24T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-24T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £20, in building // An evening of live music and performance with West End actors to celebrate the works of celebrated composer, lyricist, actor and cabaret legend Anthony Newley. \\r\\n\\r\\nLovingly created by producer Neil Marcus and director Adam Lenson (Cable Street, Southwark Playhouse) with musical director Theo Jamieson (Everybody's Talking About Jamie).  \\r\\n\\r\\nAnthony Newley together with collaborator Leslie Bricusse wrote a slew of hits including Goldfinger for the Bond franchise, Candy Man, Pure Imagination and an incredible score for Charlie & The Chocolate Factory, and What Kind Of Fool Am I from Stop The World I Want To Get Off amongst many other songs. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Anthony Newley\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 June-29 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491401AMBRVMRMNKPHPSQMGPCCSNPSLPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-29T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-29T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.00pm, £20 // 15 minute interval at 8:10pm, event ends approx 9:15pm // An Evening Celebrating Poet, Playwright and Author Bernard Kops; An evening of poems, readings, excerpts from stage plays, clips and songs celebrating Bernard and we will hear from friends and family both live and on video. The line up will include Olivier Award Winner Elliot Levey (Cabaret/Giant) and George Layton (Oliver! - London Palladium/It Ain't Half Hot Mum)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Bernard Kops\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 February-16 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"468401ANKQQQPSTKKBNSBTJKSHHQGCSQP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-16T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-16T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £20 // 15-min interval at 8.10pm // An evening of music and performance to celebrate the works of award winning lyricist Don Black CBE(Born Free, Diamonds Are Forever, Billy, Sunset Boulevard, Tell Me On A Sunday).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Don Black\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 March-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"468601ABLVPJHHLMRKBJBKVQHBGGQRKJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-9.30pm, building only, £20 (includes book) // To mark the launch of Dr Keith Kahn-Harris's new book Everyday Jews, come and join the author and friends for an evening of silliness with a serious message. At a heavy and significant time for the Jewish people, Dr Kahn-Harris and guests will remind us that Jewish life can also be trivial and parochial. There will be interesting talks on boring Jewish things, there will be affectionate celebrations of Jewish communal incompetence, there will be Palwin cocktails and an Adon Olam karaoke session.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Everyday Jewishness: A Seriously Playful Evening\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 March-11 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450802ABTPDNNMNKTTBBLQLMSRTQSDHMD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-11T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Purim\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Keith Kahn Harris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"\\\"Join expert Political and Middle East analyst Jonathan Paris as he looks at:-\\r\\n• The Political Situation Inside Israel\\r\\n• Iran and the Bomb – Where are we Now\\r\\n• Israel, Saudi Arabia – Normalisation?\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications. \\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Challenges Facing the Middle East\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-30 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"458001APSJKDPHNJGMPRGMDMRRGNDSDQC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Israel & the Middle East\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"5pm-6:30pm, £5, in building // in Hebrew, ages 9+ // no interval // The incredible story of Oren Smadja, a shy boy from Ofakim, who, thanks to extraordinary determination, perseverance, and hard work, along with the support and belief of his father, became an Olympic medalist with international achievements. \\r\\nA moving story of the triumph of the Israeli spirit. \\r\\n\\r\\nOren Smadja will be present at the show and will answer questions from the audience. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Champion of Israel: The Powerful and Inspiring Story of Oren Smadja \",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"457201ANLTTPPVBKRGTHHMLGGCKBBCMNB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T17:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-9pm, £20, building only, ages 13+ // This powerful documentary explores themes of war, migration, and the refugee experience, with a poignant focus on the healing power of art. It tells the story of Marika Henriques, a Jewish girl hidden from the Nazis in a Budapest cellar during World War II. After escaping Communist Hungary following the 1956 Uprising, she trained as a Jungian therapist in England. Decades later, it was the creation of extraordinary art that allowed her to process her childhood trauma. Now in her 80s, Marika shares her story for the first time. The film has been celebrated with numerous accolades, including the prestigious NAAP Gravida Documentary Award. \\r\\n\\r\\nThere will be a Q&A with filmmaker, Sal Anderson and Gaby Glassman a psychologist and psychotherapist specialising in transgenerational transmission of trauma. The conversation will be moderated by journalist and producer Wendy Robbins. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chaos Dragon and the Light\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 February-13 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"456601AMCHDHCDTKKNPQCTVTMKNCPPKRN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-13T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-13T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £20, in building // The events of October 7 were unprecedented, leaving tens of thousands of Israeli children from both the Gaza Envelope and Northern Israel coping with trauma on an unimaginable scale. In such a crisis, neither authorities, experts, nor decision-makers were fully prepared to respond. The Hebrew University’s School of Social Work, together with the Haruv Institute—global leaders in child welfare research and training—developed treatment guidelines and trained professionals to identify and address trauma. Conversations with affected children revealed deep emotional scars, insecurity, and isolation, highlighting new challenges in trauma care.\\r\\nToday, the National Center for Innovation in Children’s Resilience and Mental Health, in collaboration with the Haruv Institute and the School of Social Work, is pioneering new approaches to trauma recovery. The central question remains: How can we best support these children?\\r\\nIn a special talk, Professor Asher Ben-Arieh will discuss how the Hebrew University and the Haruv Institute helped shape Israel’s response. He will explore their collaboration with the government and the IDF in building a rehabilitation framework for children returning from captivity, as well as those coping with other traumas, emphasising the urgent need for early intervention.\\r\\n\\r\\nBio\\r\\nPROFESSOR ASHER BEN-ARIEH, Dean of the Paul Baerwald School of Social Work and Social Welfare, holds the Haruv Chair for the Study of Child Maltreatment at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem, where he is a Professor of Social Work. He has published extensively on children’s well-being, with a concentration on the indicators of children's well-being and child maltreatment. He is also the founding editor-in-chief of the Child Indicators Research Journal and the Child Well-Being: Indicators and Research book series. Currently, Prof Ben-Arieh is one of the principal investigators of the International Study of Children’s Well-being research project.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn partnership with BFHU (British Friends of the Hebrew University\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Children in the Aftermath of 7 October\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 May-20 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483201AQKDNHMBTRVRVKBSDLCLGQLMJSS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-20T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-20T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Israel & the Middle East\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Professor Asher Ben-Arieh\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When Los Angeles private eye J.J. Jake Gittes is hired by Evelyn Mulwray to investigate her husband's activities, he believes it's a routine infidelity case. Jake's investigation soon becomes anything but routine when he meets the real Mrs. Mulwray  and realizes he was hired by an imposter. Mr. Mulwray's sudden death sets Gittes on a tangled trail of corruption, deceit and sinister family secrets as Evelyn's father becomes a suspect in the case. | Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 10m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":130,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/eb24ef7f-dc80-4572-9bed-74321db73ea2.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chinatown\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 March-18 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/eb24ef7f-dc80-4572-9bed-74321db73ea2-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481401ALHNHJLSTVRCRMSPQGPLCNJNPTB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-16T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-18T13:50:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.15pm, £20, hybrid // Churchill famously said “If Hitler invaded Hell I would at least make a favourable reference to the Devil in the House of Commons “.  So began the unlikely alliance between Liberal Democracy and Communism, between Churchill and Stalin, in the face of Hitler’s rampant Nazism.\\r\\n\\r\\nWilliam Tyler MBE is a superb communicator. He is a freelance educator, lecturer, public speaker, writer and consultant with a main focus on History. He was the Principal of The City Lit, Britain’s largest college of adult education. William is a Freeman of the City of London. In 2009 he was awarded his MBE for services to education.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Churchill and Stalin: An Unlikely Alliance\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 April-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453801ACHHRGKRQGBGGJKMHCHPKPBLSVH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"William Tyler MBE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Approx 2 hours including interval // Early bird pricing through till Feb 2025 - Preview: 7 - 9 December £15\\r\\nOff Peak: 11-19 December & 2-4 January  £16 chid £25 adult\\r\\nPeak: 20 - 31 December £19 child £29 adult\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cinderella and the Matzo Ball\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 December-4 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472801AGBRGQGRPKMJNPTHSCLTMJDNMLP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-12-07T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This is a venue hire, customers should email Frederiqueassor@yahoo.co.uk to book // Join Frederique, a world-trained Oriental dancer with over 15 years of experience, as she shares her passion for this mesmerizing art form. Whether you're refining your skills or taking your first steps into Egyptian dance, these classes are for you! //\\r\\nIntermediate Class (7:10 PM - 8:15 PM): Elevate your dance with a focus on choreography, layering, musicality, and technique. Explore diverse routines, from classical songs to baladi, chaabi, golden era, and drum solos—refining technique, improving musicality, and enhancing rhythm recognition.\\r\\nBeginner Class (8:20 PM - 9:20 PM): New to Oriental dance or revisiting the fundamentals? This class builds a strong foundation with essential movements, posture, and fluidity. A welcoming space for all levels!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Classical Egyptian Dance Class\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-30 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503601ADCDVKSBDMCTNKJKBHKPKBHVJCD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-23T19:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-30T20:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Venue Hire\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"**VENUE HIRE** Experience the Magic of Egyptian Dance with Frederique Assor!\\r\\nJoin Frederique, a world-trained Oriental dancer and teacher with over 15 years of experience, as she shares her passion for this captivating art form. Egyptian dance is more than movement—it strengthens your core, boosts flexibility, and improves posture and balance, all while being gentle on your joints.\\r\\nFeel empowered, relieve stress, and connect with your body through graceful, artistic expression. Perfect for all ages and fitness levels, this inclusive and enriching experience fosters a sense of community and promotes both physical and emotional well-being. Step into the rhythm and let the magic begin!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Classical Egyptian Dance Class (Raks Sharki)\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-9 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472201AHQPTVKBVDQCRGVVNQSMPQBGBLH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-08T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-09T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"An enigmatic young man tries to make money by reselling shrewdly obtained goods on the internet under the pseudonym ‘Ratel’. | This film is in Japanese with English subtitles | Rating: 15, Duration 2h 4m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/14dbb3e8-a2e6-4294-a30c-3ed44535290d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cloud\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/14dbb3e8-a2e6-4294-a30c-3ed44535290d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506801AVGPMLPKNGHSKBPCDGDPTCDTNKD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T15:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, building, £20 // The thirty-five years of relative peace and global stability that followed the Cold War have now come to an end.  A growing alliance of authoritarian regimes, led by China, Russia, Iran, and North Korea (CRINKS), is steadily intensifying its challenge to the Western-led post-war order.  Much like in the 1930s, when Western democracies failed to deter the Axis powers, the question arises: Does the West possess the will and economic strength to ensure that deterrence does not falter once again? What lessons can be drawn from the recent conflicts in Ukraine and the Middle East?  One economist argues that the ancient dictum Si vis pacem, para bellum (If you want peace, prepare for war) has never seemed more relevant. // Michael is Professor at City St George’s, University of London and former head of its Economics department. He has worked at the University of Houston, University of Haifa and the Bank of Israel and served on the US National Academy of Sciences Panel on Economic and Fiscal Impact of Immigration and the Technion's Economics of National Security Program. He serves on the Grant Assessment Panel of the Economic and Social Research Council (ESRC) from 2021 and the editorial board of Economic Affairs.  He has appeared on Al Jazeera, BBC, CNBC, GBNews, Israel's Kan Reshet Bet Radio, Sky News and published commentary in the Conversation, Financial Times, Institute for Economic Affairs (IEA) Blog, Haaretz, LSE EU Politics, LSE Economics and Finance, Quillette and Israel’s economics newspaper The Marker.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cold War II or World War III?\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 June-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487401ACSCGDQPHGMSRVKTLPHBMHVSTPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-18T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-18T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Prof Michael Ben-Gad\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-3.30pm, £20, in building // No other city in the world offers such rich pickings for treasure and bargain hunters as Paris. \\r\\n\\r\\nBeautiful and precious objects can be found for a pittance. \\r\\n\\r\\nPatrick Bade will take you on an excursion through the city showing you where and how these treasures can be found in flea markets, auction houses and in the galleries in the \\\"passages\\\" with some delicious and inexpensive meals along the way.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Collecting in Paris: How to Find Treasures and Bargains\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 April-8 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"494201ABNBBLGLMTLJCHCVPMNPDQDHQHR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-08T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-08T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patrick Bade\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When Cardinal Lawrence is tasked with leading one of the world's most secretive and ancient events, selecting a new Pope, he finds himself at the center of a conspiracy that could shake the very foundation of the Catholic Church. // Rating: 12A, Duration: 120m // Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/13568c3a-a6cb-4b21-9bb9-71a9476d0de6.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Conclave\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 March-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/13568c3a-a6cb-4b21-9bb9-71a9476d0de6-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"463001ATRPCKSGBGKJDPSNPLRRVVHKSRM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-03T19:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8pm, £20, building only // Uncover the remarkable, yet often overlooked, contributions of British-born Jewish women to the arts in the twentieth century. From household names to hidden trailblazers, these women left an indelible mark on their fields. Whether familiar or forgotten, their stories are rich with creativity and resilience. \\r\\n\\r\\nIsabelle has a doctorate in philosophy, specialising in the Jewish East End of London and is a blue badge tourist guide. Aviva is the Executive Director of Jewish Renaissance, the UK's Jewish arts magazine. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Creating A Storm: Jewish Women in the World of Arts & Culture\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 March-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"456401AVDRHLTJNTLTPRQCTGTNCRNGBPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays //\\r\\n28 April – 21 July* \\r\\n*No class 26 May or 2 June // 2pm–3.30pm // £20 per session or £180 for the 10 weeks // Join Paula as she brilliantly tackles the news of the week. Topics are generated by you, and the issues of the day.\\r\\n\\r\\nPaula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\\r\\n\\r\\nNB: This series will take place both in the building and online. To attend in in person, click the \\\"Book Now\\\" button on this page. To attend online, click the button below.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Spring [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487402AKKHBVJPPQKDNJLCQKDGKVSGCNQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-21T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays  \\r\\n28 April – 21 July* \\r\\n*No class 26 May or 2 June // 2pm–3.30pm //\\r\\n£20 per session or £180 for the 10 weeks //\\r\\nAlso available online // Join Paula as she brilliantly tackles the news of the week. Topics are generated by you, and the issues of the day.\\r\\n\\r\\nPaula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\\r\\n\\r\\nNB: This series will take place both in the building and online. To attend in in person, click the \\\"Book Now\\\" button on this page. To attend online, click the button below.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Spring [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487002AKJGSSHRCGPLQMNJLBJGSKGPRPJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-21T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays 13 January – 31 March* *No class 17 February 2pm – 3:30pm, £20 per session, £198 for the 11 weeks Also available online Join Paula as she brilliantly tackles the news of the week. Topics are generated by you, and the issues of the day. Paula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Winter 2025 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450401AJJVRHLPBKNPDQHHBPSMSMLRPGV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building // Opening our Season, Dame Imogen Cooper is treating us to a recital centred round two sets of Schubert Impromptus, each containing four quite short pieces of extraordinary profundity, composed towards the end of Schubert’s short but richly productive life.   Dame Imogen is famous for her Schubert interpretations and has recorded these pieces to great acclaim.  Two Bach Chorales and some Beethoven Bagatelles complete this unmissable programme. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dame Imogen Cooper\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 September-30 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493001ATJHKMSMNTDJGGRGCKMRJMGLMQD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-30T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-30T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This is a venue hire, customers should email mayasamson@sky.com directly to book // Get ready for a high-energy, feel-good class!\\r\\nStep into a safe and supportive space where you can learn, grow, and challenge yourself—free from judgment and pressure.\\r\\nFeel empowered, relieve stress, and let loose as you move to your favorite songs.\\r\\nImmerse yourself in an infectious community vibe that will leave you feeling unstoppable.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Dance Classes with Maya\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 April-1 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502401AHPCJBCSCGNTBTMTQJBHKBPVJVT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-10T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-01T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Venue Hire\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // Join David Pleat as he launches his new memoir Just One More Goal. This is your chance to hear and meet the author as he talks with his North London rival, David Dein, interviewed by sports journalist by Graham Miller\\r\\nJust One More Goal is not just an account of one man’s lifelong obsession with football. It is the story of an evolving game, one that moved away from instinct and spontaneity towards something colder and more technical. David Pleat’s memoir is the perfect answer to the question of how modern football became what it is today.\\r\\nThere will be a book signings following the main event, with copies of the book available to purchase.\\r\\n \\r\\nBios\\r\\n David Pleat has been manager and director of football at Tottenham, manager of Luton, Leicester City, Sheffield Wednesday and Nuneaton Borough. As a footballer, he played for Nottingham Forest, Luton Town, Shrewsbury, Exeter and Peterborough.\\r\\nDavid Pleat has lived a life at the heart of football. From his debut as an England Schoolboy international in 1960 to his time as a scout for Tottenham Hotspur up to 2024.\\r\\nIn 1986, Pleat was given his shot at the big-time at Tottenham. But for a fabricated tabloid scandal, his sole season as manager, which featured a third-placed finish, an FA Cup final and a League Cup semi-final, might have been the start of a transformation at White Hart Lane.\\r\\n David Dein is currently International Ambassador for the FA and Ambassador for the Premier League. He was the former Vice Chairman of both Arsenal Football Club and the Football Association. He was also President of the G-14 group of European football clubs and International Ambassador of England’s bid to host the World Cup in 2018.\\r\\nDuring his 24 years at Arsenal, the club won 18 trophies including the Invincible season of 2003/2004.\\r\\nDein was the driving force behind the creation of the FA Premier League in 1992 which is now the most successful league competition in the world. He has been at the forefront of many important changes in football, including the introduction of Goal Line Technology and VAR.\\r\\nIn 2019 he was awarded an MBE for his services to football and charity.\\r\\nGraham Miller is a Broadcast Journalist with more than 30 years experience of covering news, current affairs and sport on British television, radio, newspapers and magazines. During a distinguished career including 10 years as ITN's Senior Sports Correspondent Graham has twice been nominated by the Royal Television Society as Sports Presenter of the Year.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"David Pleat in conversation with David Dein\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 January-27 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"442401AGDMLKSLLMLJBDPNGMNDTKJNJSJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"David Pleat, David Dein\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"JW3 hosts its fourth Death Café – an intimate space for a lightly facilitated conversation about death and dying.  \\r\\n\\r\\n And at JW3, there’ll be a Jewish twist. There is no formal agenda, and this is not a grief support or counselling session.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWhile it is difficult to talk about death and dying, Death Café offers participants the opportunity to share their thoughts about life-and-death in a relaxed and non-judgemental setting. More general information about the concept is here. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe group will be facilitated by Sally Berkovic, author of Death Duties: The Chevra Kadisha – what being around the dead taught me about life.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Death Café\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 March-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"456001ARSHBSDSRTKQMRJCCPRVVMQDTDP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"False\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sally Berkovic\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thu 10 July 2025 //\\r\\n2:00pm // \\r\\n£20 // Diane Keaton: Film Star, Rom-Com Heroine, and Fashion Icon\\r\\n\\r\\nDiane Keaton has appeared in over 50 films, won numerous awards (including the Academy Award for Best Actress), is famous for a specific ‘look’ that emerged in conjunction with her star-making role in the 1977 film, Annie Hall, and has dated some of Hollywood’s most eligible bachelors (Warren Beatty, in particular).  Even with this notable career longevity, there is a deep connection between Keaton- star and actress- and Annie Hall- character; often referred to in the popular press. This talk will examine Keaton’s film stardom from early films co-starring her then-boyfriend, Woody Allen, through to celebrated dramatic roles, contemporary ‘silver screen’ romantic comedies, and her position as an enduring fashion and beauty icon.   \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Julie Lobalzo Wright is an Assistant Professor in Film and Television Studies at the University of Warwick. She has taught and researched film and television stardom for many years, publishing work and giving talks on various stars, including Judy Garland, Elvis Presley, David Bowie, and Diane Keaton. Her next project is a book length study of Barbra Streisand that will focus on the authorship of her star image throughout her career.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Diane Keaton: Film Star, Rom-Com Heroine, and Fashion Icon\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 July-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"484201AHGMNDTGGGBCPBCLRKLSJKBJTPP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Julie Lobalzo Wright\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building, £20 // In our divisive age, argument is increasingly seen as a plague to be avoided or a contest \\r\\nto be won. Daniel Taub, an experienced peace negotiator and diplomat, argues that an ancient Jewish wisdom offers a third way. Weaving ancient insights with contemporary research in conflict resolution, and illustrating his findings with behind-the-scenes \\r\\npersonal stories of diplomacy and negotiations, Beyond Dispute is a passionate call to rediscover and harness the \\\"subversive power of a good argument\\\".\\r\\n\\r\\nDaniel Taub is a diplomat, peace negotiator and former Ambassador to the UK. He has lectured and written about conflict resolution and Biblical studies. He has written drama for television and theatre. His articles have appeared in The Times, The Daily Telegraph, The Guardian and the Huffington Post, and he has been interviewed on the BBC, Sky, and CNN. He lives in Jerusalem with his wife Zehava. They have six children.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Don't Argue Less, Argue Better!\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 June-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"504601ALCCLGVCSHRGCLQVPTQTCTTLQSD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-18T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-18T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Daniel Taub\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Eid is a young man from Rahat. He dreams of becoming a playwright and secretly writes a play based on the sexual assault he experienced as a child. He is in love with a married Arab actress who lives in Paris and helps him with his writing. When his parents inform him that they are arranging a marriage for him with a girl he's never met, he has no choice but to marry. When his wife asks him for a child, Eid makes an agreement with her - he will give her a child and in return, he will continue to have his freedom. Eid saves money and travels to Paris, but his lover does not show up. In his solitude, he writes an ending to his play and returns to Rahat. Winner of Best film at the Jerusalem Film Festival.\\r\\n| This film is in Arabic and Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | This screening will be preceded by the short film, Midnight. | Duration: 90 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/034869a8-8bf7-449b-85db-97a799e75bae.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Eid\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/034869a8-8bf7-449b-85db-97a799e75bae-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502801AVDQHHMHCVVMGTTQVMQJRGJTJVP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays 2.30pm - 4.30pm //\\r\\n13 May 2025 //\\r\\n-\\r\\n3 June 2025 //\\r\\n£20 per session or £72 for the 4 weeks // Embed your Life Writing Skills    \\r\\n\\r\\nYou’ve tried your hand at some life writing, and you’ve enjoyed it. This course helps you to develop your own distinctive writing voice and explore a structure to bring to life the faces and places that populate your world. With the use of your own photographs, memories and musings, start to build up a collection of life writing pieces.\\r\\n\\r\\nWeek One: Finding your Voice\\r\\n\\r\\nWeek Two: Creating a structure to house your memories\\r\\n\\r\\nWeek Three: Writing inspired by faces (using your own photos)\\r\\n\\r\\nWeek Four: Writing inspired by places (using your own photos)\\r\\n\\r\\nPam Cohen completed an MA in Creative Writing with distinction at The Open University where she specialised in creative non-fiction. She was a print and television journalist in South Africa, working for a women’s magazine, a national Sunday newspaper and British television, before coming to London. She has a passion for facilitating others to tap into their own creativity and discover the joy of expressing themselves on the page.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Embed Your Life Writing Skills\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-3 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485002APVPVCMHKLBHSDPTMGJRVSLDDTB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-03T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Pam Cohen\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The Roman occupation of Britain ended in 410 but for at least half a century before that there were signs that things were going wrong. We will examine the evidence from archaeology and written sources to uncover the secrets of this lesser known period of our history. Disclaimer Even the experts are divided.\\r\\nJill Stern is an historian. Aged twenty she graduated with first class honours in History from King’s College London. Much of her working life was spent as a teacher at Wycombe Abbey School and as chairman of a Health Authority in West London and vice-chairman of North Thames Regional Health Authority. Returning to academic study she gained an MA (Distinction) and a doctorate in seventeenth century Dutch history at University College London. As a doctoral student she was awarded the prestigious Pollard Prize for History. She has a book and many published articles to her credit. She has lectured in Britain, the Netherlands and New York. History is her lifelong passion and she is keen to share that passion.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"End of Roman Britain\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455801ARGMKLGNKJTPSSNGQBQBPCBJMDK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-26T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-26T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"False\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The sequel to American Humane's award-winning documentary, Escape from Extinction, introduces rewilding - a proven method for sustainable conservation that has the potential to bring back hundreds of thousands of species from the brink of extinction. Narrated by Academy Award winner Meryl Streep, the film follows tireless conservation efforts of leading organizations implementing rewilding practices across a diverse array of species in equally diverse environments. | Duration: 1h 30m, Rating: 12 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6cdf757d-c34e-49fd-bb33-97a7d76c0fd8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Escape from Extinction: Rewilding\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6cdf757d-c34e-49fd-bb33-97a7d76c0fd8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507001AMQBGVVHKKTGJGPSKBPPTVHVGVL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T11:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T13:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wed 02 July 2025 //\\r\\n2:00pm // \\r\\n£20 // Join Jonathan to look at topics including:\\r\\n• Antisemitism in Europe & UK\\r\\n• Aliyah from Europe\\r\\n• Israels' Relationship with Europe.\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Europe and the Middle East\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 July-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"484401ANKHGQMGHHTHLNTRHGRGBHPKNQG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-02T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-02T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Israel & the Middle East\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The Impressionists are the most popular group in art history – millions flock every year to marvel at their masterpieces. But, to begin with, they were scorned, penniless outsiders. 1874 was the year that changed everything; the first Impressionists, “hungry for independence”, broke the mould by holding their own exhibition outside official channels. Impressionism was born and the art world was changed forever. What led to that first groundbreaking show 150 years ago? Who were the maverick personalities that wielded their brushes in such a radical and provocative way? The spectacular Musée d’Orsay exhibition brings fresh eyes to this extraordinary tale of passion and rebellion. The story is told not only by historians and curators, but in the words of those who witnessed the dawn of Impressionism: the artists, press and people of Paris, 1874. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 30m\\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/55fd3aa0-1519-43a2-8abe-dda92ba362b8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Dawn of Impressionism: Paris 1874\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/55fd3aa0-1519-43a2-8abe-dda92ba362b8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"500001ALQRVQLQVNPJCJTQJQLLLRGBGLG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-17T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The spectacular sculptures and paintings of Michelangelo seem so familiar to us, but what do we really know about this Renaissance giant? Michelangelo’s genius is evident in everything he touched. Beautiful and diverse works such as the towering statue of David, the moving Pietà in the Papal Basilica of St. Peter and his tour-de-force, the Sistine Chapel ceiling, still leave us breathless today. \\r\\n\\r\\nSpanning his 88 years, Michelangelo – Love and Death takes a cinematic journey through the print and drawing rooms of Europe through the great chapels and museums of Florence, Rome and the Vatican to seek out a deeper understanding of this legendary figure’s tempestuous life, his relationship with his contemporaries and his incredible legacy. \\r\\n\\r\\nThrough expert commentary, stunning visuals and Michelangelo’s own words, this film takes a fresh look at a master artist whose life and genius are celebrated in every mark he made. Returning to cinemas in 2025 to celebrate this iconic artist’s 550th birthday. \\r\\n\\r\\nSculptor, painter, architect, poet, genius – discover why Michelangelo is without a doubt one of the greatest artists of all time. | Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 30 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/7a5f97c8-5f43-4317-bee3-2ddf14a0b61f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Michelangelo: Love and Death\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/7a5f97c8-5f43-4317-bee3-2ddf14a0b61f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506602AGCTTNDJPTCKCDHLJVPQPGSCLVM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-20T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T13:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"200 years after its opening and a century after acquiring its first Van Gogh works, the National Gallery is hosting the UK’s biggest ever Van Gogh exhibition. Explore one of art history’s most pivotal periods in this once-in-a-century show. Made in close collaboration with the National Gallery. \\r\\nRated: 12A | 1 hour 3 minutes\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/edbd247f-bab0-487d-9579-c7e2edc8a80b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Van Gogh: Poets & Lovers\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/edbd247f-bab0-487d-9579-c7e2edc8a80b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"475201ATGJJDGPKHGCHSBMHQGCDTJTPBD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-11T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-12T15:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building // The Fibonacci Quartet have burst onto the international stage after winning first prize in numerous competitions including the prestigious Borciani International Competition in Italy. Audiences love the immediacy and warmth of their communication both with one another and with the listener. \\r\\nLuba Tunnicliffe is one of the UK’s finest and most musicianly young violists and played for several years in the Ruisi Quartet. \\r\\n// \\r\\nThere are only a handful of major string sextets but they are all wonderfully sonorous and warm. The extra viola and cello added to the string quartet add a lot of colour and richness, and also liberate the first viola and cello to share melodies with the first violin.  It is perhaps not an accident that all these three gorgeous pieces are part of the late Romantic era. This is a rare chance to hear them together.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Fibonacci String Quartet with Luba Tunicliffe and David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493601AMLKBDVGSMCMTQDNKCCBMGQRCBR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Rejecting his cultured upper-class background as a classical pianist, Robert Dupea (Jack Nicholson) opts for a blue-collar existence, working in a California oil field and spending time with his waitress girlfriend, Rayette (Karen Black). But when Robert discovers that his father is gravely ill, he wants to reunite with his estranged family in the state of Washington. He and Rayette take a road trip that brings the two paths of his life to an uncomfortable intersection. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 38m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":98,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a13452ac-d58d-45e5-8425-5168ceeb99e6.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Five Easy Pieces \",\"instanceDates\":\"20 March-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a13452ac-d58d-45e5-8425-5168ceeb99e6-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"482001AGRBRTRSKVCHTCCBMNSJKRGRMCL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T15:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T16:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A wondrous journey, through realms natural and mystical, Flow follows a courageous cat after his home is devastated by a great flood. Teaming up with a capybara, a lemur, a bird, and a dog to navigate a boat in search of dry land, they must rely on trust, courage, and wits to survive the perils of a newly aquatic planet. From the boundless imagination of the award-winning Gints Zilbalodis (Away) comes a thrilling animated spectacle as well as a profound meditation on the fragility of the environment and the spirit of friendship and community. Steeped in the soaring possibilities of visual storytelling, Flow is a feast for the senses and a treasure for the heart.\\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: U, Duration: 1h 25m\\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":85,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/3e7696cd-19db-43c6-a78e-e53f6855db04.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Flow\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-24 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/3e7696cd-19db-43c6-a78e-e53f6855db04-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499801AKKVSPMPPVTJGSPPTNHJNPKNLNL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-22T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, £17 // This is the true story of Hitler's visit to a centuries-old Bavarian Passion Play, the Nazi blacksmith playing Jesus and the only Jew in the village, Max Peter Meyer. The showcase will be the culmination of work with choirs, musicians and actors on the two-play saga.  If you would be interested in becoming involved as a performer, please contact Joe Harmston via JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Forging The Pledge\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 January-30 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"468201AMQJPLDKJJPMKRJTGDCSHVNCMNV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-30T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-30T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £200 (10 weeks), in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485801AJBDNVDTCBNRPQBBDTNCPGGCKHH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-21T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 1pm-3pm, £200 (10 weeks), in building\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487001AKDQMQBDQTMGQMKMQNSPJKTTCVK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-21T13:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £216, in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"459201AMTJLDKHNSRKHRGBGTGLBRLQCCG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 1pm - 3pm, £216, in building\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"459402AJGGVHQJBPCGBLKRMGJJVCGBCJM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T13:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am - 12.30pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Intermediate with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-15 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"494801ADRMTRJBRPJGCPRKHDPJPTTSLMJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-22T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-15T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £216, in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Intermediate with Patricia Zerah [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 January-1 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"460002ATSSLTRCGJQPQMNPDNPHQBCTPMH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-07T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-01T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"In a Jaffa bra shop's fitting room, a heartfelt and humorous journey unfolds as women confront their love-hate relationship with their bosom buddies. As each heroine searches for the perfect bra, she bares not only her chest but her soul, sharing stories of triumph, tribulation, and the occasional wardrobe malfunction.\\r\\nBreasts are more than just accessories—they’re the protagonists of our life’s epic. From the awkward first breakout to the sobering reality of mammograms, our relationship with our \\\"girls\\\" is a bouncy rollercoaster of ups and downs. This film unravels the mystery, myths, and full support between women and their breasts, a story written on our bodies in every curve, contour, and stretch mark. | This film is in Arabic and Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | This screening will be preceded by the short documentary, M/other. | Duration: 68 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":87,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/4df5eb46-b363-40f7-86c7-f8c7d150ac24.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Full Support\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/4df5eb46-b363-40f7-86c7-f8c7d150ac24-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503001ABNMCMBBCLGGCKTJJMNQTBBTQDS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T20:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T20:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"9am-5pm, in-building // JW3 is hosting the NHS blood donation team. Donating blood can be done in under an hour and can potentially save a life. To donate blood, you must book in advance through www.blood.co.uk. No walk-ins allowed. Please note that JW3 is not handling bookings so please do not contact our Box Office.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":480,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Give Blood @ JW3\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 May-19 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477201ATKVQLMMGTPTQGNVHLSVCVJDGMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T09:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T09:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"9am-5pm, in-building // JW3 is hosting the NHS blood donation team. Donating blood can be done in under an hour and can potentially save a life. To donate blood, you must book in advance through www.blood.co.uk. No walk-ins allowed. Please note that JW3 is not handling bookings so please do not contact our Box Office.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":480,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Give Blood @ JW3\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 September-29 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477401ABNRRPMMRBKJMMDTKBRHRJPLMLQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-29T09:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-29T09:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesday 26 March \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n2pm – 3pm, £20, also available online \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat will global politics look like in 2045?  \\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan will discuss the rivalry between the US-led West and China-led autocracies as global cooperation weakens; the rise of the Global South, led by India and Africa, and their challenges with climate change; and Israel's role in the Middle East and how the region will fit into the world. \\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan is a London-based Middle East analyst and appears as a commentator on Sky, BBC, France 24 and Al Arabiya. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Global Trends 2045\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"451001ADLMQJLCDQBDHGNRVQLGQCGQNLN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-26T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-26T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"3 x 90 mins sessions, £5 to cover costs, in building // Looking for a fun and meaningful activity for the whole family this half-term? Come volunteer together and help us prepare freshly made meals for our foodbank recipients with a special Indian menu!\\r\\nJoin us in learning how to make authentic Indian dishes including:\\r\\n-Bhajis\\r\\n-Curry\\r\\n-Chutneys & Raitas\\r\\n-Rotis\\r\\n \\r\\nThere will be three cooking sessions during the day, and a charge of £5 per head to cover the cost of ingredients. Suitable for children ages 8+, to be accompanied by parents or guardians.\\r\\n \\r\\nSession 1: 10.30am-12pm (aimed at younger age group (8-12 years old)\\r\\nSession 2: 12.30-2pm (aimed at 12-16 year olds)\\r\\nSession 3: 2.30-4pm (mixed age group)\\r\\n \\r\\nIf you would like to help support our foodbank as costs continue to rise, we also encourage donations of non-perishable food items (must be suitable for vegetarians).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Half Term Foodbank Volunteering for Families\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 February-18 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477801AVSSNQLGDMJVGBVRLHSLBLSSGGQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-18T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-18T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Reunited with Leigh for the first time since multiple Oscar-nominated Secrets and Lies, the astonishing Marianne Jean-Baptiste plays Pansy, a woman wracked by fear, tormented by afflictions, and prone to raging tirades against her husband, son, and anyone who looks her way. Meanwhile, her easy-going younger sister, played by Michele Austin (Another Year), is a single mother with a life as different from Pansy's as their clashing temperaments -- brimming with communal warmth from her salon clients and daughters alike. This expansive film from a master dramatist takes us into the intensities of kinship, duty, and the most enduring of human mysteries: that even through lifetimes of hurt and hardship, we still find ways to love those we call family.\\r\\nRated: 12A | 1 hour 37 minutes\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":97,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/27717018-faeb-4473-b953-8252a9499213.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hard Truths\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 February-27 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/27717018-faeb-4473-b953-8252a9499213-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"475801ANBCSPTSCTCGVDRDGBMLLPDHVHV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-16T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-27T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Rachel Samstat (Meryl Streep), a New York food critic, beds Mark Forman (Jack Nicholson), a Washington, D.C., newspaper columnist. The two fall in love, and Rachel relinquishes her job and relocates to be with a man who views himself as unfit for marriage. They try to build a life together -- literally -- as they struggle with the construction crews renovating their home. When Rachel gets pregnant, Mark is enthusiastic, but then soon begins doubting whether he could be a family man. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 48m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":108,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/7e20302e-4903-444f-bcbf-232f84d74430.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Heartburn\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/7e20302e-4903-444f-bcbf-232f84d74430-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"482401ABDBTPDVDHGKBSGQRQGVRJRDGQS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-25T13:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-26T13:50:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £220, in building //\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Advanced 1 (Term 2) with Haggit Inbar-Littas\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"496001AQVCTQBDBRGSVKLRKKLCHRLRHPJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-16T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Haggit Inbar-Littas\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 10.30am-1pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Advanced 2 with Rina Gurvitz\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"496002ABMRMQDVVKQDCHJRVLNVQBDNKHD\",\"firstIns