ribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nurit Gance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £216, in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Not Quite Beginners with Reuven Vazan [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 January-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"462201ANDBHPTKDGVJBSHPQCRKMSTJLTL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-09T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Reuven Vazan\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £60 for the course, in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Singing Club with Ira Kalechman\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"459002ANSCLJKJNKHVDGSNMPJSMLVNSKP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ira Kalechman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 7.15pm - 8.15pm, £60, in building // Led by singer and Choir Director Ira Kalechman, Hebrew Singing Club is a great way to improve and practice your Hebrew fluency and understanding, while enjoying singing together and meeting new people.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe meeting will take part in basic Hebrew.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Singing Club with Ira Kalechman\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488002ADMVJBVBTCCTJCJJRRGDGKPDDTP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-21T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ira Kalechman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £180, in building (reduced price, funding from WZO)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Total Beginners with Esti Levene [New] [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"459601ARVCBBNPDKVPRKJPLMSSNRCTLGT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-06T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £180, in building // Reduced price because of WZO funding\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Total Beginners with Nurit Gance [New] [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 January-1 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"460601APJKQLPPMVVLSQKVTQNCRKDDSQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-07T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-01T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nurit Gance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £187, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Total Beginners with Orit Eyal-Fibeesh - NEW\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 April-17 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"495603APMSDLGNBVPCSRHTKPHHHDQLPML\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-17T19:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Orit Eyal-Fibeesh\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Starring Idan Ameady and Tali Sharon, this gripping mystery follows Daphna, a 41-year-old former promising detective in Tel Aviv now stuck in the quiet town of Afula. With her days filled with petty crimes and awkward questions about not having children, Daphna's world is turned upside down when Orly Elimeleh, a beautiful and rebellious army widow, goes missing. As she digs deeper, Daphna is troubled by one question: why is no one searching for her? Driven by fear and determination, Daphna will stop at nothing to uncover the truth behind Orly's disappearance. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | This screening will be preceded by the short film, Summer 2004. | Duration: 109 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":133,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c653aa31-46b2-4445-9f9c-de3cb86fedd8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Highway 65 + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c653aa31-46b2-4445-9f9c-de3cb86fedd8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502601AGDCQDRBGHLMQPGNSSSLQSHGQDV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am - 12noon, hybrid, free // Join us as we mark Holocaust Memorial Day. \\r\\n\\r\\nWe're honoured to welcome guests Lord Mann and Daniel Finkelstein. The morning will feature music from chazan (cantor) Jonny Turgel and pianist Josh Nesbitt and include filmed and live survivor testimony.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Holocaust Memorial Day 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 January-24 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455602AMHBTTJNQRVLQJTVJVBJDGNJHTB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-24T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-24T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"After the tragic death of his father, 18-year-old Totone is thrust into the unexpected and very adult role of looking after his younger sister and their failing family farm in the Jura section of France. He assumes even more responsibility when he enters a cash competition for the best Comte cheese made in this western part of the French Alps. A \\\"verité\\\" look at the hardscrabble life of French agriculture, it is simultaneously a moving love story and above all an ode to the love of cheese. \\r\\n\\r\\n| This film is French with English subtitles. \\r\\n| Rating: TBC, Duration: 1h 32m  \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":92,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/433e832b-64a7-4cd2-878f-61c52bfc6aee.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Holy Cow\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-1 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/433e832b-64a7-4cd2-878f-61c52bfc6aee-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"498602APHSMGPNVRHNLTPQSVHTTPDMPQS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-27T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-01T13:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tue 10 June 2025 //\\r\\n7:30pm // \\r\\n£20, in building //\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us in conversation with food writer Linda Dangoor as she launches her second cookbook, From the Tigris to the Thames. The book is a tapestry, part memoir and part cookbook, where she interweaves recipes with personal reflections on the idea of home and belonging. \\r\\n\\r\\nLinda Dangoor was born in Baghdad, Iraq. She’s a designer, painter and ceramicist, and now also a food writer. She has worked in the design field for many years creating products for the gift market in Paris in London.\\r\\nLinda is the author of two cookbooks. The first one, Flavours of Babylon is an exploration and a celebration of the flavours and recipes of her Baghdadi heritage. Her second book. From the Tigris to the Thames recounts leaving her Baghdadi home and her journey living in various countries and discovering their various dishes.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere will be an interview, a short Q&A session and a book signing whilst enjoying tasters from the book. Please note the food will contain nuts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\"In our modern world, many of us are now part of not just one, but many cultures and groups. We are where we have trod and more. So, it is, that since my family’s exile from our Iraqi homeland in the late 1950s, I have inhabited and sojourned in many countries and the word ‘home’ has taken on another, somewhat fragmented, meaning. Is Home where I was born; or where I have put down roots? Is Home a dish or perhaps a flavour? As Salman Rushdie so aptly put it, our “identity is at once plural and partial”.* And this plurality, this mingling between cultures, has enriched my own identity – and also the food that I cook today.\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can follow Linda on Instagram at @lindadangoorcreativeliving and Twitter @lindadangoor or visit her website www.lindadangoor.com\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Home, Migration and Food! \",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-10 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483601AHHHLMNMKCBCMKBJMGRGSQGJCPN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-10T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Linda Dangoor\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"12noon - 1.30pm, free, online only // Are you looking for a new job but unsure of how to navigate today’s jobs market?\\r\\nResource’s How To Get A Job Workshop will take you on a journey from writing a good CV and covering letter, using AI and Social to improve your job search, the importance of networking, honing your interview technique and nailing that job.  With over 32 years of experience, Resource’s experienced experts will simplify the process, helping you feel more confident and prepared, whatever stage of the job-search you’re in.\\r\\nWho should attend?\\r\\nThe workshop is aimed at everyone who is, or will be looking for a job in the near future. No age limit or level of experience required, all welcome.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"How to Get a Job Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"473801ADHKLCBGKQCLNJQVMJLTMCLMPNK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-26T12:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-26T12:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Social Action\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"125// 12A // A man quits work to care for his dying grandmother, motivated by her fortune. He schemes to win her favor before she passes.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":125,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"How to Make Millions before Grandma Dies\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-16 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471001AHMTJLHSNCVTPSBRSNRSGNVLKLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T17:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T14:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, £20, hybrid // The practice of astrology has been both praised and criticised throughout Jewish history, but there’s little doubt that it was a fundamental tenet of the medieval worldview. In our age of magazine mystics and Instagram astrologers, it’s easy to forget that astrological texts were once written by some of the greatest luminaries of the Jewish tradition. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk will introduce some of the evidence of practical astrology from the Cairo Genizah, the famous trove of documents preserved in the Ben Ezra synagogue in Fustat.\\r\\n\\r\\nJoseph is a Junior Research Fellow in Hebrew palaeography at Corpus Christi College and has taught on Hebrew manuscripts in Oxford and internationally. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"How to Read a Medieval Jewish Horoscope\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 January-27 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452801ARCDSSCMGPPNBMHMKPMJMSQLHCH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-27T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Oxford Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Since the 1970s, English photographer Martin Parr has held up a sometimes tender, sometimes critical and always mischievous mirror to our times, forcing us to take a hard look at how consumer society has shaped our lives. Discover the maverick behind some of the most iconic images of the past century on an intimate and exclusive road trip across England with the uncompromising Parr, whose subjects, frames and colours have revolutionised contemporary photography. // Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 8m / Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads and trailers.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":68,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/99e03ce5-8ce4-49ee-a031-5e0c6bcc4e95.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"I Am Martin Parr\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 March-13 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/99e03ce5-8ce4-49ee-a031-5e0c6bcc4e95-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480202AQDPLHMBCRDKRPDDPRRSJJVTQRJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-11T17:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-13T17:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Brazil faces the tightening grip of a military dictatorship. Eunice Paiva, a mother of five children, is forced to reinvent herself after her family suffers a violent and arbitrary act by the government. | In Portugues with English subtitles | Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 17m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":137,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1ea6a470-579f-4b37-8284-b2b4573a4258.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"I'm Still Here\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 March-13 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1ea6a470-579f-4b37-8284-b2b4573a4258-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481801AHVHNSKBHDRJBTKJMMJQBKQSNLG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-09T12:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-13T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"8-9.30pm, £5, hybrid // Join us for a thought-provoking evening as two social entrepreneurs and peace activists, Israeli Maoz Inon and Palestinian Aziz Abu Sarah, share their stories of loss and resilience. Maoz tragically lost his both parents on October 7, while Aziz lost his brother during the first Intifada. Despite their immense pain, they seek to build bridges and model a future of hope, reconciliation, and peace. Peace making means not only believing in peace and solidarity - but putting in the hard work in the face of war, hatred and division - and doing things differently.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn April 2024, at the annual TED Conference, Aziz and Maoz delivered the opening session's first talk, which became the third most-watched TED talk of the year. In May 2024, the two attended the ARENA DI PACE peace event in Verona, where they received a personal embrace and public support from Pope Francis, drawing international media attention to their shared vision for peace. Together, they have also led impactful conversations and events across the world and within their communities in Israel and Palestine. \\r\\nCurrently, Maoz and Aziz are co-authoring a book, expected to be published in 2025 by Crown Publishing House. They serve as prominent leaders of the It’s Time Coalition, an umbrella organization uniting over 50 civil society groups dedicated to advancing peace and reconciliation. \\r\\n\\r\\nBIOS\\r\\n Maoz Inon is an Israeli peace entrepreneur and a father of three. Since the murder of his parents in the Hamas attack on October 7, 2023, he has become a prominent voice for peace between Israelis and Palestinians. A sought-after speaker—from the halls of congress to universities, businesses, a wide spectrum of organizations and NGOs—he inspires audiences with his signature message that “Peace is Possible.” Before October 7, Maoz founded several peace-focused tourism initiatives within Israel and the Middle East, including the Jesus Trail, Fauzi Azar Inn, and Abraham Hostel & Tour. \\r\\nIn recognition of his efforts, Maoz was honored in 2024 with two prestigious awards: the Franco-German Human Rights Prize, awarded by France and Germany, and the Shared Living Award from Abraham Initiatives. \\r\\nAziz Abu Sarah is a Palestinian peacebuilder, author, and mission-driven entrepreneur whose personal story of transformation began after the tragic loss of his brother, who was killed by Israeli soldiers. Aziz is the co-founder of InterAct International, a nonprofit focused on advancing sustainability, education, and cross-cultural connections, and he has served as the Executive Director at the Center for World Religions, Diplomacy and Conflict Resolution at George Mason University. He is also a former Chairman of the Parents Circle–Family Forum, a network of bereaved families advocating for peace. Aziz’s contributions to peacebuilding have been recognized by notable figures, including former United Nations Secretary-General Ban Ki-Moon. Aziz is the author of two books: Crossing Boundaries: A Traveler’s Guide to World Peace (2020) and Strangers, Neighbors, Friends: Muslim-Christian-Jewish Reflections on Compassion and Peace (2018).\\r\\nAziz has been recognized among the “500 Most Influential Muslims in the World” by the Royal Strategic Studies Centre in Jordan annually since 2010 for his impactful work in cultural education and conflict resolution. As a National Geographic Explorer and TED Fellow, Aziz has demonstrated the power of travel as a tool for peacemaking. In 2009, he co-founded MEJDI Tours, a leader in responsible travel and creator of the pioneering Dual Narrative™ method, which uses travel to foster understanding and dialogue.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"In conversation with Aziz Abu Sarah and Maoz Inon\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 March-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"482801AKPHHSDRTDGTQCHPLGRHMGKMCSJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // Join us for an important conversation with Conservative peer, campaigner, and podcaster Baroness Sayeeda Warsi, as she discusses her new book, Muslims Don't Matter. (Book title in italics)\\r\\n\\r\\nBaroness Warsi once said that Islamophobia has \\\"passed the dinner table test\\\" yet many refuse to acknowledge its existence. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe book draws on her experience as Britain’s first Muslim Cabinet minister, as well as personal insights, to shed light on Islamophobia in Britain. From the far-right violence in the summer of 2024, to hatred directed at Muslims during the Gaza conflict, Warsi urges us to change course and unite to dismantle this toxic bigotry.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"In Conversation with Baroness Sayeeda Warsi\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 June-23 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"498001ANMQPBSGVGJKCPVJHVHRDNVGPBM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-23T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-23T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Baroness Sayeeda Warsi\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // Join us in conversation with Emma Barnett and Deborah Joseph to celebrate the launch of Emma's new book Maternity Service, a heartfelt, reassuring and bracingly honest book about the experience of being on maternity leave.\\r\\n\\r\\nEmma wrote this book live as her experiences were unfolding; in moments snatched while doing her second tour of duty in the faraway land that is maternity leave. She couldn’t believe how much of it she had forgotten from the first time. The book aims to capture how she felt while she still could in a bid to faithfully remember and record it—while throwing a life-line to other women who have been through it or are about to or are trench-deep. \\r\\n\\r\\nEmma Barnett is an award-winning broadcaster and journalist. She was named Interviewer of the Year for 2022 at the British Journalism awards and is a presenter on BBC Radio 4’s flagship Today Programme, as well as hosting TV interviews and documentaries across the BBC. She has presented programmes that include Woman’s Hour on BBC Radio 4 and Newsnight. She also presented a global interviews programme on Bloomberg TV, interviewing international figures from across the world of politics, sport, entertainment and technology.\\r\\n\\r\\nEmma pens a bi-weekly newspaper column for the i, and was previously a columnist for the Sunday Times and the Daily Telegraph, where she was also the Women’s Editor. After the birth of her first child, she wrote Period: It’s about Bloody Time, her first book.\\r\\n\\r\\nEmma grew up in Manchester, and now lives in London with her husband and their two children.\\r\\n\\r\\nDeborah Joseph is an award-winning magazine editor and journalist who writes regularly for The Times and Daily Mail. Until recently, she was Editor-in-chief of Glamour magazine where she focused on driving conversations around equality for women and lobbied the government to make deepfake pornography illegal. She was the 2023 Chair of the British Society for Magazine editors  and is currently a judge for the Women’s Prize for Fiction.\\r\\nShe has three children and two dogs and speaks regularly on work life balance.\\r\\n\\r\\nBooks will also be available to buy and be signed on the night\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"In conversation with Emma Barnett\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483002ATPGSVHDGBRJQVTGRLDGRSKHCVJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Emma Barnett\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // The October 7 atrocities in Israel challenged the west to support the defence of civilisation against barbarism. It has not done so. In her provocative new book, The Builder's Stone: How Jews and Christians Built the West -- and Why Only They Can Save It, Melanie Phillips argues that the key lessons for cultural survival lie with the Jewish people in an alliance for civilisation to restore core western values.\\r\\n\\r\\nBooks will also be available to buy and be signed on the night\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"In conversation with Melanie Phillips\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-30 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483001ACJBHHHPNDTDJTLQPDVVHQKPPHS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 11am-1pm, £90 for 4 week course only, in building // Our Introduction to British Sign Language (BSL) course offers the perfect first step on your journey to learning this visual and expressive language.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis 5-week course is designed for individuals who want to build a foundational understanding of BSL. Whether you're interested in learning for personal curiosity or to communicate more effectively with family members, colleagues, or customers who are Deaf, this course will provide essential skills.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe course will be taught by Antony Rabin, an experienced instructor who teaches at adult colleges, universities, and within the public sector in London.\\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Overview:\\r\\n\\r\\n• Greetings and Leave-Takings: Learn how to sign common greetings and farewells.\\r\\n• Family and Describing People: Understand how to sign about family members and describe others.\\r\\n• Travel and Transport: Gain vocabulary for signing about different modes of transport.\\r\\n• Numbers: Learn how to sign numbers accurately.\\r\\n• Fingerspelling: Master the technique of fingerspelling.\\r\\n• Personal Information: Know how to sign essential personal information such as name, age, and address.\\r\\n• Hobbies and Leisure: Learn how to sign about hobbies and leisure activities.\\r\\n• Food and Drink: Acquire the signs for food and drink-related vocabulary.\\r\\n• Likes and Dislikes: Learn how to express preferences.\\r\\n• Feelings: Gain vocabulary for expressing emotions.\\r\\n• Signing Space: Understand the concept of signing space and how to use it effectively.\\r\\n• Non-Manual Features: Learn how to use facial expressions and other non-manual features in BSL.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is perfect for beginners and those looking to take their first steps into the world of BSL without committing to a long-term program.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Introduction to British Sign Language (BSL) Winter 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 February-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477001AQHSBDLKQLLDVMGPLLVGHPQBCHT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-24T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-24T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Antony Rabin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2.30pm-4pm, £20 per session or £108 for 6 week course, in building // Interested in Life Writing but don’t know how or where to start? This four-week course will help you to access and explore your memories while learning a variety of exciting creative non-fiction writing techniques to further develop and enhance your writing skills.\\r\\n\\r\\nExperienced print and TV journalist Pam Cohen will explore issues of why we write, what is memoir and how we can broaden out to open different doorways into the self.\\r\\nWeek One: Why, when and how we write. What is memoir/biography/autobiography?\\r\\nWeek Two: Exploring different techniques of creative non fiction\\r\\nWeek Three: The role of truth and memory in life writing\\r\\nWeek Four:  The “eye” and the “I” in life writing\\r\\n\\r\\nPam Cohen has completed an MA in Creative Writing at The Open University where she specialised in creative non-fiction. She was a print and television journalist in South Africa for some years, working for a women’s magazine, a national Sunday newspaper and British television, before coming to London. She has also worked as a teacher. She has a passion for both teaching and writing.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Introduction to Life Writing*\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 February-11 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"466801ASCBRTMRPDVBRTSHGQDQLRVHTTQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-04T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-11T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Pam Cohen\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Part of the Kinoteka Polish Film Festival. 19-year-old Irena Gut Opdyke is promoted to housekeeper in the home of a highly respected Nazi officer when she finds out that the Jewish ghetto is about to be liquidated. Determined to help twelve Jewish workers, she decides to shelter them in the safest place she can think of: the basement of the German commandant's house. Over the next two years, Irena uses her wit, humour, and courage to hide her friends until the end of the German occupation. Her story is one of the most inspiring of our time.\\r\\nThis screening is part of the 23rd KINOTEKA Polish Film Festival, 6 March to 25 April 2025, bringing another compelling line-up of contemporary and classic Polish cinema. | Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 1m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":121,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a2a382e4-e566-4bbe-ad44-b2580cd26fc0.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Irena's Vow\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 March-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a2a382e4-e566-4bbe-ad44-b2580cd26fc0-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"479801ATBVSCTRPPKKSTNPHJPNBRLDVDH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-23T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-23T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Kinoteka Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £30 adult £15 student, in-building // Irène Duval has been a soloist with the Philharmonia, Dresdner Philharmonie, Sinfonia Varsovia, Kremerata Baltica, and COE and has performed chamber music with Steven Isserlis, Joshua Bell, Jean-Efflam Bavouzet, Gidon Kremer, Olli Mustonen, and Christian Tetzlaff. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nAlasdair Beatson is the superb pianist of the Nash Ensemble, making a welcome return to JW3.  \\r\\n\\r\\nAsbjørn Nørgaard is one of the leading classical Danish musicians of his generation, and the outstanding violist of the world-class Danish String Quartet. Asbjørn also teaches viola and chamber music at the Royal Danish Academy of Music. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nMozart’s often played E minor masterpiece for piano and violin was profoundly affected by the recent death of his mother.  Fauré’s first piano quartet is full of youthful vitality and imagination and is one of his most immediately appealing works.  Brahms’s first piano quartet is composed of beautifully conceived melodies and its vigorous Finale in the Zingarese (Gypsy) style is thrilling -an exciting way to bring the series to an end.  \\r\\n\\r\\n**please note a slight change in line up than originally advertised**\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Irène Duval, Asbjørn Nørgaard, David Waterman, and Alasdair Beatson\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 March-12 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"398201AQMNTLSBCTKHVVPHGQSMSVTCJGG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am–12.15pm, £20 per session or £90 for the 5 weeks // Just about every Jew knows about the built-in prejudices of the United Nations against Israel and the regular, disproportionate attacks and condemnation that Israel regularly suffers there as a result. // In this programme though, Clive intends to stand back a bit and look at the United Nations as a whole - not just in the light of its dreadful record on Israel but also in the light of its myriad other activities.  // Taking the rough with the smooth, is the UN a force for good overall or an aggravating feature in the real messy world we all live in? \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Is The United Nations Better Than Nothing? [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-8 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489001AMDNHBBRDLKNQPDGRRTLNBJRPNG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-10T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-08T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Clive Lawton\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am–12.15pm, £20 per session or £90 for the 5 weeks // Just about every Jew knows about the built-in prejudices of the United Nations against Israel and the regular, disproportionate attacks and condemnation that Israel regularly suffers there as a result. // In this programme though, Clive intends to stand back a bit and look at the United Nations as a whole - not just in the light of its dreadful record on Israel but also in the light of its myriad other activities. // Taking the rough with the smooth, is the UN a force for good overall or an aggravating feature in the real messy world we all live in?\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Is The United Nations Better Than Nothing? [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-8 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489201ANMKSLTRLRMLVBNVMSGCVHTTRNJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-10T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-08T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Clive Lawton\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesday 5 February, 2pm – 3pm, £20, also available online \\r\\n\\r\\nHow will 2025 look for Israel? Jonathan will explore who won the Gaza War; Iran, Hezbollah and the Houthis, and US relations with Israel under the new administration. \\r\\n \\r\\nJonathan is a London-based Middle East analyst and appears as a commentator on Sky, BBC, France 24 and Al Arabiya. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Israel: Outlook for 2025 \",\"instanceDates\":\"5 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450601AVGGJSCJPNKGVDNHQDLKLQPCHHM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, £20, hybrid // Peter will explore the connection between the founders of the Federation of Women Zionists (1918), later WIZO (1920), and the women’s suffrage movement in the UK, including the militant Women's Social and Political Union. \\r\\n\\r\\nHe'll highlight how many key figures in these Zionist organisations were also active in the fight for women's political rights, especially following the 1918 Representation of the People Act, which granted voting rights to women over 30 in Britain.\\r\\n\\r\\nPeter is Lecturer in Oriental Studies at Mansfield College, specialising on the British Mandate for Palestine, with a particular interest in Maximalist-Revisionist Zionism.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Feminism: Between Suffrage and WIZO\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 February-10 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453002AJCCNRBQTTBKTMMJQHTLNLCCCNQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-10T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Oxford Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8pm, £20, hybrid // For over two millennia, Jewish communities used languages like Aramaic, Yiddish, Ladino, and Judeo-Arabic for daily communication and writing. These languages became part of a vibrant book culture, reaching wide audiences through affordable publications. \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover how Jewish languages have evolved over the centuries, offering us an extraordinary insight into the linguistic richness of Jewish life.\\r\\n\\r\\nJudith is President of the Oxford Centre for Hebrew and Jewish Studies and Fellow of Corpus Christi College. César is Hebrew and Judaica Curator at the Bodleian Library and Director of the Leopold Muller Memorial Library. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Languages and Book Culture\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 January-20 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452601ATSCSCJPLKKCTPRPDVHBJTDDLLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-20T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-20T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Oxford Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wed 11 June 2025 //\\r\\n7:00pm //\\r\\n£20 //\\r\\nDiscover \\\"Jewish Odesa\\\" with Dr. Marina Sapritsky-Nahum\\r\\n\\r\\nExplore Jewish Identity and Revival in Odesa\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an illuminating evening with Dr. Marina Sapritsky-Nahum as she delves into the fascinating and complex history of Jewish communities in Odesa.\\r\\n\\r\\nDrawing on years of ethnographic research and her acclaimed book Jewish Odesa: Negotiating Identities and Traditions in Contemporary Ukraine, Dr. Sapritsky-Nahum will explore how Jewish life in this historic port city has navigated waves of change, from Soviet rule to Ukrainian independence, and through the profound disruptions of Russia’s invasion of Ukraine.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk will shed light on how Odesa’s Jewish residents have redefined their identities and traditions in the context of cultural revival, migration, and national transformation. Discover the resilience and adaptability of a community deeply rooted in Odesa’s cosmopolitan heritage yet continually evolving to meet the challenges of a rapidly changing world.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout the Speaker:\\r\\n\\r\\nDr. Marina Sapritsky-Nahum is a renowned anthropologist whose work focuses on post-Soviet Jewish experiences, migration, philanthropy, and religious revival. Her research bridges anthropology, history, and Jewish studies, with a focus on Ukraine and its diaspora. Currently a Visiting Fellow at LSE and an Honorary Research Fellow at UCL, Dr. Sapritsky-Nahum has been documenting the impact of war, migration, and heritage preservation on Ukrainian Jewish life.\\r\\n\\r\\nKey Highlights:\\r\\n• Insights from her book, Jewish Odesa, which has received critical acclaim.\\r\\n• An in-depth look at Jewish identity in contemporary Ukraine.\\r\\n• Reflections on the challenges and resilience of Jewish communities amid geopolitical upheavals.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis event is a must for anyone interested in Jewish history, post-Soviet culture, or the dynamics of identity and belonging in times of transformation.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Odesa\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 June-11 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"483801ARJHBLBVLMBBHMGBLVDPVRQPNPG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-11T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Book Launches\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marina Sapritsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building // Charlston’s heavenly voice, Manson’s exquisite gamba and cello playing, and Bucheli’s delicate and sensitive lute playing promise to be perfectly matched with each other and with the music in their fascinating and very varied programme of composers all born before J S Bach (albeit Handel by only 7 weeks). // \\r\\nThe centrepiece is a dramatic and impassioned Handel cantata, and the other..shorter.. pieces by Purcell, Dowland, Marais, Charpentier et al are equally riveting.  The very intimate JW3 Hall will be perfect for this music. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jonathan Manson, Helen Charlston, and Sergio Bucheli\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 October-30 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493201ADJCCLQBTHJLVHRBCJGNRQKGPJQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-10-30T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-10-30T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"As the star player at an elite youth tennis academy, Julie's life revolves around the game she loves. She trains hard, pausing only for class or physical therapy before returning to the gym fixated on making it into the Belgian Tennis Federation. When her coach Jérémy is suddenly suspended following the suicide of one of his female protégées, all the players at the academy are encouraged to speak up about their experiences with him. Julie, however, decides to keep quiet. Despite strong suspicions from those around her that Julie's relationship with Jérémy was inappropriate at best, her persistent silence begins to speak volumes. Confused and full of anxiety, the pressure she once channeled solely towards training shifts inward, affecting her confidence, her focus, and her game. Executive produced by tennis champion Naomi Osaka, Julie Keeps Quiet is a \\\"tense, taut, artfully hushed debut feature\\\" (Variety) by Belgian writer-director Leonardo van Dijl. Led by newcomer Tessa Van den Broeck whose performance embodies the different ways trauma is internalized, Julie Keeps Quiet respectfully and empathetically examines why some victims choose to remain silent. | This film is in French and Dutch with English subtitles | Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h30m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/8dbd0b6b-5455-4242-a7b7-56d92ede8f73.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Julie Keeps Quiet\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-22 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/8dbd0b6b-5455-4242-a7b7-56d92ede8f73-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507601ABLBKJGMTTTVQPPDHTTKQQVMDQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T14:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £17, ages 16+ // JW3 Comedy Club is back showcasing the best in Jewish Comedy. We’re bringing you Jewish and Jew-ish comics, from rising stars to names you'll recognise, and not just from sitting next to them at your niece's bat mitzvah! Be aware, you might hear one or two words that your Bubbe only said in Yiddish, hoping you wouldn't understand...   Line Ups will be announced through JW3’s socials and mailing list so make sure not to miss out.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3 Comedy Club (February)\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"467801AHQTBMMPKBTRGPRKDJVKGVPPKJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-26T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy Club\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £17, age 16+ // JW3 Comedy Club is back showcasing the best in Jewish Comedy. We’re bringing you Jewish and Jew-ish comics, from rising stars to names you'll recognise, and not just from sitting next to them at your niece's bat mitzvah! Be aware, you might hear one or two words that your Bubbe only said in Yiddish, hoping you wouldn't understand... \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\nLine Ups will be announced through JW3’s socials and mailing list so make sure not to miss out.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3 Comedy Club (January)\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"467402ACCQBLSGLDJDJKQPQCQHHKPDSQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-29T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-29T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy Club\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £17, in building // 16+ // JW3 Comedy Club is back showcasing the best in Jewish Comedy. We’re bringing you Jewish and Jew-ish comics, from rising stars to names you'll recognise, and not just from sitting next to them at your niece's bat mitzvah! Be aware, you might hear one or two words that your Bubbe only said in Yiddish, hoping you wouldn't understand...\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3 Comedy Club (June)\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 June-25 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491001ADTLRNBMCMTVQRBJDLCTDCVNNHT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-25T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-25T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy Club\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £17, ages 16+ // JW3 Comedy Club is back showcasing the best in Jewish Comedy. We’re bringing you Jewish and Jew-ish comics, from rising stars to names you'll recognise, and not just from sitting next to them at your niece's bat mitzvah! Be aware, you might hear one or two words that your Bubbe only said in Yiddish, hoping you wouldn't understand...   Line Ups will be announced through JW3’s socials and mailing list so make sure not to miss out.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3 Comedy Club (March)\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 March-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"468001ADGQHDCJVTLNLLRJBJBBBQMDGPK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy Club\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Winter pop-up at JW3 // 8 Dec - 5 Jan // 12noon - 8pm Sun-Thurs // 7pm-9pm Sat // Pre-bookings through Kasa's website. Customers must select JW3 as the venue when making their booking. Walk ins are also available but booking is strongly recommended.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":600,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Kasa Bar & Grill \",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"446401AKTCJHVNBVCVCJCNKDBJQNTMQCB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-15T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-17T12:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wed 02 July 2025 // \\r\\n11:00am //\\r\\n£20 // We have all heard of King Arthur and his knights of the Round Table but who was Arthur? Was he a real live historic individual or was he always just a figure of fiction? On this issue, historians disagree profoundly. This talk takes us into the so-called ‘Dark Ages’, the period after the Romans had left Britain when Arthur is supposed to have lived. It is a world where a post-Roman British society was trying desperately to defend itself against the incursions of the Anglo-Saxons from across the North Sea. It was a society in need of heroes. Was there really a king who fought back against the incomers or did a beleaguered society create its own myth?\\r\\nCome along and find out more about a mysterious period in our history. \\r\\n\\r\\nJill Stern is an historian. Aged twenty she graduated with first class honours in History from King’s College London. Much of her working life was spent as a teacher at Wycombe Abbey School and as chairman of a Health Authority in West London and vice-chairman of North Thames Regional Health Authority. Returning to academic study she gained an MA (Distinction) and a doctorate in seventeenth century Dutch history at University College London. As a doctoral student she was awarded the prestigious Pollard Prize for History. She has a book and many published articles to her credit. She has lectured in Britain, the Netherlands and New York. History is her lifelong passion and she is keen to share that passion.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"King Arthur: History or Myth\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 July-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"484601AHRRMMSNCNVVRBHSMJMGCCPPGMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-02T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-02T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The series explores the lives of Noacham Shtisel, a diamond dealer and the estranged brother of Shulem Shtisel, and his daughter Libbi, as they grapple with the departure of the family matriarch. While Noacham seeks forgiveness for his ex-wife in the hope that she will return, Libbi refuses to make room for her mother in her life. At the same time, Libbi harbors a secret dream that could jeopardize her chances of finding a suitable match. | We will be screening the first two episodes of Kugel | This programme is in Hebrew and Yiddish with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 90 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d9b5cba4-fc08-496e-9a03-cef60a2d86b3.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Kugel + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d9b5cba4-fc08-496e-9a03-cef60a2d86b3-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503202ALPMRTGCKRKLQHCPJNGLVSJNLRJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"La Cocina captures the frenetic energy of the lunch rush at The Grill, a bustling restaurant in Manhattan's Times Square. When money goes missing from the till, suspicion falls on Pedro, an undocumented cook who dreams of a better life and is in love with Julia, an American waitress who cannot commit to a relationship. Rashid, the restaurant owner, has promised to help Pedro obtain legal status, but a shocking revelation about Julia compels Pedro to spiral into an act that threatens to shut down one of the city's busiest kitchens once and for all. The film is a comic and tragic tribute to the invisible people who keep our restaurants running and our stomachs full, all while chasing an elusive version of the American dream. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 19m\\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":139,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1543e7fb-0289-4b2e-9243-47f7caf0b51f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"La Cocina\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-24 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1543e7fb-0289-4b2e-9243-47f7caf0b51f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499201AVCKTTNTDMGTKJTPVMPCRDQVKVP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-22T18:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T15:50:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm–8.45pm, £15, building, age 13+ // Join us for the screening of documentary film Liga Terezin, that tells the incredible story of the football league which took place in Ghetto Theresienstadt, from 1942 to 1944.  // Jewish prisoners played hundreds of matches in the courtyards of the Barracks where they lived. Thousands of spectators watched a mixture of professional and amateur players and briefly escaped the reality of their terrible plight, shrouded in fear cast by the terror of the transports that sent people to the 'East' and their certain death.  // A panel, with some of the biggest names in sports journalism and antisemitism, will follow the screening. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Liga Terezin: Screening and Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 April-24 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"490401AQJJGMCHQHDGKMSVLBPSJPVLRHS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Luisa Gottardo\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, £20, online only // Discover the daily life of Egyptian Jews during the Graeco-Roman period through papyrological evidence. These documents, preserved in the Corpus Papyrorum Judaicarum, offer insights into their social, economic and religious life. From legal contracts to religious observances, the papyri reveal how Jewish communities balanced their traditions within the broader Graeco-Roman world.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeron is Associate Professor of Ancient Jewish History, with his research focusing on the history of the Second Temple period, the Jews in ancient Egypt and Jewish papyrology. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Lives Unrolled: Tracing Jewish Life through Ancient Egyptian Papyri\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-3 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"453001ALBHSCJBBSPQGDKMJJNLLRDMSPJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Oxford Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10am-12noon, £20, off-site // Meeting location provided upon booking // Step into the footsteps of brilliant minds who shaped the modern world. This fascinating walking tour along the scenic Regent’s Canal unveils the stories of visionary scientists, engineers, and innovators whose groundbreaking work transformed transportation, medicine, electronics, and AI.\\r\\n\\r\\nAs you stroll through this historic area—often compared to Amsterdam’s charming canal life—you’ll uncover the hidden history behind world-changing discoveries and inventions. Led by expert guide Boaz Tal, this tour offers a unique blend of history, science, and culture, bringing the past to life in the very place where innovation thrived.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking. \\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Londoners Who Changed the World\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491602AKMPCRDDGMJLRBSVMSRDKNDQQCK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T10:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Boaz Tal\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Date: Sunday, March 30, 2025. //\\r\\nTime: 2:00 PM - 4:00 PM. //\\r\\nLocation: Starting point will be provided upon booking. //\\r\\n\\r\\nLondon's Jewish History over the Centuries\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an enlightening walking tour to explore 1000 years of Jewish history. This experience is for everyone interested in London’s extraordinary culture and heritage! \\r\\n\\r\\nStarting in Aldgate and crossing the historic City of London, you will discover the fascinating story of London’s Jewish population from medieval times to the present day. Learn about the Jews brought to England by William the Conqueror after 1066, the expulsion under Edward I in 1290, the resettlement under Cromwell in 1656, and subsequent Jewish immigration up to the present day. \\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our walk, you will see many of the most important sites in the City – including those connected to London’s rich and complex Jewish history. Hear about various London Jewish personalities over the years, and about Jewish life in Britain and beyond. Don’t miss this opportunity to delve into centuries of Jewish and general history in London. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"London's Jewish History over the Centuries\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 March-8 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455401AMHJVTKCLNLVQKLVCSSGSMMTQQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-30T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-08T15:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am - 12noon, building, whole course must be booked, £144 // Judaism was classically depicted as a religion shaped by law, with its emotionally deficient adherents restricted to performing commanded actions.  But Jews and Judaism definitely don’t lack feeling and are absolutely not deficient in love! Three great loves, in particular, have coloured the Jewish tradition: loving God, loving our neighbour, loving the stranger.  Without needing to make comparisons or reference negative stereotypes, we’ll explore Jewish insights into the lasting strength and beauty of these loves. And we’ll totally love it! // Angela has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She is the author of over 40 books on aspects of religion and history, and is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Love Love Love\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"486202ARSSQGPNKCBSLSGJPPGSQRSTMLN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-14T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Angela Gluck\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"124 // 15 // Maria Callas, the world's greatest opera singer, lives the last days of her life in 1970s Paris, as she confronts her identity and life.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Maria\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-30 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471602AQGKCJKTLDCGLJGGGJHKKNQKKPM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T13:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-30T20:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building //Whether playing concerti, chamber music or unaccompanied violin, or directing orchestras such as Chamber  Orchestra of Europe or the Royal Northern Sinfonia, Polish-born Maria Włoszczowska captivates her audiences with her liveliness, charm, and finesse and her palpable love of music and of the violin. Alasdair Beatson’s charisma and expressiveness is already well known to JW3 audiences. // The programme includes two unsurpassable major masterpieces from the piano trio repertoire by Schumann and Brahms.  The two middle movements of the Schumann trio are amongst the most overwhelmingly moving in the trio literature. The concert opens with Mendelssohn’s marvellous F major violin and piano sonata. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":129,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Maria Włoszczowska, David Waterman, and Alasdair Beatson\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493801AJMGJBVQDLNMHLKCTRKMNMRVPTL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Join us for a special retrospective honoring Director Erez Tadmor, featuring this charming and heartwarming romantic comedy with a delightful Orthodox twist on Romeo and Juliet. Full of humor, love, and unexpected turns, this film offers a fresh take on a timeless classic, bringing together two worlds in a story that’s as touching as it is entertaining. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 118 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":158,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d8dee476-0ead-459e-9394-12fda5fad513.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Matchmaking 2\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d8dee476-0ead-459e-9394-12fda5fad513-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"504401APHGTVLTBQSKLSDKHQSSKTDBLBP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Join us for a special retrospective honoring Director Erez Tadmor, featuring this charming and heartwarming romantic comedy with a delightful Orthodox twist on Romeo and Juliet. Full of humor, love, and unexpected turns, this film offers a fresh take on a timeless classic, bringing together two worlds in a story that’s as touching as it is entertaining. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival  | Duration: 118 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":118,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/46cab692-967f-4a34-810c-e47017848cdf.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Matchmaking 2 + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/46cab692-967f-4a34-810c-e47017848cdf-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"501601AQMBSPPSDTSLHJDDMTRDKNLGRDC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T17:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"17 June 2-3.30pm, 2 July 7-8.30pm, building, £12 // Meet the artist behind the vibrant and colourful history of the London Jewish community, splashed across a 9-storey mural for everyone to see!   \\r\\n\\r\\nWe’ll take an artistic journey through the artwork, its story, and strange and magical stories of London’s Jews. \\r\\n\\r\\nLeon is an artist from London, whose life has been split between the UK, US and Asia. His art is a bold new form of visual storytelling. Around the world, from Taiwan to Mexico, families, communities, cities and organizations have commissioned Leon to depict their story in his kaleidoscopic style. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Meet the Artist: Leon Fenster\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 June-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"484801AVHMNCRBKQPHRRVLMLQVNJLQHDP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-17T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-02T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Mural\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Leon Fenster\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"24 June, 7-8.30pm, £12 // Come and hear the stories that inspired Leon to create this wonderful artwork that celebrates the diverse and dynamic contributions of Jewish individuals to London's history and culture. \\r\\nThe mural, featuring over 150 faces from historical figures to local legends, includes scenes such as Nicholas Winton and the Kindertransport, Queen Elizabeth I at the trial of her Jewish doctor, and Jewish boxers across generations. Notable personalities like Freud, Benjamin Disraeli, and a host of rabbis including Julia Neuberger and Jonathan Sacks are vividly brought to life. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Meet the Mural\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 June-24 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485001ACRTHQRBJQSKCPLKDHGCDDCJQBS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-24T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Mural\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Leon Fenster\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Grace Pudel is a lonely misfit with an affinity for collecting ornamental snails and an intense love for books. At a young age, when Grace is separated from her fire-breathing twin brother Gilbert, she falls into a spiral of anxiety and angst. Despite a continued series of hardships, inspiration and hope emerge when she strikes up an enduring friendship with an elderly eccentric woman named Pinky, who is full of grit and lust for life | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 35m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/fb89205d-ccc0-48dc-908d-1bb1c6e21db9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Memoir of a Snail\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 March-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/fb89205d-ccc0-48dc-908d-1bb1c6e21db9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480201ARHLHQPDTTRMJDCPGNRNGDSTVVB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-03T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T17:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, hybrid // George explores the professional careers of Mickey Rooney and Judy Garland in such classic films as Babes In Arms, Andy Hardy and Words & Music. Dive into the life and careers of two top entertainers.\\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has worked in the media for over 35 years, latterly at the BBC where he was responsible for all feature films and non-UK TV series. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mickey & Judy: Together at MGM\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452602AGDHTGQTSHQRKMQVJHBBGHHNKGT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-29T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-29T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"From the Academy Award-winner Bong Joon Ho, comes his next groundbreaking cinematic experience. The unlikely hero, Mickey Barnes has found himself in the extraordinary circumstance of working for an employer who demands the ultimate commitment to the job… to die, for a living. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 17m \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":137,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c9696c1b-750f-49e5-81f1-60951dfb56a1.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mickey 17\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 April-10 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c9696c1b-750f-49e5-81f1-60951dfb56a1-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"500601ABPSQLDCTCJGCCKMPBNBNBGJGPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-06T19:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-10T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am - 12.15pm, £20 per session, £198 for 11 wks // \\r\\nPaula will explore how the region developed during this decade, the rise of the Arab nationalism and the divisions and territorial ambitions.\\r\\n\\r\\nPaula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Middle East 1936-46 [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"449801ATMCHQPQRBHNGBGLKGVJGHHSQDQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am - 12.15pm, £20 per session, £198 for 11 wks // Paula will explore how the region developed during this decade, the rise of the Arab nationalism and the divisions and territorial ambitions. Paula is an historian and writer. She regularly contributes to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Middle East 1936-46 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"450001ABCVNQGTNDGCBBSMCJPSPMRVDRR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-31T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The teasingly entwined ambiguities of love and death continue to fascinate Alain Guiraudie, who returns with a sharp, sinister, yet slyly funny thriller. Set in an autumnal, woodsy village in his native region of Occitanie, his latest follows the meandering exploits of Jérémie, an out-of-work baker who has drifted back to his hometown after the death of his beloved former boss, a bakery owner. Staying long after the funeral, the seemingly benign Jérémie begins to casually insinuate himself into his mentor's family, including his kind-hearted widow and venomously angry son, while making an increasingly surprising--and ultimately beneficial--friendship with an oddly cheerful local priest. In Guiraudie’s quietly carnal world, violence and eroticism explode with little anticipation, and criminal behavior can seem like a natural extension of physical desire. The French director is at the top of his game in Misericordia, again upending all genre expectations. \\r\\n\\r\\n| This film is French with English subtitles. \\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 44m  \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":104,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/eeb830cb-7847-4f88-95e3-95091f1afdf5.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Misericordia\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-24 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/eeb830cb-7847-4f88-95e3-95091f1afdf5-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499601AGDQMDDGTSMHSNJLMMPPVCGMNDM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-22T16:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-24T13:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"5.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building // Both Mishka and Alasdair have enraptured JW3 audiences in multiple appearances so it will be enthralling to hear them collaborate and share one piano for this unusual and beautifully conceived programme. // Schubert wrote many masterpieces for four hands; Ravel is a master of colour and subtlety; Rachmaninov was one of the greatest pianists and composers of the 20th century; the Bach arrangement is perfectly realised by the great contemporary composer Kurtag; Brahms and Dvorak were also masters of four-hand writing.  This will be a hugely enjoyable treat.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mishka Rushdie Momen and Alasdair Beatson\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 November-16 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493401AVKCNTQJRKSGBBBLGHVDHSHVNRP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-11-16T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-11-16T17:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10:30-12:30, £20 per session, £180 for the 10 week course, in-building // Join Aviva as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature. Dr Aviva Dautch is the Executive Director of Jewish Renaissance, the UK's Jewish arts magazine. She is a published poet, has a PhD in literature and lectures on modern Jewish literature weekly at JW3. She is a regular contributor to courses and programmes for the British Library, British Museum and BBC Radio 4 and LSJS.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 January-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"451401AKTVQQCVQNGHKHPNBBVCVVQQRHJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays // 8 May – 10 July*  *No class 29 May //\\r\\n10.30am–12.30pm // £20 per session or £162 for the 9 weeks //\\r\\nAlso available online // Join Aviva as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature. \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Aviva Dautch is the Executive Director of Jewish Renaissance, the UK's Jewish arts magazine. She is a published poet, has a PhD in literature and lectures on modern Jewish literature weekly at JW3. She is a regular contributor to courses and programmes for the British Library, British Museum and BBC Radio 4 and LSJS. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 May-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"497601ATGLLPSHPJDBSMBGDSGVQDLDTVL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-08T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10:30-12:30, £20 per session, £180 for the 10 week course, in-building // Join Aviva as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature. Dr Aviva Dautch is the Executive Director of Jewish Renaissance, the UK's Jewish arts magazine. She is a published poet, has a PhD in literature and lectures on modern Jewish literature weekly at JW3. She is a regular contributor to courses and programmes for the British Library, British Museum and BBC Radio 4 and LSJS.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 January-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"451801APTKQSLVTDLSPJRPMQLHQDLVLLB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10:30-12:30, £20 per session, £180 for the 10 week course, in-building // Join Aviva as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature. Dr Aviva Dautch is the Executive Director of Jewish Renaissance, the UK's Jewish arts magazine. She is a published poet, has a PhD in literature and lectures on modern Jewish literature weekly at JW3. She is a regular contributor to courses and programmes for the British Library, British Museum and BBC Radio 4 and LSJS.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 May-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"497801ADMGSQQPTRSJSHRQTTQGBDVDCCV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-08T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mr. Burton tells the true story of the relationship between Port Talbot schoolmaster Philip Burton and a wild young schoolboy called Richard Jenkins, the son of a wayward drunk. Richard dreamed of becoming an actor, but his ambitions were in danger of being derailed by a combination of family trouble, the pressure of war, and his own lack of discipline. Mr. Burton recognized the raw talent in his pupil, becoming his tutor, strict taskmaster and eventually his adoptive father. | Rating: 12A, Duration: 2h 4m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/dc95501c-7948-4d87-b4f5-bdae6652a6bc.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mr Burton\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 May-22 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/dc95501c-7948-4d87-b4f5-bdae6652a6bc-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506202ARNPTCKDHKJLSJDVBQQMSSCLTJD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-21T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T16:40:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £20, in building // Ages 16+, contains references to sex // Join us for a unique drag extravaganza showcasing the magical, imaginative world of a woman living with motor neurone disease for decades. Starring internationally renowned drag artists, Cheddar Gorgeous, Pixie Polite, Tete Bang, Duane Nasis and Chanukah Lewinsky. \\r\\n\\r\\nSarah Ezekiel is a paralysed visual artist with Motor Neurone Disease (MND), who created Ms MaNDy’s Adventures in Wonderland using eye gaze technology and incorporating AI and animation. She writes, storyboards, designs, and directs this live theatre production using eye and chin movements.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe show features original music by Alex Herd, a composer also living with MND.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Ms MaNDy's Adventures in Wonderland\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 June-15 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488001AMPDDRTBMCVSPTJCNJMHQLDNBJM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-15T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Seven-time BAFTA Award-winner Steve Coogan (Alan Partridge, The Trip) plays four roles in the world premiere stage adaptation of Stanley Kubrick’s comedy masterpiece Dr. Strangelove. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a rogue U.S General triggers a nuclear attack, a surreal race takes place,seeing the Government and one eccentric scientist scramble to avert global destruction.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis explosively funny satire is led by a world-renowned creative team including Emmy Award-winner Armando Iannucci (The Thick of It, Veep) and Olivier Award-winner Sean Foley (The Upstart Crow, The Play What I Wrote).\\r\\n\\r\\n| Duration: 2 hours 30 minutes, Rating: TBC \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":250,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e0ac1f91-3359-4970-a630-21b38957038b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Dr Strangelove\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 March-27 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e0ac1f91-3359-4970-a630-21b38957038b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472401AHGGHJJNNQQDHDDRKKJMJDVPJGV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-27T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Max Webster directs a joyful and flamboyant reimagining of Oscar Wilde’s most celebrated comedy. Olivier Award-winner Sharon D Clarke is joined by Ncuti Gatwa and Hugh Skinner in this hilarious story of identity, impersonation and romance. \\r\\n170 minutes including an interval // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":170,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c5e3a372-fd13-4365-af15-7ff31417871d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: The Importance of Being Earnest\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 February-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c5e3a372-fd13-4365-af15-7ff31417871d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"475001AJDRDMPVSNKRQDBCKGDDPMCMSPV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-20T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm - 8.30pm, £12 per household, online only // Which secondary school should your child go to?\\r\\n\\r\\nAndrew Doe, Head of Middle School (Years 7-9) at Habs Girls until June 2022, will speak in depth about his experience of 11+ entrance exams and their likely requirements in the current climate. Together with Gabriella Wagerman, experienced 11+ tutor, they will discuss in depth the key considerations when selecting a school for your child to move on to.\\r\\n\\r\\nGaby will explain the importance of assessments, finding the right tutor and the right guidance, as well as advising on how parents can ensure children reach their potential whilst keeping expectations realistic. They will also discuss how both independent school and grammar school examinations changed in recent years due to Covid and how the landscape is likely to look going forwards.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere will be an opportunity for questions at the end of the talk. Suitable for parents of children in years 3, 4 and 5.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Navigating the 11+ Journey\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-3 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"435201AVCQSMQDCHVMDJJSNSPQDBKNCDT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, hybrid, £12 // In the 1930s, thousands of refugees from Nazi Europe got to work rebuilding their lives — as well as their continental coffee houses, restaurants, social clubs, bookshops and cabarets — along Finchley Road.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nSo many, in fact, that bus conductors would yell \\\"Next stop, Finchleystrasse!\\\" as they approached. From the Cosmo, Dorice and Balsam cafes to the Laterndl theatre and Blue Danube Club, the establishments of this microcosm of Mitteleuropa became a home from home for the displaced of NW3 and a tribute to a vanished world. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nEtan is a London-based freelance journalist, whose work has featured in publications on four continents, including The New York Times, The Daily Telegraph, The Guardian, The Times, The Independent, FT, Daily Mail, The Forward, LA Times and The Australian. He is also a grandson of two Finchleystrasse pioneers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Next Stop, Finchleystrasse!\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 July-9 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485401ADKDTDLDHLRHNPHMQLTJCQVJQNC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-09T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-09T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Mural\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Etan Smallman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This film made by a Palestinian-Israeli collective shows the destruction of the occupied West Bank's Masafer Yatta by Israeli soldiers and the alliance which develops between the Palestinian activist Basel and Israeli journalist Yuval \\r\\n\\r\\n| Duration: 1h 32m, Rating: 15 \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":92,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a8f3a5f6-f48c-4793-ab85-a82e9a56dfd8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"No Other Land \",\"instanceDates\":\"8 April-9 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a8f3a5f6-f48c-4793-ab85-a82e9a56dfd8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"448001AQNLSCKPVVRJQCQVSRVDJBHVTPH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-08T19:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-09T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"133 // 15 // A gothic tale of obsession between a haunted young woman and the terrifying vampire infatuated with her, causing untold horror in its wake.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":133,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Nosferatu\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-23 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471201APNSLDLGLGQRLTCJQHJRJBLLHDQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-19T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-23T16:10:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Inspired by the harrowing events of 7/10, this gripping film follows 16-year-old Dar as she returns to her kibbutz in search of her lost dog amidst a terror spree. As she navigates the horrors around her, Dar is caught between escalating violence beyond the fence, those thirsting for revenge, and those holding onto hope and humanity. A tense and emotional journey through chaos, where survival and compassion collide. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 82 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":82,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c5413ebb-68fa-4dd2-a340-c2217b908824.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Of Dogs and Men + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c5413ebb-68fa-4dd2-a340-c2217b908824-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502602ALSNPTRRKCKRCBLRKLBRPSCCNNG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T20:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T20:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesday 19 February, 7pm – 8.30pm, £20 // \\r\\n\\r\\nAmidst the noise of political mudslinging and misinformation, it’s become nearly impossible to discuss antisemitism constructively.  \\r\\n\\r\\nIn Off-White, Rachel Shabi untangles the complex histories of racism and antisemitism. Her urgent analysis shines a light on how recognising this complexity can build stronger coalitions and guide progressive politics forward in today’s divisive climate. Join her for her book launch, in conversation with Alona Ferber. \\r\\n \\r\\nRachel has written for the Guardian, The New York Times,  \\r\\nIndependent, the Nation, Prospect magazine and The New York  \\r\\nReview of Books. Alona is the editor of the New Statesman's Spotlight policy section and supplement. She also writes specialist coverage of Israel and conducts interviews with major public figures.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Off-White: Rachel Shabi in conversation with Alona Ferber  \",\"instanceDates\":\"19 February-19 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"451201ADNBBKLVHCCGTBHTQTTKGGQGVPV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-19T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Shabi\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-8pm, free but donation requested, in building // Join New York’s Park Avenue Synagogue rabbi, R.Elliot Cosgrove, author of For Such a Time as This: On Being Jewish Today, for a thought-provoking conversation with Rabbi Miriam Berger, Founding Director of Wellspring.\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\nRabbi Cosgrove has earned his reputation as one of American Jewry’s leading voices. In the aftermath of October 7, 2023, a day that marked a turning point for the Jewish community worldwide, he reflects on the rise of antisemitism and the enduring strength of Jewish identity. Drawing on a rich trove of Jewish history and tradition, he has written an essential guide to help make sense of this fraught moment, what it means to be Jewish today and the challenging questions embedded in the soul of contemporary Jewry.\\r\\n\\r\\nThrough warmth and insight, For Such a Time as This highlights the profound connection to community, culture, and faith that sustains Jewish life, even in challenging times.\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThis intimate evening, hosted by JW3, the Board of Deputies, and JLC, promises to be an inspiring exploration of what it means to be Jewish today. It will be hugely relevant to all those involved in Jewish education, leadership, community building, or Israel-Diaspora endeavours.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are offering this as a free event, with encouragement to please consider making a donation to help us cover the costs of the event.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"On Being Jewish Today: An Evening with Rabbi Elliot Cosgrove\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 March-10 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"478401ATQPLHNLPQCMGGHNBRMLTQTPBTV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-10T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-10T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"An expansive and revelatory inside look at the 18 months John Lennon and Yoko Ono spent living in Greenwich Village in the early 1970s, One to One: John & Yoko, delivers an immersive cinematic experience that brings to life electrifying, never-before-seen material and newly restored footage of Lennon's only full-length, post-Beatles concert. With mind-blowing remastered audio overseen by their son, Sean Ono Lennon, the film is a seismic revelation that will challenge pre-existing notions of the iconic couple. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 40m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/10493666-af3b-4ec7-ae57-57c27e07af5f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"One to One: John & Yoko\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 May-8 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/10493666-af3b-4ec7-ae57-57c27e07af5f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506401AHJMJNVKHPRLTRRBCHPKDNCLNGD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-04T16:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-08T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 2-4.30pm, in building, £25 per session or £220 for the 10 week course // Do you want to learn to paint and draw or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSuitable for all levels from beginners to experienced, students in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals.  Basic art materials are provided; specialised materials must be purchased independently.  Please note that each class has limited numbers to ensure each student has adequate time with the tutor.\\r\\n\\r\\nMichael Ajerman is an American representational painter based in London. He has exhibited his work nationally and internationally. He has taught in a wide variety of educational settings and levels.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio - Winter 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-30 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"466001ADTSVLRVKPTVPBNMKBPGSGDRGJJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-08T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 2pm-4.30pm, £25 per session or £200 for 9 the week course // Do you want to learn to paint and draw or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSuitable for all levels from beginners to experienced, students in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals.  Basic art materials are provided; specialised materials must be purchased independently.  Please note that each class has limited numbers to ensure each student has adequate time with the tutor.\\r\\n\\r\\nMichael Ajerman is an American representational painter based in London. He has exhibited his work nationally and internationally. He has taught in a wide variety of educational settings and levels.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio (Daytime)\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 May-23 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"500201ABVLSVVHCLDBNQNRTSMJNGSGDTP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-07T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-23T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm–8.30pm, £25 per session or £135 for the 6 weeks, building only // Do you want to learn to paint and draw or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you.  // Suitable for all levels from beginners to experienced, students in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects).  //  The teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals.  Basic art materials are provided; specialised materials must be purchased independently.  Please note that each class has limited numbers to ensure each student has adequate time with the tutor. // Michael Ajerman is an American representational painter based in London. He has exhibited his work nationally and internationally. He has taught in a wide variety of educational settings and levels. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio (Evenings)\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 June-6 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488801ACQGRSSPKGQJTSDRQCSGPHNHJHK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-25T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-08-06T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesday 25 February \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n7pm – 8pm, £20 // Join Judy for an Open Mic Poetry Night, where poets and poetry lovers can share their original works or favourite poems. Whether you'd like to perform or just listen, everyone is welcome to this relaxed, informal evening celebrating the beauty of poetry.  \\r\\n \\r\\nJudy Karbritz, together with Pattie Greenberg, is the co-founder of the JPS.  Judy is also Harrow’s Community Poet and for nine years has written Poetry Corner for the Harrow Times and Barnet Borough Times.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Mic Night with the Jewish Poetry Society \",\"instanceDates\":\"25 February-25 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"451601ACHHPMNTTDSRLSVCRTBVSKMLGQT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-25T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-25T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Judy Karbritz\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Parthenope, born in the sea of Naples in 1950, searches for happiness over the long summers of her youth, falling in love with her home city and its many memorable characters. From Academy Award-winning filmmaker Paolo Sorrentino comes a monumental and deeply romantic story of a lifetime. | This film is in Italian with English subtitles | Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 17m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":137,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e0550577-35ca-49b3-9199-9922bffb4ba3.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Parthenope\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e0550577-35ca-49b3-9199-9922bffb4ba3-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507201AJPPDCLQQBJBDGQTSHPLGLBGHKV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T14:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-14T14:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £10 adult, £12 child, under 2s free, in-building // Experience a spectacular Purim party featuring all your Purim faves. We'll have storytelling and puppets with Ilana Banana, grogger making with the Junk Orchestra, hamantaschen baking with Fabienne, sing-a-longs, face-painting, costumes, crafts and so much more. So put on your best costume and get ready to have some Party on Purim fun!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Party on Purim\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 March-16 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"469801ALJNKRGQKRVVHSPHCRKNCDCPNBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-16T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-16T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Purim\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"3pm-4pm, £5, in building // show is in Hebrew, ages 6-10 // no interval // Peter Pan - The Eternal Child is Tom's Hero! With the help of Tinkerbell, Tom fulfills his dream and becomes Peter Pan. \\r\\nIn \\\"Neverland,\\\" Tom learns to share and cooperate, understands the importance of setting a good example and taking responsibility, and learns the valuable lesson that it’s possible to grow up, move to a new place, and still make new friends. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Peter Pan: Tom's Super Hero\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"457001ASHGNJHJQSQBQTTGSPBPJTGQDMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T15:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"One of Nir Bergman's best films, this gripping drama unfolds in an ultra-Orthodox Jewish community in Jerusalem. Bati seems to have the perfect life with her husband Lazer and their three children, but everything unravels when Lazer is blackmailed and Bati discovers his secret affair with his male study partner. Desperate to protect her family, she supports Lazer as he attempts to \\\"cure\\\" his homosexuality, while also uncovering her own hidden desires. A powerful exploration of love, identity, and self-discovery. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | | Duration: 106 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b3069a57-42b4-4db1-8b77-1bec803d3e0a.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Pink Lady\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b3069a57-42b4-4db1-8b77-1bec803d3e0a-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502201AKMBVJQLCLHLQCQCGJKVMQDNKDD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This session ages 4-7 // 2.30pm - 4.30pm, £12 child £5 adult, in building // An illustration workshop with Israeli artist Inbal Leitner // This year marks the 10th anniversary of PJ Library in the UK! Exciting activities are planned for all ages: Meet the renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel, enjoy an art session with Israeli illustrator Inbal Leitner and little ones will have a blast with interactive live music with Ilana Banana. Before your chosen age-appropriate session, get creative with book-themed arts & crafts, and after, we’ll celebrate with a birthday disco party. Programme: 2:30pm Get creative with book-themed arts & crafts and take part in a book swap (bring any two pre-loved books in great condition and swap them at our book table). 3:00pm – book your session: • For ages 0-3: Live music fun – an engaging sensory session with Ilana Banana. • For ages 4-7: Let your creativity guide you – an illustration workshop with Israeli artist Inbal Leitner. • For ages 8+: Creating a character for your own story – a workshop with renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel. 4:00pm A mega party disco and help us wish PJ Library a happy 10th birthday! Your ticket covers the whole event, including all arts and crafts, your selected age-appropriate session and the disco finale.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"PJ Library Celebration: Illustration Workshop (Ages 4-7)\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 March-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"479201AQDRKRDHGGHTJLTLJGBNVDGBPJS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"PJ Library Celebration\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Inbal Leitner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This session ages 0-3 // 2.30pm - 4.30pm, £12 child £5 adult, in building //  An engaging sensory session with Ilana Banana // This year marks the 10th anniversary of PJ Library in the UK! \\r\\n \\r\\nExciting activities are planned for all ages: Meet the renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel, enjoy an art session with Israeli illustrator Inbal Leitner and little ones will have a blast with interactive live music with Ilana Banana.\\r\\n \\r\\nBefore your chosen age-appropriate session, get creative with book-themed arts & crafts, and after, we’ll celebrate with a birthday disco party. \\r\\n \\r\\nProgramme:\\r\\n2:30pm\\r\\nGet creative with book-themed arts & crafts and take part in a book swap (bring any two pre-loved books in great condition and swap them at our book table).\\r\\n \\r\\n3:00pm – book your session:\\r\\n• For ages 0-3: Live music fun – an engaging sensory session with Ilana Banana.\\r\\n• For ages 4-7: Let your creativity guide you – an illustration workshop with Israeli artist Inbal Leitner.\\r\\n• For ages 8+: Creating a character for your own story – a workshop with renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel.\\r\\n \\r\\n4:00pm \\r\\nA mega party disco and help us wish PJ Library a happy 10th birthday!\\r\\n \\r\\nYour ticket covers the whole event, including all arts and crafts, your selected age-appropriate session and the disco finale.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"PJ Library Celebration: Live Musical Fun (Ages 0-3)\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 March-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"479001ABKBNSJLHNVJQHDCQBJKPGDJRLD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"PJ Library Celebration\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ilana Banana\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This session ages 8+ // 2.30pm - 4.30pm, £12 child £5 adult, in building // A workshop with renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel // This year marks the 10th anniversary of PJ Library in the UK! Exciting activities are planned for all ages: Meet the renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel, enjoy an art session with Israeli illustrator Inbal Leitner and little ones will have a blast with interactive live music with Ilana Banana. Before your chosen age-appropriate session, get creative with book-themed arts & crafts, and after, we’ll celebrate with a birthday disco party. Programme: 2:30pm Get creative with book-themed arts & crafts and take part in a book swap (bring any two pre-loved books in great condition and swap them at our book table). 3:00pm – book your session: • For ages 0-3: Live music fun – an engaging sensory session with Ilana Banana. • For ages 4-7: Let your creativity guide you – an illustration workshop with Israeli artist Inbal Leitner. • For ages 8+: Creating a character for your own story – a workshop with renowned children's author Ivor Baddiel. 4:00pm A mega party disco and help us wish PJ Library a happy 10th birthday! Your ticket covers the whole event, including all arts and crafts, your selected age-appropriate session and the disco finale.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"PJ Library Celebration: Stories Workshop (Ages 8+)\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 March-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"479401ARNTJVBNHRCTQKBMVRLCLCKRKNH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"PJ Library Celebration\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ivor Baddiel\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30, in building, £45 // Tal Sunderland-Cohen is back at JW3 for another evening of education, anecdotes and amazing fine Kosher wines! In this episode: The best Kosher wines from around the world!\\r\\n\\r\\nKosher wine, once primarily associated with Israel, is now crafted in esteemed wine regions worldwide, including France, Spain, the United States, and Argentina. French kosher wines from Bordeaux and Burgundy offer elegance and complexity, while Italian varieties from Tuscany and Piedmont highlight the richness of native grapes like Sangiovese. In California, kosher wines reflect Napa Valley’s innovative spirit, rivalling some of the finest non-kosher wines. This global production, rooted in ancient practices, underscores the quality and evolving reputation of kosher wine, transforming it from a sacramental beverage to a gourmet delight.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou'll also be able to purchase wine on the night, so you're well-stocked for Purim\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Purim Wine Tasting Evening\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 March-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"458201ATSLSRMBTLNLNKPRLPKRCTGHGVT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Purim\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Tal Sunderland-Cohen\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30-9.30pm, £25 // Dust off your magic carpet and be transported to the enchanting land of Agrabah for an early Purim celebration with Young JW3.\\r\\n\\r\\nStart the festivities with a delicious Persian-inspired feast that will transport you to a world of exotic spices and rich traditions. After the meal, settle in for a screening of the beloved original Disney animated classic, Aladdin — complete with magic lamps, music and plenty of heart. It's the perfect way to kick off Purim 2025 and a fantastic chance to meet new people in a fun and relaxed setting.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Purim with Young JW3: A Night in Agrabah\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 March-12 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"478201AJQSLBCDGCRSBNGSSJVCCLTMGNT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-12T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"137 // 18 // In 1950s Mexico City, an American immigrant in his late forties leads a solitary life amidst a small American community. However, the arrival of a young student stirs the man into finally establishing a meaningful connection with someone.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":137,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Queer\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-9 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470601AJMGQVLPCQLDNQLQRGDDTHLJRCV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-05T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-09T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9pm, £20, in building // Unveiling the covert operation of \\\"The Voice of Israel in Arabic,\\\" a radio station established by Jewish immigrants from Arab countries, this film explores its transformation into a propaganda powerhouse.  \\r\\n \\r\\nOperating in the 1940s to 1960s, it covertly utilised propaganda, psychological warfare, and encoded messages to activate agents. Unveiling this enthralling narrative, it reveals the formidable threat it posed to Arab rulers and its lasting consequences.  \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a film screening followed by a discussion. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Radio Propaganda\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"454801APSJBLRQMMNGSCSBNBKNGJDMQLP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-15T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Invitation only // 7.30pm-8.45pm, free, in building // How Israelis, British and World Jewry Can Partner More Effectively For a Better Shared Future // A joint invitation-only event at JW3 in cooperation with The London Initiative (TLI).\\r\\n \\r\\nSir Mick Davis is a former chief executive of the UK Conservative Party, a former chairman of the UK Jewish Leadership Council and UJIA, and an international businessman and philanthropist.\\r\\n \\r\\nMike Prashker was founding director of Merchavim, The Institute for the Advancement of Shared Citizenship in Israel. Author of “A Place for Us All – Social Cohesion and the Future of Israel (2017), he advised The Ted Arison Family Foundation before moving on to lead the London Initative.\\r\\n \\r\\nDr. Jeffrey R. Solomon is Senior Advisor to Chasbro Investments, the family office of Charles Bronfman. For two decades, he was the President of the Andrea and Charles Bronfman Philanthropies, a group of foundations operating in Canada, Israel and the United States.  He is the author of over 150 academic publications.\\r\\n \\r\\nProfessor Dov Waxman is the Rosalinde and Arthur Gilbert Foundation Professor of Israel Studies at UCLA and author of four books: The Pursuit of Peace and The Crisis of Israeli Identity: Defending / Defining the Nation (2006), Israel’s Palestinians: The Conflict Within (2011), Trouble in the Tribe: The American Jewish Conflict over Israel (2016), and, The Israeli-Palestinian Conflict: What Everyone Needs to Know (2019).\\r\\n \\r\\nHanna Veiler is President of the German Union of Jewish Students, vice-president of the European Union of Jewish Students, a trainer in the ADL Words to Action program, Lauder Fellow at WJC and works as a political educator and publicist\\r\\n \\r\\nPnina Pfeuffer is a haredi feminist and human rights activist. CEO of Yad Levi Eshkol, Pnina founded “The New Haredim”, a grassroots network of over 70 Haredi community organizers, activists, and leaders, to strengthen democratic and progressive values.\\r\\n \\r\\nShaira Shalaby is the Co-Executive Director of The Abraham Initiatives, a joint Jewish-Israeli and Palestinian-Israeli organization that promotes social inclusion and equal rights for Palestinian citizens of Israel. She previously served as Deputy Mayor of Haifa and as a city councilor. Shahira has spearheaded several initiatives aimed at improving the status of Arab women and advancing the social rights of Palestinian citizens of Israel.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Re-Committing to The Declaration of Independence\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 February-13 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"467201AKGRLKMDGRMBKNTHQMSSSTSTTMH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-13T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-13T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £20 // Includes an interval // RISE is a new rock musical about a group of Jewish women resistance fighters during the Holocaust who wage an uprising against the Nazi regime. Enjoy a special concert performance of the show that Broadway World calls \\\"a daring and important new musical\\\" with a \\\"superb score.\\\" Followed by a discussion with the writer/composer. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"RISE\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"468801ALQLHHJHBRBNJKCKVGSMTPMSCDQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am - 1pm, £20, off site // Meeting location provided upon booking // Walk in and around Westminster and follow in the footsteps of British monarchs (and a republican), past and present as Rachel uncovers the many and varied  the Jewish community has had with the Royal family.  \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom churches, palaces and parks, you’ll discover some background to 'the Firm', royal personalities and at the same time uncover Jewish associations through friendships, the arts, heritage and honours bestowed. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking. \\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Royal Connections\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 June-19 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492601AKSDBRQRJQTVDMLTLSDQJNMJPSS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-19T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-19T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £20 // Sabra Swing explore the world of Jews in Jazz, their influence on the Great American Songbook and the soundtrack of the silver screen. With music by Irving Berlin, George Gershwin, Johnny Mandel, Sholom Secunda, Carole King and many more. // The New York Times described the band as “soulful and virtuosic”, and their heartfelt, fiery performances make them an audience favourite. Featuring Miriam Kramer - “a violinist of superior natural talent” (The Strad), singer Sara Feldmann Brummer - “sensuous and impertinently hilarious vocals\\\" (This Is Cabaret) and pianist Nicholas Durcan, whose Rhapsody in Blue (Gershwin) was praised as \\\"a sparkling performance\\\" by The Observer.  Bassist Nick Haward and drummer Hamish Birchall complete the sound. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sabra Swing\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 April-3 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"469001ADKJLKLCQHLVRKMJMHQTQCSVBTT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-03T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm-9pm, £20, in building // 12+ // Join us for a live sculpting session by internationally renowned sculptor Frances Segelman as she will be creating a sculpture of Holocaust survivor Harry Olmer MBE in front of an audience.  \\r\\n\\r\\nYad Vashem UK works closely with Frances Segelman producing Holocaust survivor sculptures. This will be the 8th sculpting she has done in a series for Yad Vashem UK. \\r\\n\\r\\nA wonderful opportunity to see Frances Segelman in action, find out more about the process of creating a sculpture as well as meeting Holocaust survivor Harry Olmer and be part of this special occasion. \\r\\n\\r\\nFrances will start sculpting from 6 pm onwards, with a break at 7pm, before resuming at 7:30 pm. There will be a Q&A at 8:15pm.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome light refreshments will be provided.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sculpting Lives: An Evening with Frances Segelman and Harry Olmer MBE\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-13 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"437201AGRLDSLPVJMPLPVRCQKRBSQVPTR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £5, in building // In Hebrew, ages 11+ // no interval // When Abraham Orbach, a dedicated Palmach fighter, decides decides to refuse an order and faces being expelled from the battalion, he has no choice but to reveal his great secret to his commander. With all the cards on the table, his fascinating story of survival, where all he wanted was to live life itself, comes to light. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe play is based on the real-life personal story of Avraham Aurbach. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sentenced to Life: The Story of Abraham Orbach\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"457401AHBJVNPLCTTNHVCBRNQVGVKMLKD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Set during the 1972 Munich Summer Olympics, the film follows an American Sports broadcasting team that quickly adapted from sports reporting to live coverage of the Israeli athletes taken hostage. Through this lens, \\\"September 5\\\" provides a fresh perspective on the live broadcast seen globally by an estimated one billion people at the time. At the heart of the story is Geoff (John Magaro), a young and ambitious producer striving to prove himself to his boss, the legendary TV executive Roone Arledge (Peter Sarsgaard). Together with German interpreter Marianne (Leonie Benesch) and his mentor Marvin Bader (Ben Chaplin), Geoff unexpectedly takes the helm of the live coverage. As narratives shift, time ticks away, and conflicting rumors spread, with the hostages' lives hanging in the balance, Geoff grapples with tough decisions while confronting his own moral compass.\\r\\nRated: 15 | 1 hour 35 minutes\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e138d5c2-76a9-438d-9200-fed9c59e22cb.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"September 5\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 February-27 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/e138d5c2-76a9-438d-9200-fed9c59e22cb-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"474601AHNSBDSSGTQSNCMTVNSGGQRHVHR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-16T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-27T17:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building only, £20 // When we think about retirement, our planning mostly focuses on money. This is important, but what about the rest? What will your purpose be? How will you maintain connections? How will you spend all your time?  \\r\\n \\r\\nAs with any big life change, retirement comes with a lot of emotions and questions. We can’t control everything, but in making time to think about what it may involve, you can take steps to prepare for the life that you want and anticipate challenges.\\r\\n \\r\\nIn this interactive workshop you will: \\r\\n\\r\\nSet your vision for Year 1 of retirement\\r\\nIdentify your dreams & concerns\\r\\nExplore your attitudes towards purpose, connection and time\\r\\nConsider cost implications for retirement\\r\\nCreate an action plan\\r\\n\\r\\nDani Serlin is a Retirement Readiness Coach and Founder of Second Spring, providing coaching support to people approaching retirement to focus their vision, create a plan, and take action. She is an ICF accredited coach with over 20 years of global experience in project, programme and people management.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Set Your Foundations for Retirement Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"427601AMDTDHCSPKTNCGHMSGQMJRQDDQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-15T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dani Serlin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.15pm, £20, building only // Join us for a celebration of Jack Nicholson, with a film season paying tribute to Hollywood royalty. Hear from Dr Julie Lobalzo Wright for a talk examining his extraordinary career. Plus, catch some of his most popular films on the big screen.    \\r\\n\\r\\nAn actor, director, writer and producer, Nicholson is widely liked for his wicked personality (and devilish smile). His career-making roles include Five Easy Pieces, Chinatown, The Shining and his Oscar-winning performance in One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest.\\r\\n\\r\\nJulie is an Assistant Professor in Film and Television Studies at the University of Warwick. She has taught and researched film and television stardom for many years, giving talks on a variety of stars.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shining Star: Jack Nicholson\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 March-20 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"454001ADLLGNSMJCTVPDHTTQCQTRRCPNL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dr Julie Lobalzo Wright\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.45pm, £20, in building // The Road to Auschwitz contains disturbing images which viewers may find distressing. Please use your discretion when booking. // In this year marking 80 years since the liberation of the last concentration camps, renowned historian Sir Simon Schama has made an extraordinary new documentary film for the BBC. \\r\\nIn this exclusive event for JW3, Simon, in conversation with the film's director, Hugo MacGregor, will examine how the Holocaust has been portrayed on screen since the war’s end and reflects on what its legacy means today. They will also introduce a special preview screening of the documentary, followed by a Q&A.\\r\\n \\r\\nThe Road to Auschwitz is most personal and unflinching film of Simon Schama's career, in which he confronts the enormity of the Holocaust as not just a Nazi obsession, but as a European-wide crime of complicity. In a journey that ends with his first visit to Auschwitz, Simon travels to mass killing sites in Lithuania - the home of his mother’s family - and to the Netherlands - a nation famed for its long history of tolerance - to reveal how across the continent deep-rooted prejudice was weaponised to turn people against their Jewish neighbours.\\r\\n \\r\\nSimon was born two weeks after the liberation of Auschwitz - it’s been with him all his life, but until now he’s never actually been there. He has dedicated much of his career to documenting Jewish history, but has been committed to telling the story of life, not death. In a profoundly emotional first ever visit to Auschwitz, the film follows Simon as he finally confronts the ‘monster’ and comes face to face with the horrifying reality of what happened there.  \\r\\nAt every step Simon uncovers extraordinary evidence of the resilience of the Jewish people and recounts remarkable acts of resistance, above all the compulsion of Jewish \\\"keepers of memory\\\" to document the unprecedented atrocities that were happening to them, in the hope they could never be denied or repeated.\\r\\nAnd, as a moving interview with 98-year-old survivor Marian Turski reveals, ‘evil comes step-by-step’ - a statement that remains powerfully relevant today. With hatred once again on the rise and the last survivors passing on, this film is a powerful testament to the importance of preserving the truth and ensuring that the full enormity of the Holocaust is never forgotten.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Simon Schama: The Road To Auschwitz\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-2 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499002ADSCKMTNSDGSRCSDHRCRDRVDGHL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Simon Schama\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-3.30pm, £20, hybrid // Sinatra had a hugely successful film career even winning an Oscar  as well as being a recording artist and appeared in over 40 movies. \\r\\nLet’s look at him in action in Anchors Aweigh, From Here to Eternity, Pal Joey , Von  Ryan’s Express and many others and trace his life story. \\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge has worked in the media for over 35 years, latterly at the BBC where he was responsible for all feature films and non-UK TV series.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sinatra at the Movies\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 June-9 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491801APLCGKGRVJTHRQJKSVTNNSVKRNN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-09T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-09T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building //Mozart was the first composer to realise the great potential of adding an extra viola to the string quartet, and his exceptionally expressive quintet in g minor is a major masterpiece which resounds through the centuries.  Brahms also enjoys the extra sonorities offered by the medium and his quintet is full of sunlit vitality and warmth.  Bruckner wrote very little chamber music apart from a viola quintet and this Adagio movement at its centre is sublime beyond words.  The programme opens with a wonderful little-known rarity from late Beethoven. // This group includes the inspirational and poetic violinists Simonen and Ruisi, and the superb, richly gifted violists Larivière and Tunnicliffe. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sini Simonen, Alessandro Ruisi, Sào Soulez Larivière, Luba Tunnicliffe, and David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 March-4 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"494001AJQGVDBQQRGTJSJQRSTMCLKVMVV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"5.30pm, £30 adult £15 student, in-building // Schubert Sonatina in D major, D. 384 - approx 12 mins // Schumann Piano trio no. 1 in D minor, op. 63 - approx 30 mins // Interval - 20 minutes, approximately 6:30pm // Dvořák  Piano Quartet no. 2 in E flat major, op. 87 - approx 35 mins //\\r\\n\\r\\nSini Simonen (the inspiring first violin of the Castalian Quartet) and Alasdair Beatson (the superb pianist of the Nash Ensemble) make a welcome return after entrancing JW3 audiences last season with their marvellously gripping and very expressive playing. Garfield Jackson and David Waterman team up again after their 42 years in the world-renowned Endellion Quartet and their concert for JW3 in November.     \\r\\n\\r\\nSchubert’s early Sonatina is graceful, amiable and touching. In contrast, Schumann’s D minor trio ranges from the turbulent, anguished and introspective to the outgoing and joyful. It is one of his very greatest instrumental pieces. Dvořák’s rare gift for Slav-flavoured melody and drama is exemplified in his unusually attractive second piano quartet. It is a favourite amongst players and audience alike.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sini Simonen, Garfield Jackson, David Waterman, and Alasdair Beatson \",\"instanceDates\":\"2 February-2 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"398001ARNGQSSPTMVHKLVRMPHPBMNSDDG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-02T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-02T17:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"In Sister Midnight, the audacious debut feature from London based Indian artist and filmmaker Karan Kandhari, rebellious small-town misfit Uma arrives in Mumbai to find herself totally unsuited to life as a housewife. At odds with her prying neighbors and under the constant oppressive noise and heat of the city, she decides to break free from the shackles of domesticity and follow her own path in this bold, unpredictable, and darkly funny debut. Featuring an eclectic soundtrack and singular visual aesthetic, the film world-premiered in Cannes’ Directors Fortnight and won the award for Best Film in the Next Wave section at Fantastic Fest. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Film is in Hindi and English with English subtitles \\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 47m  \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":107,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6446b9a0-7c08-4f84-b71b-62a421428376.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sister Midnight\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-30 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6446b9a0-7c08-4f84-b71b-62a421428376-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499001ARJMNSKCDGTBHRQMJKKLMBNQSLG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-27T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-30T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, building, £20, age 18+ // This new film is based on the true story of Ziko, a nine-year-old orphan from Salonica.  \\r\\nZiko joins a group of Greek Jews from Volos sheltering on the Pelion mountain. During WWII they were saved from being sent to the death camps  by their Christian neighbours and the Communist underground. A Nazi SS Unit intent on deporting the Jews to Auschwitz arrives to set up their headquarters. They demand to be billeted with the group.  The film will be followed by a Q&A with the director, Rami Kimchi.  An author, cultural critic and award-winning film-maker, Rami Kimchi is a professor at Ariel University. His film, Night of Fools, about the Algerian-Jewish underground in in 1942, was shown at JW3 in 2017.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sleeping with the SS: Screening and Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 June-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"486201AVKQQVSKDMRRCGTCVBKTSRVSLPQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-30T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-30T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A live-action musical reimagining of the classic 1937 film. Starring Rachel Zegler in the title role and Gal Gadot as her Stepmother, the Evil Queen, the magical music adventure journeys back to the timeless story with beloved characters Bashful, Doc, Dopey, Grumpy, Happy, Sleepy, and Sneezy. | Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 49m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":109,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/efdd7d66-10e7-471e-9e81-690ea081697d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Snow White\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/efdd7d66-10e7-471e-9e81-690ea081697d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506203AGQCRBVLTPSJLSSJPLQGSTPGVJG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-25T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Starring Lior Raz (Fauda) and Rotem Sela, this gripping drama is set in 1956, when a beautiful seamstress moves into a tight-knit neighborhood of Holocaust survivors. Whispers about her mysterious past as a Capo stir unrest, especially for Shalom, the community’s respected leader and former resistance fighter. Torn between his growing passion for the woman and his duty to uncover the truth of her past, Shalom faces an emotional battle that could unravel everything. A compelling tale of love, loyalty, and moral conflict. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 96 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":96,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9a5e3230-0fb6-459b-9f94-9a96f6eae1a0.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Soda + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9a5e3230-0fb6-459b-9f94-9a96f6eae1a0-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"501401ABNSNVBMGJNMBSPDDKVPDJCGNKV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"124 // PG// During her family's move to the suburbs, a sullen 10-year-old girl wanders into a world ruled by gods, witches and spirits, and where humans are changed into beasts.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Spirited Away\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-9 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470401ALTDQRKMPJKPCJBTRBTSQSRPQQT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-05T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-09T17:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"3-5pm, £20, off site // meeting location provided upon booking // Stroll with us through the Spitalfields area adjacent to the venerable City of London, where magnificent Georgian houses line the side streets of an historic (now trendy and multi-cultural) neighbourhood.  \\r\\n\\r\\nOur walk will start in Aldgate at the site of the 2000-year old Roman Wall that defined the original settlement of Londinium, take us past Bevis Marks, London's oldest functioning synagogue opened in 1701, through famous streets such as Petticoat Lane and Brick Lane, and end at Spitalfields - a former Victorian covered market that is now famous for food, fashion, and art.   \\r\\n\\r\\nHear about immigrant communities over the centuries that found refuge and work nearby, including French Protestant silk weavers, East European Jewish tailors, and Bangladeshi Muslim restauranteurs. \\r\\n\\r\\nSee historic streets where Yiddish was once the common language, later to be replaced by Bengali. Hear about the vibrant Jewish community that dominated the area in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, and learn about 1000 years of Jewish history in Britain.  \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us to celebrate London's cultural diversity in the heart of this great city! \\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking. \\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Spitalfields: The Historic Jewish East End of London \",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-20 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492401ALPRVCKJRHQJPPRLHJBPBGJTDRT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-20T15:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm–8.30pm, £17.50, building // Join us for a powerful and thought-provoking event marking the 80th anniversary of VE Day and the end of World War II in Europe.  // Stories of Liberation weaves together eyewitness testimony, voices of descendants, creative explorations and historical context to reflect on the closing chapter of the war and its aftermath, including the horrors uncovered at Bergen-Belsen and other concentration camps.  // Through the stories of survivors, liberators and those who provided vital relief, we will explore the complexities of liberation, where hope and unimaginable loss existed side by side.  // While acknowledging that freedom did not mean an immediate happy ending, we will reflect on the resilience, courage and determination of those who survived, bore witness and rebuilt their lives.   // The evening will include a short performance of A Hell on Earth by Time Will Tell Theatre, a powerful reenactment of first-hand accounts from the liberation of Bergen-Belsen.   \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Stories of Liberation: Resilience, Relief and Remembrance\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 May-6 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"490001ARBJPHKNDKLHCCHVGVKJCBMGRPK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-06T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-06T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"This is a venue hire, customers should visit mirimusic.com to book // At the Miriam School of Music, your child can learn, sing, and grow — with inspiring Jewish and secular music taught by conservatoire-trained professionals.\\r\\nLed by Itamar Rashkovsky, violinist at the Royal Welsh College of Music and the Junior Guildhall School of Music\\r\\nEvery teacher is conservatoire-trained — excellence you can trust.\\r\\n•\\tBuild musicianship skills with fun, interactive games\\r\\n•\\tSing Jewish songs in choir \\r\\n•\\tKids of all ages and musical backgrounds welcome!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Summer Music School\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 June-29 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503801AMDLBQCMKGKSGVBRBTRHLKMJGGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-15T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-29T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Venue Hire\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9.15pm, £15, in building // film screening and q&a with creator Zoom Rockman //\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Survivor\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 January-28 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"466402AHDJKGJPMVHPJDQQRSGMBNRQCBN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-28T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-28T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Zoom Rockman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Survivor follows the experience of 12-year-old Ivor during the Holocaust. When the Nazis invade his village in Hungary, Ivor is separated from his family and sent to Auschwitz, where he lies about his age to survive. After he and his brother endure the relentless horrors of the camp, they are sent on a death march, which they narrowly escaping. With his family gone, Ivor tries to carve out a new life in post-war Germany. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":40,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9717cf5b-27a4-4de9-ac44-41dfc6eb60f9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Survivor \",\"instanceDates\":\"6 February-17 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9717cf5b-27a4-4de9-ac44-41dfc6eb60f9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"474801AMVNTSDGMDNQRLTJLNBPVSKMJQH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-06T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-17T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Venue hire, customers do not book via JW3 // 9.30am-10.30am // Immerse yourself in the seamless movements of Tai Chi. This ancient Chinese art enhances flexibility, coordination, strength, agility, and balance. Explore Qingong with Qi (energy) and breathwork, fostering mental clarity and stress reductions. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Tai Chi and Qigong \",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-2 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"474201ABPPJCQSHPHBRQNGNTTLDDHHBHL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-15T09:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T09:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £16, in building // TamaRadah is an extraordinary Ethiopian folk singer, captivating audiences with her fusion of African-Caribbean grooves and the rich heritage of Ethiopian music.  \\r\\n\\r\\nAmidst the constellation of iconic names in the music scene, Tamar Radah shines as a trailblazing artist carving her own path to stardom. At 35 years old, she is not only an independent music creator but also a promising talent hailing from the esteemed \\\"Rimon\\\" music academy.   \\r\\n\\r\\nAs the lead singer of her band, TamaRadah, she shares stages with living music legends. Over the years, Tamar has impressively written, composed, and produced three albums, collaborating with some of the finest musicians, including Ehud Banai, Ariel Horowitz, Idan Reichel, Ester Rada, and Doron Talmon (Jane Bordeaux). \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"TamaRadah\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 July-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"491201AHLCBPJQJKJSMTKMCVGGBDHVJJD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"TamaRadah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building, £20 // Food will contain nuts // Enjoy a virtual Israel tour in our cinema of the three-day hike from the Mediterranean Sea to the Sea of Galilee with special surprises! What normally takes three days of difficult hiking across the country, you’ll do in an hour with a glass of Israeli wine and fun music! Hiking in the small but diverse landscape of Israel is a true Israeli cultural experience. The trek will be your backdrop for exploring sites, both ancient and modern, which had a lasting impact on the local areas of the north and the rest of the country. Josh has been a licensed Israeli tour guide since 2017. He uses stories, explanations and music to help you feel a deep connection with Israel. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Taste Israel: Immersive Virtual Tour\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-5 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487202ALCMGHRLRQHVDJHVTCMHDTSTMMN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Israel & the Middle East\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Josh Hartuv \",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Widow Aurora Greenway (Shirley MacLaine) and her daughter, Emma (Debra Winger), have a strong bond, but Emma marries teacher Flap Horton (Jeff Daniels) against her mother's wishes. When the marriage grows sour due to Flap's cheating, Emma eventually splits from him, returning to her mother, who is involved with a former astronaut (Jack Nicholson). Soon, Emma learns that she has terminal cancer. In the hospital, supported by Aurora, she tries to make peace with Flap and her children. | Rating: 12A, Duration: 2h 12m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":132,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1dcd001b-0f45-4ad3-8f6c-777b2bde173d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Terms of Endearment\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 March-27 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1dcd001b-0f45-4ad3-8f6c-777b2bde173d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"482201ACLPLTDDQMDPCLPKMPBPPHQBLCJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-25T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-27T16:10:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Jack Nicholson Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Test Event\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Test Event\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-2 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"504201ADCKKKGTRNCRPNMDGNPGMDLKHJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Join us for a special retrospective honoring Director Erez Tadmor, featuring the powerful film The Art of Waiting. Follow Liran and Tali, a couple in their thirties with hopes of starting a family. What begins as a straightforward dream quickly evolves into a journey filled with unexpected challenges when they are faced with the reality of fertility treatments.\\r\\nAn intimate and thought-provoking story that beautifully explores the complexities of love, hope, and the path to parenthood. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 90 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a8856f9a-9038-47b0-8ce1-6f629b3086d3.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Art of Waiting + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 May-9 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a8856f9a-9038-47b0-8ce1-6f629b3086d3-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"501801AHJVTGSJJKDNBVNTQGCDPPHHGLL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-09T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-09T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"An inside look into the corruption charges against Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu through leaked police interrogation videos.\\r\\n// Rating: 15, Duration: 113 Minutes // Preceded by 10-15 minutes of ads/trailers // Screening on 2 March to include a 30-min live Q&A with Alexis Bloom // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":113,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/bf06afd4-ba8d-417c-b384-3cd7e42add1d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Bibi Files\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 January-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/bf06afd4-ba8d-417c-b384-3cd7e42add1d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470001ATVGCLSNBBKGDVJJSTVGMQTJPRK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-03T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-02T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Jeff Bridges plays Jeff Lebowski who insists on being called \\\"the Dude,\\\" a laid-back, easygoing burnout who happens to have the same name as a millionaire whose wife owes a lot of dangerous people a whole bunch of money -- resulting in the Dude having his rug soiled, sending him spiraling into the Los Angeles underworld. | Rating: 18, Duration: 1h 57m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":117,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b041dd2a-8a58-47c1-9f9b-eac2ef757f63.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Big Lebowski\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b041dd2a-8a58-47c1-9f9b-eac2ef757f63-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480801AGNDRBJLVNJKPLVJLLQMKQLSKVG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-16T17:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Join author Peter Lantos to hear about his newest book, The Boy Who Didn’t Want to Die: The Graphic Memoir. It describes an extraordinary journey, made by Peter, a boy of five, through war-torn Europe in 1944 and 1945. Peter and his parents were deported from a small Hungarian town to Bergen-Belsen. Along the way, unforgettable images flash one after another: sleeping in a tent and then under the sky, discovering a disused brick factory, catching butterflies in the meadows, but the adventure gradually turns into nightmare of starvation, freezing cold, disease and death. Peter's father dies in the concentration camp, while he and his mother survive. \\r\\n \\r\\nOriginally published as a biography for children in 2023, The Boy Who Didn’t Want to Die was the Times Children’s Book of the Week, won the UK Literacy Association's Non-Fiction Book of the Year, shortlisted for the British Book Awards Children’s Non-Fiction Book of the Year, and reviewed to great acclaim.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPeter will be speaking about his experiences of the Holocaust that formed the basis of his books, and talk about the experience of seeing his story turned into a graphic novel.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPeter Lantos will be in conversation with Angela Gluck who has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She is the author of over 40 books on aspects of religion and history, and broadcasts on these subjects. She devotes part of her work to teaching children, young people and adults in cross-communal settings. She is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Boy Who Didn't Want to Die\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-3 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"457601ACPVLNNKRDLPTHLHTNSGKPRNSKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-03T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Peter Lantos\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Escaping post-war Europe, visionary architect László Toth arrives in America to rebuild his life, his work, and his marriage to his wife Erzsébet after being forced apart during wartime by shifting borders and regimes. On his own in a strange new country, László settles in Pennsylvania, where the wealthy and prominent industrialist Harrison Lee Van Buren recognizes his talent for building. But power and legacy come at a heavy cost.... \\r\\nRated: 18 | 3 hours 35 minutes including a 15 minute interval.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":215,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1aaebfa2-cf01-4ffe-af5c-c0286ae99690.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Brutalist\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 February-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/1aaebfa2-cf01-4ffe-af5c-c0286ae99690-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"474401ADNLLJGVHVMSJNJQQHVDGHTSMNH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-02T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T13:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-9.15pm, £17.50, building, film screening + Q&A // To mark Holocaust Memorial Day and the 80th anniversary of the liberation of Auschwitz, join us for a special screening of The Commandant's Shadow, a remarkable documentary following Hans Jürgen Höss, son of Auschwitz Commandant Rudolf Höss, as he confronts his father's legacy for the first time. Featuring a historic meeting with Holocaust survivor Anita Lasker-Wallfisch and her daughter Maya, their families come together to explore themes of loss, guilt, trauma, and reconciliation. Returning by popular demand, this powerful film delves into the lasting impact of Auschwitz on the descendants of both the perpetrators and survivors. The screening will be followed by an exclusive Q&A with the film director, Daniela Völker and Maya Lasker-Wallfisch. This event is in partnership with the AJR, the largest community of Holocaust descendants in the UK. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Commandant's Shadow\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 January-16 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472601APQKRSSHNGDCSJMSDDVVJRGCPQQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-16T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesday 2 April \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n2pm – 3.30pm // £20, also available online // \\r\\nIn 1927, Al Jolson revolutionised the movies by talking and singing. Silent films were dead and Hollywood now dramatically rose to the challenges of sound cinema. George looks at some extremely rare moments from the early talkies. \\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has worked in the media for over 35 years, latterly at the BBC where he was responsible for all feature films and non-UK TV series.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Dawn of Sound  \",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-2 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452001AVLNRPPGRDBHGDNJCGKBGRQCCKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee \",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Writer and teacher Iris finds her comfortable, solitary New York life thrown into disarray after her closest friend and mentor dies suddenly and bequeaths her his beloved 150 lb. Great Dane. The regal yet intractable beast, named Apollo, immediately creates practical problems for Iris, from furniture destruction to eviction notices, as well as more existential ones, his looming presence constantly reminding her of her friend's problematic choices in both life and death. Yet as Iris finds herself unexpectedly bonding with the animal, she begins to come to terms with her past, her lost friend, and her own creative inner life. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 59m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":119,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/17499bc7-8b76-4cd0-b368-f9a613da78bd.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Friend\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 May-22 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/17499bc7-8b76-4cd0-b368-f9a613da78bd-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507401ADCLMNMMPSCCCGRJRNQPMQSGMRB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"123 // 15// Copenhagen 1919: A young worker finds herself unemployed and pregnant. She meets Dagmar, who runs an underground adoption agency. A strong connection grows but her world shatters when she stumbles on the shocking truth behind her work.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":123,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Girl with a Needle\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-30 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471603AJLQMSHNBLVGMMDNNGRMQNBSVJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T20:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-30T15:50:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The Jewish Outsider Trilogy - comprising Invisible City (1991), East Endings (1993), and Jewish Item (1996) - explores Jewish identity, exile, and memory through bold, independent filmmaking. Now newly restored and acquired by the BFI, this is the first time all 3 films will be screened together. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn 1991, Mark Jay was commissioned by BFI and Channel 4 to create Invisible City, a sci-fi parable reimagining an exiled Russian cinema of the 1970s. The film tells the story of two Jewish escapees from Eastern Europe in 1938 who find themselves in the ruins of a future city where language and memory have been erased.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhile making this film at the BFI, Jay worked alongside groups of Black and Asian filmmakers who were actively exploring identity, representation, and diaspora. He noticed that similar work from within the Jewish filmmaking community was less visible, often created in isolation. This realization led him to seek out Jewish artists and filmmakers working outside the mainstream—outsiders in their own right.\\r\\n\\r\\nA loose collective was formed, and in collaboration with this group, Jay produced two further films exploring Jewish identity, both past and present: East Endings (1993) and Jewish Item (1996). These films have been screened at international festivals and community events, with Invisible City also receiving two Channel 4 broadcasts. More recently, East Endings has enjoyed a revival, selling out four director Q&A screenings last year.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing this renewed interest, the BFI has now acquired all three films for its Mediatheque at BFI Southbank, in association with the UK Jewish Film Festival, with plans to make them available on BFI Player. Jay is deeply honored to present The Jewish Outsider Trilogy at JW3—the first time these three films will be screened together as an interconnected body of work, contextualized within the heart of the community in a vibrant, inclusive space that celebrates Jewish history and values. | Duration: 103 minutes\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":103,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b94769d1-b95d-4050-8c5c-6feabeafffe6.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jewish Outsider Trilogy\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 April-10 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b94769d1-b95d-4050-8c5c-6feabeafffe6-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"501001AQSCSPLTTNLCQDRQNSLNLPHVNRQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-06T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-10T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Mark Jay\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.15pm-9pm, £17.50, in building // 13+ // Includes a pre-event reception with light refreshments from 6.15pm-6.45pm. // Join us for the launch of The Jewish Revolt, Rachel Auerbach’s searing eyewitness account of the Warsaw Ghetto Uprising, now available in English for the first time.  \\r\\n\\r\\nAuerbach’s vivid narrative captures both the defiance and despair of a community fighting for survival during the Nazi’s final assault on Passover 1943.   \\r\\n\\r\\nThis powerful edition includes rare photographs, the striking photo essay Yellow Star, and Auerbach’s haunting reflections “Yisker” and “A Grave Marker”. New technology has helped identify faces in these images, restoring names to history. The evening will feature Rachel Riley and other guest speakers.  \\r\\n\\r\\nIncludes a pre-event reception with light refreshments.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":165,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jewish Revolt: A Warsaw Ghetto Exhibition\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-23 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492801ARCJMTPBBSLMMJQJGPNLJGKNLMJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-23T18:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-23T18:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Literature\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £20, in building // The running time is approximately 1 hour, followed by a 45 minute talk back session and chance to explore the artwork up close. // Actor, writer and knitter Kirk Dunn presents his multidisciplinary one-man show, The Knitting Pilgrim, featuring the Stitched Glass tapestries.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe show, which theatre critic Lynn Slotkin called “a stunning piece of theatre… glorious and so moving” combines personal storytelling, image projection and three huge knitted panels, designed in the style of stained-glass windows, that look at the commonalities and conflicts of the Abrahamic Faiths: Judaism, Christianity, and Islam.   \\r\\n\\r\\nIt recounts Kirk’s 15-year artistic and spiritual journey handknitting the ambitious project, and looks at why the faiths struggle to get along today, the meaning of art, the challenge of grant-writing and the power of love to overcome major obstacles (and minor mishaps).  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe show premiered at the Aga Khan Museum in 2019, and has been performed to acclaim almost 100 times in Canada, Austria, Germany and the United States. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Knitting Pilgrim\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488201AKTQLBBGHTRVDGKDRRJNSRGJVVH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"How can there be music in the worst place in the world? The Last Musician of Auschwitz reveals how music became a lifeline and form of resistance amid the Holocaust's horrors. At its center is 99-year-old cellist Anita Lasker-Wallfisch, the last living survivor from the camp orchestras, whose testimony frames this powerful documentary. The film examines the SS's perverse relationship with music—forcing prisoners to perform for their entertainment and accompany slave labourers, turning art into another form of torture. It also celebrates three other remarkable musicians—Ilse Weber, Szymon Laks, and Adam Kopyciński—whose compositions are brought to life in moving performances by contemporary artists, including Anita's son Raphael Wallfisch. Filmed in locations surrounding Auschwitz, these deeply emotional performances explore themes of loss, memory, and resilience. Through this innovative approach, the documentary illuminates music's extraordinary power to preserve humanity in its darkest hour - offering not just testimony to suffering, but a profound spark of hope and defiance that continues to resonate today. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 30m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":137,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/72d436e5-f0f9-46cb-a8db-c488780369bf.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Last Musician of Auschwitz\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 May-22 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/72d436e5-f0f9-46cb-a8db-c488780369bf-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506002ATDPPHPGKJSTQDJBJCCVMLGVCTG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-19T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-22T14:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9.30pm, £16 // Screening & discussion with musical performance tbc //  \\r\\nHow can there be music in the worst place in the world? The Last Musician of Auschwitz reveals how music became a lifeline and form of resistance amid the Holocaust's horrors. At its center is 99-year-old cellist Anita Lasker-Wallfisch, the last living survivor from the camp orchestras, whose testimony frames this powerful documentary.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe film examines the SS's perverse relationship with music—forcing prisoners to perform for their entertainment and accompany slave labourers, turning art into another form of torture. It also celebrates three other remarkable musicians—Ilse Weber, Szymon Laks, and Adam Kopyciński—whose compositions are brought to life in moving performances by contemporary artists, including Anita's son Raphael Wallfisch.\\r\\n\\r\\nFilmed in locations surrounding Auschwitz, these deeply emotional performances explore themes of loss, memory, and resilience. Through this innovative approach, the documentary illuminates music's extraordinary power to preserve humanity in its darkest hour - offering not just testimony to suffering, but a profound spark of hope and defiance that continues to resonate today.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Last Musician of Auschwitz + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"505801AKKCJLDQKJDHPTMHBVDPSPNQQHD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When the glittering Las Vegas revue she has headlined for decades announces it will soon close, glamorous showgirl Shelly (Pamela Anderson) must reconcile with the decisions she’s made and the life she has built as she plans her next act whilst also striving to repair the relationship with her daughter (Billie Lourd). With an outstanding ensemble cast that includes Jamie Lee Curtis, Dave Bautista, Brenda Song and Kiernan Shipka, The Last Showgirl is a joyous tribute to a long-gone Las Vegas – and all the women who made it glitter. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 28m | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of ads/trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":88,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b8330e27-94ab-43e5-8589-0a3720cb0872.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Last Showgirl \",\"instanceDates\":\"16 March-20 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/b8330e27-94ab-43e5-8589-0a3720cb0872-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"481002AJQPHHQVGRHCLGDDMDVHJRSKLNP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-16T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T20:10:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-12pm, £5, in building // In Hebrew, suitable for ages 3-7 // no interval // \\r\\nIt's Eric the Lion King's birthday, and Eric is angry and dissatisfied. Despite his close friends trying to help him and warn him about hunters, Eric dismisses them, saying, I don't need any help; I'm the strongest and the biggest—I can do anything!\\\" Eric will learn the hard way how to treat his friends and will be surprised to discover that help can come in different forms, not just through strength, but also through wisdom. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"456801AGGTKCJGRDNPMCLSHNJJKPKMRLC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thibaut is an internationally renowned conductor who travels the world. When he learns he was adopted, he discovers the existence of a younger brother, Jimmy, who works in a school cafeteria and plays the trombone in a small marching band. Everything seems to set them apart, except their love of music. Sensing his brother's exceptional talent, Thibaut decides to remedy the injustice of fate. Jimmy begins to dream of a different life. | Film is in French with English subtitles | Rating 15, Duration: 1h 43m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":103,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/0535c658-1ae6-4f64-a378-302949ecd184.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Marching Band\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/0535c658-1ae6-4f64-a378-302949ecd184-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507202AQVTQPLNJPPGRGBRGNGKPKBJMQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-25T16:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T15:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Once upon a time, a poor woodcutter and his wife lived in a great forest. Cold, hunger, poverty and a war raging all around them meant their lives were very hard. One day, the woodcutter's wife rescues a baby. A baby girl thrown from one of the many trains that constantly pass through the forest. This baby, this \\\"most precious of cargoes\\\", will transform the lives of the poor woodcutter's wife and her husband, as well as those whose paths the child will cross - including the man who threw her from the train. And some will try to protect her, whatever the cost. Their story will reveal the worst and the best in the hearts of men. \\r\\n\\r\\n| This film is in French with English subtitles \\r\\n| Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 21m  \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":81,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a06a03bb-bfef-440c-8b60-49e25cdb2fab.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Most Precious of Cargoes\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 April-1 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/a06a03bb-bfef-440c-8b60-49e25cdb2fab-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"500401AMJGGSPVVMMTQDHQNLQSLHVSPHK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-06T11:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-01T16:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Inspired by the true story of a disillusioned Englishman who went to work in a school in Argentina in 1976. Expecting an easy ride, Tom discovers a divided nation and a class of unteachable students. However, after he rescues a penguin from an oil-slicked beach, his life is turned upside-down. | Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 51m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":111,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/5ddc1fee-4806-4a11-ba2d-651ae4d81e8c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Penguin Lessons\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 May-8 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/5ddc1fee-4806-4a11-ba2d-651ae4d81e8c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506001AKBPBVBNBNBGQMMBGVTPJGNLMJD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-04T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-08T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £15, in building, 13+ // In 1930s Hungary, the future shimmered with promise for young pianist Stephen de Bastion. His life swirled with cocktails, romance, applause, and the vibrant energy of Budapest, echoing with music late into the night.   Then came 1939.  Stephen’s world collapsed. This is the story of his brutal descent—through forced labour camps, Mauthausen, Gunskirchen—and the unimaginable horrors he endured as a man of Jewish descent during the Holocaust. Yet, it is also a story of extraordinary escape, resilience, and the piano that waited for him.   Decades later, that same piano finds its way to Roxanne de Bastion, Stephen’s granddaughter, after the death of her father. It had been in the family for over a century, but it is only when Roxanne, deep in grief, discovers an old cassette recording of Stephen that the piano’s astonishing history—and her family's—begins to unfold.  Drawing on her grandfather’s original recordings, unpublished memoirs, letters, and documents, Roxanne intertwines music with storytelling to bring this extraordinary history to life.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Piano Player of Budapest\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 June-12 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"494401AQSKJGMPRCBHRSKBLNVHHGRBDCS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-12T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm–8.15pm, £15, building // Jack Fairweather in conversation with Jonathan Freedland. The Prosecutor tells the gripping true story of Fritz Bauer, a gay Jewish lawyer who returned to postwar Germany to seek justice for Holocaust crimes—only to find himself battling a nation eager to forget.  // As the Cold War took hold, the world moved on, leaving thousands of Nazi perpetrators unpunished. While the CIA funded Hitler’s former spies and Nazi-era laws remained in force, Bauer risked everything to hold his country accountable. His pursuit of Adolf Eichmann would pit him against his own government and a powerful network determined to silence him.  // Drawing on newly declassified records and exclusive interviews, Jack Fairweather unveils the hidden struggles behind the fight to establish the Holocaust’s legal legacy. The Prosecutor is a riveting portrait of one man’s defiance in the face of denial—and the price of forcing the world to confront the truth.  //\\r\\nJack Fairweather is an award-winning and bestselling British writer and journalist. His last book, The Volunteer, won the Costa Book Prize and was a #1 Sunday Times bestseller, hailed as a modern classic and compared to Schindler’s List. He splits his time between the UK and Vermont.   Jonathan Freedland is a Guardian columnist and former foreign correspondent. He is the presenter of BBC Radio 4’s contemporary history series, The Long View, as well as two podcasts, Politics Weekly America for the Guardian and Unholy, alongside the Israeli journalist Yonit Levi. He is a past winner of an Orwell Prize for journalism. The Escape Artist: The Man Who Broke Out of Auschwitz to Warn the World is his twelfth book. He is the author of nine thrillers, mostly as Sam Bourne, including The Righteous Men which was a Sunday Times number one bestseller.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Prosecutor\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 May-21 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488802ABPHGNCHNBCQVPGDRKJDLVBCQSR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-21T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-21T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jack Fairweather\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"After 20 years away, Odysseus washes up on the shores of Ithaca, haggard and unrecognizable. The King has returned from the Trojan War, but much has changed in his kingdom. His beloved wife Penelope is a prisoner in her own home, hounded by suitors vying to be king. Their son Telemachus faces death at the hands of these suitors, who see him as merely an obstacle to their pursuit of the kingdom. Odysseus has also changed--scarred by his experience of the Trojan war, he is no longer the mighty warrior from years past--but he must rediscover his strength in order to win back all that he has lost. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 56m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":116,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/fd2b39b1-5f63-40ca-8cc8-55905240ebae.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Return\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 May-8 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/fd2b39b1-5f63-40ca-8cc8-55905240ebae-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506201ASQNHJPMVDNGRKSMHGTNSGCCLNM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-04T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-08T16:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Winner of Best Documentary at the Jerusalem Film Festival, this film explores the life of Ka-Tzetnik, the mysterious writer who captivated millions with his haunting depiction of Auschwitz, famously calling it \\\"The Other Planet.\\\" However, when an experimental LSD treatment leads him to new insights, his revolutionary message is tragically overlooked. A powerful exploration of trauma, revelation, and the complexities of Ka-Tzetnik’s legacy. | This film is in Hebrew, Yiddish and English with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of adverts and trailers | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":81,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/cfefa7a8-b69e-4f2a-8893-521d62ef9cc8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Return From the Other Planet \",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/cfefa7a8-b69e-4f2a-8893-521d62ef9cc8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503401APTPRRCTMMMMNSMCMRRNJTVLVLP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When Iman is appointed as an investigating judge in Tehran, his family is thrust into the public eye when. As political unrest erupts in the streets, Iman realizes that his job is even more dangerous than expected, making him increasingly paranoid and distrustful, even of his own wife Najmeh and daughters Sana and Rezvan. | Rating: 15, Duration: 2h 47m | In Persian with English subtitles | Preceded by 10-20 minutes of trailers/ads.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":167,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/92ddce91-bc5b-4c64-ab08-079b4697384f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Seed of the Sacred Fig \",\"instanceDates\":\"10 March-13 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/92ddce91-bc5b-4c64-ab08-079b4697384f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480601AHJCGSGNGDDKBNVSQGRRKPTJGHQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-10T15:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-13T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.45pm, £20, hybrid // The State of Israel will be celebrating 77 years of independence after the longest war in its history. In addition, the future of Israeli democracy has never looked so uncertain. At the same time, Israeli society has achieved extraordinary levels of civic and patriotic solidarity in the face of this, and the Middle East has been radically transformed by Israel's military achievements.\\r\\n\\r\\nPaul Gross will try to make sense of these different lenses through which to view Israel after its 77th birthday.\\r\\n\\r\\nPaul Gross writes and lectures on Israeli and global politics. His writing can be found in a number of publications in Israel, the UK, and the US; and he has appeared as a political commentator on Israeli English-language news channels. In the months before 7 October, he was involved in the mass protests against the government, as one of the leaders of the “Olim for Democracy” movement. Paul moved to Israel from the UK in 2007 after working for the Home Office on legislation tackling religious discrimination, and for the Embassy of Israel in London as the Ambassador’s speechwriter. He has a Masters in Middle East Politics from the School of Oriental & African Studies (SOAS).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The State of Israel at 77 in a transformed Middle East\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 May-7 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"478601AJRVLGRVNDLHLLKMLGJNPDNMDJP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-07T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-07T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Israel & the Middle East\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paul Gross\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"118 // 15// Physicist congress in Alps encounters Iranian guest, mysterious pianist. Bizarre cloud, underground booming. Quantum mechanical thriller unravels amidst enigmatic events. Black and white setting.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":118,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Universal Theory\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-8 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"470202ANSVGQHBJCSVCQQTGRQPPGPTQPR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-05T17:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-08T14:20:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"From Director Andrew Ahn comes a joyful comedy of errors about a chosen family navigating cultural identity, queerness, and family expectations. Frustrated with his commitment-phobic boyfriend Chris and running out of time, Min makes a proposal: a green-card marriage with their friend Angela in exchange for her partner Lee's expensive IVF. Elopement plans are upended, however, when Min's grandmother surprises them with an extravagant Korean wedding banquet. Starring Bowen Yang, Lily Gladstone, Kelly Marie Tran, Han Gi-chan, Joan Chen, and Youn Yuh-jung, The Wedding Banquet is a poignant and heartfelt reminder that being part of a family means learning to both accept and forgive. | Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 42m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":102,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d2f9453b-a7c8-4402-9b75-dd05af271452.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Wedding Banquet\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/d2f9453b-a7c8-4402-9b75-dd05af271452-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507203AGKMPHNLLSSLLMVRLRRHQTJRQPT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-25T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T17:50:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The incredible, untold true story of how a group of prisoners attempt a seemingly impossible escape from the first Nazi death camp in order to provide the first eyewitness account of the Holocaust. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 15, Duration: 1h 49m\\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":109,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c0a11310-57dc-4c7c-b5b2-5768706d9b96.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The World Will Tremble\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-1 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/c0a11310-57dc-4c7c-b5b2-5768706d9b96-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"499401APGNHRMRMDGVSPSQMKVTLGNCLNR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-01T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"8pm-10pm, £20 Early Bird, £25 Standard, £40 VIP (Pre-show meet and greet, selfie opportunity, and front row seat) // 18+ // Following Tova's sell out European tour in 2024 she is back with the same show by popular demand! From the 'mental load' and 'rushing woman syndrome' to hot flashes and why the secret to a healthy marriage is sleeping in different bedrooms, join bestselling author and global internet sensation Tova Leigh as she spills the beans on all things marriage, perimenopause, parenting and more. From C Section shelfs to nights sweats, feminism and the death of her libido, this show, much like her online videos and books, is filled with real life relatable and hilarious stories about all the things no one ever talks about.\\r\\n\\r\\nTova's opening act will be the incredibly talented Riona O'Connor.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Tova Leigh: Honey, I'm Losing It! \",\"instanceDates\":\"24 July-24 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488401AVHBJMCDVBGGGRMHNJPJJMTVPNT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-24T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-24T20:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Tova Leigh\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A group of clever East Germans seizes the chaotic post-GDR era in 1990 to retrieve hidden millions from an underground vault. As they outsmart formidable opponents, the heist takes an unexpected turn when money officially unrecognized in the GDR circulates. | This film is in German with English subtitles | Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 53m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":113,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9df417da-3cc9-4806-9068-5a0e77296183.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Two to One\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9df417da-3cc9-4806-9068-5a0e77296183-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"507801ADMQGVJJJLQBJMGTPQCVPGVMTHJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-26T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T20:10:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, building only // We are thrilled to welcome Patrick Bade back to JW3 and he will take you on a virtual tour of The National Gallery's winter blockbuster \\\"Van Gogh: Poets and lovers\\\" containing some of the artists most beloved and famous pictures drawn from collections around the world. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis thrilling exhibition attempts to present a fresh view of Van Gogh and his art. He emerges as less the tormented and doomed figure of popular imagination but instead, in the words of the National Gallery  \\\"an artist of lucid intention, deliberation and great imagination.\\\" Few artists in the history of Western art pack the emotional impact of Van Gogh. From across the wide spaces of the National Gallery rooms his paintings have an almost visceral effect with their singing colours and bold brushwork.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Van Gogh: Poets & Lovers\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"456201AJHHGVRDGJMVPRTNBVPNPHNBLDB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-12T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-12T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Film will be preceded by approx 20m of ads/trailers  // 1h 59m , Rating: 15 //\\r\\n\\r\\nThis film is in Italian with English subtitles.  \\r\\n\\r\\n1944. In Vermiglio, a high mountain village of the Italian Alps where war looms as a distant but constant threat. The arrival of Pietro, a refugee soldier, disrupts the dynamics of the local teacher’s family, changing them forever.  \\r\\n\\r\\nCredits \\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\nGenre: Drama, History \\r\\nDirector: Maura Delpero  \\r\\nStars: Tommaso Ragno, Roberta Rovelli, Martina Scrinzi  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":119,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Vermiglio\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 February-6 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"476401ACGBHRHNGHHDJNCHQMJJHBTVDSM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-02T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-06T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Margy Kinmonth’s feature documentary shines a light on the trailblazing role of women war artists, on the front lines round the world, championing the female perspective on conflict through art and asking: when it's life or death, what do women see that men don't?  Traditionally a male domain, war art by women has been largely unrecognised. Until now... \\r\\nCulture breaks the taboo, crosses borders - tells the truth to power. Artists featured include Dame Rachel Whiteread, Zhanna Kadyrova, Maggi Hambling, Assil Diab, Dame Laura Knight, Marcelle Hanselaar, Cornelia Parker, Maya Lin, Shirin Neshat and Lee Miller. An entirely female cast of contributors makes this film a unique undertaking – telling vital truths in turbulent times.  \\r\\nWar Paint – Women At War is the third instalment in Kinmonth’s trilogy of films about how artists depict war, following the acclaimed Eric Ravilious – Drawn To War and War Art with Eddie Redmayne. \\r\\n\\r\\n| Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 29m  \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":89,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6ab63387-f7e9-4ceb-854a-ffc81e6d72f1.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"War Paint: Women at War\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-16 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/6ab63387-f7e9-4ceb-854a-ffc81e6d72f1-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"500801ANDBLLHNBRTTKKLBNJHNJQRMNBG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-15T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-16T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"108 // 15 // An up-and-coming chef and a recent divorcée find their lives forever changed when a chance encounter brings them together, in a decade-spanning, deeply moving romance.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":108,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"We Live in Time\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 January-30 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"471601APHNMSRBBTVVNCKQKLKJGTKQVGR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-20T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-30T18:10:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"After a tumultuous life in Paris, Michelle has retired to a quiet existence in Burgundy, tending her garden and attending services at her parish. The voracious hostility of her adult daughter Valérie remains Michelle’s great puzzlement: how can a child for whom she sacrificed so much treat her with such contempt and suspicion? When Valérie drops off her son for a week with his grandmother, Michelle sees an opportunity to repair the relationship, but a culinary accident soon undercuts whatever trust remains. With the help of her best friend Marie-Claude, whose son has recently been released from prison, Michelle plots a path towards restoring the family life so long denied her. With a deceptively placid surface, master stylist François Ozon cooks up a twisty and destabilizing thriller where family ties remain the most mysterious ingredient of all. \\r\\n\\r\\n| This film is French with English subtitles. \\r\\n| Rating: 12A, Duration: 1h 42m \\r\\n| All films will be preceded by 10-20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":102,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/92acd3d2-ce13-45d3-88da-132c755a5f99.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"When Autumn Falls\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/92acd3d2-ce13-45d3-88da-132c755a5f99-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"498801ALJDGSKCSBVSCNLVHPPKKTGQCVV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-15T16:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-17T14:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9.15pm, £15, in building // 20 min interval at 8pm // Written by Rachel Bellman, Nick Cassenbaum, Noga Flaishon, Annabel Gaba and Tariq Jordan \\r\\n\\r\\nDirected by Hannah Hauer-King \\r\\n\\r\\n“When have you felt most connected to your Jewish identity?”\\r\\n“What gives you the most hope?”\\r\\n“Tell us something you wouldn’t tell your Rabbi…”\\r\\n\\r\\nInspired by real testimonies from Jews around the world, When We Listen is a brand new collection of short plays, interrogating the past twelve months of Jewish life, and where the next twelve months might take us.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Pinner to Perth, Golders Green to Golden Gate Bridge, over fifty real interviews inspire six original stories in this brand new collection of searing new plays.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease note this event is a semi-staged reading and actors will be script in hand.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"When We Listen: The Past Year of Jewish Life\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 March-4 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"479601ASCGRKGNVLQPCPNCRQVCPPBTPRP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-04T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-04T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am – 12.15pm, £20 per session or £90 for the 5 weeks // The Jewish world has produced many remarkable personalities over the last century but how many of them will be found to have left a lasting mark on the story of the Jews?\\r\\n\\r\\nIn this series, Clive will consider some of our best-known near-contemporaries and speculate on whether or not they will figure in an account of the Jews in the generations to follow. \\r\\n\\r\\nAwarded an OBE for his contribution to the community, Clive is an educational consultant, a magistrate and a regular presenter around the world.\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Will any Jews of the 20th Century survive into Jewish History? [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 February-25 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452201ATTDGKSTCKTDQHVHQDNHRGNLBHJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-25T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-25T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Clive Lawton\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am – 12.15pm, £20 per session or £90 for the 5 weeks // The Jewish world has produced many remarkable personalities over the last century but how many of them will be found to have left a lasting mark on the story of the Jews? In this series, Clive will consider some of our best-known near-contemporaries and speculate on whether or not they will figure in an account of the Jews in the generations to follow. Awarded an OBE for his contribution to the community, Clive is an educational consultant, a magistrate and a regular presenter around the world.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Will any Jews of the 20th Century survive into Jewish History? [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 February-25 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"452401ARPHKCKNJRGGKMKCCHQJJSTVJCN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-25T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-25T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Clive Lawton\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £15, in building // Willy Meisl was a trailblazing Austrian-Jewish sports journalist who revolutionised the field during the Weimar Republic.  \\r\\n\\r\\nA product of Vienna’s vibrant coffeehouse culture, he brought intellectual depth to sports writing, exploring professionalism, tactics, and sporting history with the flair of a cultural critic.   \\r\\n\\r\\nKnown as the \\\"King of the Sports Journalists,\\\" Meisl’s influence was unmatched.   But with the rise of the Nazis, his focus shifted. Forced into exile, he turned his sharp pen to the roots of Nazism, its reign of terror, and the myths of racial ideology that upended his life.  \\r\\n\\r\\nMeisl also became a leading sports journalist in Britain after the war and a critic of English football, which he considered to be far behind Central Europe. To be a leading journalist in one country and then a highly influential journalist in a foreign language after fleeing for his life speaks to his remarkable adaptability and intellect.     \\r\\n\\r\\nThis volume gathers his most powerful writings on these themes, presented in their original German with English introductions. A forgotten pioneer of interwar journalism, Meisl’s work remains as urgent and insightful today as it was in his time.    \\r\\n\\r\\nAuthors Darren O’ Bryne and Christopher Young will be in conversation with David Bolchover, author, commentator and business writer. His latest book is “The Greatest Comeback: From Genocide to Football Glory”, a biography of the football coach Béla Guttmann. The book was shortlisted for the William Hill Sports Book of the Year. David is currently writing a book on great Jewish footballers throughout Europe who were murdered in the Holocaust. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Willy Meisl: 'King of Sports Journalists'\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-5 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492001ASVLNKSLKRHMVTVLGBTDSTKMTRM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wind, Tide & Oar is a compelling exploration of engineless sailing, shot on analogue film over three years. The film delves into the experiences of those who travel solely by harnessing the natural elements alone, following a diverse array of traditional boats and uncovering the unique rhythms and motivations of engineless navigation.\\r\\n\\r\\nJourneying through rivers, coastlines, and open seas, spanning the UK, the Netherlands, and France, Wind, Tide & Oar creates a contemplative space, addressing themes of ecology, heritage, traditional skills, and maritime history. Using a 1960s hand-wound camera, Wahl offers a poetic and intimate perspective on a millennia-old craft, upended by the invention of mechanised power.\\r\\n\\r\\nThrough the film’s reveries, sailing becomes a means to explore our interaction with and responsibility to the environment. It invites deep reflection on our relationship with nature, our understanding of and commitment to sustainability, and our care for the world around us. | Rating: PG, Duration: 1h 24m | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":84,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/ec9afcfd-8ae7-4674-b074-d12d572f1151.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Wind, Tide & Oar\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/ec9afcfd-8ae7-4674-b074-d12d572f1151-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"506601ARQKJQVKDBVJTJPLKCTHPLVRNDV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-13T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Women of Worth Walking Tour // 2hr // 11am-1pm // £20 //\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin Rachel Kolsky, author and tour guide, to celebrate International Women’s Day by discovering the stories of Jewish and non-Jewish women alike who made a significant impact on the Jewish community of the East End. As you explore the backstreets of Whitechapel and Spitalfields, stories you will hear include those associated with Alice Model and her maternity hospital, Miriam Moses and her youth work, the philanthropy of the Rothschild ladies, suffragette and local politician Minnie Lansbury, and local GP, Hannah Billig.\\r\\n\\r\\nDesigner: Please kindly provide an image for this walking tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nFurthermore, the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Women of Worth \",\"instanceDates\":\"6 March-6 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455601AKRVCHVTNQBBRRJNGKGPHDHSTLB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-06T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"False\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Kolsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £10 per session or £30 for all 4 sessions, in building // \\r\\nWed 13 Nov: Sexual Health and Female Pleasure \\r\\nWed 11 Dec: Pregnancy and Postpartum Health\\r\\nWed 22 Jan: Breast Health for All Ages\\r\\nWed 26 Feb: Perimenopause, Menopause, and Beyond\\r\\n\\r\\n// Join Dr Emily Simon for this four-part series exploring essential topics in female health. Each session dives into a different topic, with expert insight from Dr Simon and her guest speakers, Dr Emily Simon and guests Miss Joanna Franks and Katie Taylor. // This series is safe and welcoming space open to everyone, regardless of age, gender identity, gender expression, and sexual orientation. We welcome everyone to come and engage with these essential topics. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Women's Health Series\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 January-20 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"444601ADCBLPLDNGQHGTVSQVLCLVRSDTJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-20T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"English\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dr Emily Simon\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12noon, £72 for 4 weeks, building only // The events of World War II have inspired countless films, but how did filmmaking in the 1940s inform, influence and persuade audiences during the war years?  // This course will explore diverse kinds of wartime filmmaking, including documentary, newsreel, drama and comedy. Through analysing key films and their associated artistic movements and cultural contexts, we can see how contemporary attitudes were shaped and reflected by film. Lectures will be illustrated with film clips. //  \\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 1: ‘Why We Fight’: Documentary and propaganda // \\r\\nWeek 2: ‘London Can Take it!’: British newsreel and government sponsored films // \\r\\nWeek 3: Innovations and emotions in Italian Neorealism // \\r\\nWeek 4: Entertainment and escape in popular drama and comedy  // Dr Julia Wagner is a lecturer and writer specialising in Jewish-interest film and television. She holds a PhD in Film Studies and is a member of the London Film Critics’ Circle. Her writing has been published widely, including by the BFI, Sight & Sound and The Jewish Chronicle. From 2017-23, she curated JW3/BFI archive project, Jewish Britain on Film.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"World War II on Film\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-26 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"488601APHMVDCGVTNSBCCCGBKVVGTTDMB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-26T10:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Julia Wagner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"As part of Erez Tadmor's retrospective, experience the intense drama of a brutal terror attack in Haifa. A suicide bomber detonates a bomb, injuring himself and many victims, leading to chaos at a nearby hospital. The story follows various characters —police officers, medical staff, and victims — caught in the turmoil. Among them is Kobi Amar, a police officer torn between his duty to secure the terrorist and the growing worry for his missing son. A powerful look at family, duty, and moral conflict during a night of crisis. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. Part of the Seret Film Festival | Duration: 80 minutes, Rating TBC | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":80,\"imageUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9df321cd-c388-4f73-aadd-8ae2a707f519.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Wounded Land + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://sysfilessacbe149174fee.blob.core.windows.net/public-container/clients/jw3/files/9df321cd-c388-4f73-aadd-8ae2a707f519-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502001AJRRMNRVHTVBNPDJKQRLLLBRBDM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-11T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, free, in building // Memorial event for the Israeli soldiers and victims of terror. The ceremony will be conducted in English and feature personal stories and songs. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Yom HaZikaron Memorial\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 April-28 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"508001AGGPTCGSJQGQVQDRDCHRCKKKGTJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-28T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm - 9pm, in building, £20 // Ever fancied baking your own challah fresh for Shabbat? Join us for a hands-on workshop where we'll prepare everyone’s favourite traditional Jewish bread from scratch. Enjoy a light summer dinner and connect with fellow bakers while the dough rises, then learn different techniques to create unique braiding designs to take home and bake for Shabbat!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 & Young Kisharon Langdon: Challah Bake\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 September-4 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487403ARCKMGCPLGCNDSBCMDVVQLMQMQR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-04T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-09-04T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6-10pm, £25, building // A magical summer BBQ Shabbat dinner under the open sky on our JW3 Beach. Enjoy a delicious spread of grilled favourites and a warm, relaxing atmosphere. Come hungry, bring your friends, and let's make it a night to remember!  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Friday Night Dinner: Summer BBQ on the Beach \",\"instanceDates\":\"29 August-29 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"489204ANTTPKGDNQDLVJPQMTTKDDKHSPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-08-29T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-08-29T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £15, in building // Listen to and understand the powerful music of Israeli pop artists — both new and established —who, after the shock of 7th October, have crafted a musical tapestry that reflects a wide range of national and personal emotions. In this session, join Young JW3 and expert Israel Tour Guide, Josh Hartuv, as we explore the pop songs that have resonated most and moved the soul, as well as the impact of radio broadcasts on the public. Light refreshments will be provided.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Heartbeats & Hits: Israeli Pop in Times of Turmoil\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-2 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"478801ADQSKCDMSSGVNVBTTQBDPMRNRBB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Josh Hartuv\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6-10pm, £30, building // Celebrate Lag Ba'Omer with an evening of dance, community and celebration. Start with a lively Israeli folk dance class led by Liat Oberlander from the Israeli Dance Institute, followed by candle lighting to bring in Shabbat. Enjoy an aromatic Israeli-inspired dinner filled with delicious food, fine wine and great company.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Lag Ba’Omer Israeli Dance Class & Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 May-16 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"490402ACPTPKPQRPMVPVGMHJVQLLQTMRB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-16T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-16T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"£10 movie / £16 pizza & movie, 7.15pm-9.30pm // Join us for our monthly queer movie screening and pizza party at the JW3 cinema! We will be watching 'Who's Gonna Love Me Now?' (2016), a heartfelt exploration of one man’s struggle to reconcile with his Israeli family, while finding a new chosen family in London Gay Men’s Chorus.\\r\\n\\r\\n7.30pm - Pizza party\\r\\n8.15pm - Film starts\\r\\n9.45pm - Film ends\\r\\n\\r\\nVegan pizza available upon request.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Queer Movie & Pizza Night: Who's Gonna Love Me Now?\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"473201APMSCJNHVQJLCPSRRJNLJJLMCRJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-05T19:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-7.30pm Social, 7.30pm-9pm TamaRadah Concert, £16 including concert ticket // 20s and 30s // Join us for an exciting evening of music, conversation, and connection! \\r\\nWe’ll kick things off at the JW3 Café, where you can grab a drink and snack and enjoy chatting with others from the group. Then we'll join an unforgettable live performance by TamaRadah. It’s the perfect chance to unwind after work and meet new people who share your passion for music and culture. Don’t miss out!\\r\\n\\r\\nTimings:\\r\\n6.30-7.30pm - Social in the Café\\r\\n7.30-9pm - TamaRadah concert in the Hall\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout TamaRadah:\\r\\nTamaRadah is an extraordinary Ethiopian folk singer, captivating audiences with her fusion of African-Caribbean grooves and the rich heritage of Ethiopian music.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor Tamar, this harmonious fusion of cultures beautifully mirrors the essence of a contemporary world an exuberant and diverse society assembled like a vibrant cultural puzzle from all corners of the globe. \\r\\n\\r\\nAmidst the constellation of iconic names in the music scene, Tamar Radah shines as a trailblazing artist carving her own path to stardom. At 35 years old, she is not only an independent music creator but also a promising talent hailing from the esteemed \\\"Rimon\\\" music academy.\\r\\n\\r\\nAs the lead singer of her band, TamaRadah, she shares stages with living music legends. Over the years, Tamar has impressively written, composed, and produced three albums, collaborating with some of the finest musicians, including Ehud Banai, Ariel Horowitz, Idan Reichel, Ester Rada, and Doron Talmon (Jane Bordeaux).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Social & TamaRadah Concert\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 July-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"504801AJMTSHDJRDQDKJHRSHDTGLGLDCM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-10T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-7.30pm Pizza Party, 7.3pm-9.30pm Film, £10 ticket + £6 for pizza // Join us for our next Queer Movie & Pizza Night! This time, we’re screening Pink Lady (2024), a touching and uplifting comedy-drama which follows a young modern woman’s journey to self-discovery and liberation.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe’re proud to partner with the Seret International Film Festival, the leading showcase of Israeli cinema around the globe. Since 2012, Seret has been bringing UK audiences the best of Israeli feature films, documentaries, shorts, and TV, offering a unique window into Israeli society, culture, and storytelling. Learn more about Seret here: https://www.seret-international.org/\\r\\n\\r\\nFilm Synopsis\\r\\nIn an ultra-Orthodox Jewish community in Jerusalem, Bati seems to have the perfect life—happily married to Lazer with three children. But when Lazer is blackmailed, she uncovers his secret affair with his male study partner. Determined to hold her family together, Bati supports Lazer’s attempts to “cure” his homosexuality—only to discover her own hidden desires along the way.\\r\\nCome and celebrate queer stories and Israeli cinema with us in a warm and welcoming space. See you there!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":166,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Seret Film Festival: Pink Lady\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"505001ABVHCMVCSJKDQVRMVLBJCDJCPNN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-12T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.15pm-9.30pm, £15, in building // COPY TO BE UPDATED\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":195,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x UJIA Eurovision Watch Party\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 May-15 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"498401APJMCCSKLGTJDGGLHMNKPRRLGGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T18:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-15T18:15:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £10, in building // Make the new year a little bit sweeter and join us for our babka bake!\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you’re a seasoned baker or trying your hand for the first time, this event is the perfect chance to mix, knead and swirl your way to a delicious treat. You’ll have the choice of classic chocolate or comforting cinnamon sugar fillings to create your own babka masterpiece. \\r\\n\\r\\nWe’ll provide all the ingredients and guidance, with hot drinks to enjoy during the morning. \\r\\n\\r\\nBring a friend or come on your own and meet new ones. See you there!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Babka Bake\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"473001ATKVDLJPHBBDSJMQTDRKVGQQLTQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-26T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8pm, £10 per session or £30 for all 4, in building // Join us for this breathwork and meditation series, led by Lucy Feld. \\r\\nLucy is a passionate breathwork and meditation teacher based in London, dedicated to helping people connect with their breath in a way that feels right for them. She creates a welcoming space, guiding class participants through carefully sequenced, breath-centred practices. With a teaching style that is both thoughtful and inclusive, Lucy aims to help practitioners cultivate deep presence and ease. She is committed to dispelling the notion that you need to sit a certain way or be a particular type of person to benefit from meditation and breathwork, believing that everyone can experience positive change by simply taking a few moments each day to be present with their breath. //\\r\\n\\r\\n14 January: Grounding Ourselves in the New Year\\r\\n12 February: Taking 5 in the Office\\r\\n5 March: Sleep Easy\\r\\n29 April: Self Compassion\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Breathwork Series\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 January-29 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"445002APNCDSBBJQRNTNSNJGDRVNDNHHD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-14T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-29T19:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Sun 18 May 2025 // \\r\\n2:00pm // \\r\\n£30 // Actor Elliott Leigh presents a surreal and immersive comedy improv half-day workshop focused on creating absurd sketches inspired by classic Jewish motifs. We’ll collaboratively improvise, play, and explore mime, clowning, and Charlie Chaplin-style non-verbal acting to generate material for reels and short movies.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Comedy & Improv Workshop: Revenge of the Fish Balls!\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"487801AQHGHJPRTKRHTGVGHJVPDMNNLDC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-18T14:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Elliott Leigh\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm-7.30pm, show from 7.30pm-9.30pm, £25, in building // £5 ticket for networking ONLY // Join us for an exclusive evening designed for young professionals in the creative industries! This event offers a unique opportunity to connect, network, and share ideas, followed by a special musical preview of the electrifying new show, RISE.\\r\\n\\r\\nTimings:\\r\\n6.30pm - Young JW3 networking drinks\\r\\n7.30pm - RISE concert & discussion\\r\\n\\r\\nCome and meet like-minded individuals, expand your network, and explore exciting creative projects happening in London and beyond. Feel free to bring business cards and flyers to showcase the projects you're passionate about.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout RISE:\\r\\n\\r\\nRISE is a modern rock musical about a group of Jewish women resistance fighters during the Holocaust who wage an uprising against the Nazi regime.\\r\\n\\r\\nSet in Eastern Europe at the height of the Holocaust, RISE tells a story of courage, loyalty, sacrifice, and love, focusing on a group of young women who work as spies, smugglers, and leaders of the underground Jewish resistance as they organize and wage an uprising against the Nazi regime. \\r\\n\\r\\nEnjoy a special concert performance of the show that Broadway World calls \\\"a daring and important new musical\\\" with a \\\"superb score.\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowed by a discussion with the writer/composer, Joshua Daniel Hershfield.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":210,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Creative Industries Networking + RISE Pre Drinks\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"480001ATGGMSLDTQLPGMNQMKCPSJJGBNH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-03-19T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"bookings closed // 6pm-10.10pm, £25, building // Join us for a special Young JW3 Friday Night Dinner for LGBTQ+ individuals across the spectrum on Valentine's Day, in partnership with Sapphic Shabbat. Now in its third year, Sapphic Shabbat is a group that curates intimate Shabbat dinners designed to help guests build new connections in a welcoming, low-pressure environment. This larger gathering at JW3 will celebrate the warmth and tradition of Shabbat, offering the perfect opportunity to meet new people and make lasting friendships. The evening will also serve as a digital detox zone, giving everyone a chance to unwind and disconnect after the week. Whether you're attending solo or with friends, come and enjoy delicious food, meaningful conversation, and a night full of joy, connection, and community.\\r\\n\\r\\nTimings: \\r\\n6:00pm - Doors open and welcome drinks\\r\\n6:30pm - Shabbat dinner*\\r\\n10:00pm - Carriages\\r\\n\\r\\n*Vegetarian and gluten free food available upon request. Please specify any dietary requirements during checkout, or contact gianina@jw3.org.uk\\r\\n\\r\\nMore about Sapphic Shabbat:\\r\\nSapphic Shabbat is a Jewish sapphic group, inclusive of non-binary and trans folk who identify as lesbian, bisexual, pansexual, wlw, transmasc, and transfemme. They organise curated Shabbat dinners for small groups so guests can make new connections in a low-pressure environment. Sapphic Shabbat also hosts open meet-ups that welcome the wider Jewish queer community and allies.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":250,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: LGBTQ+ Valentine's Friday Night Dinner with Sapphic Shabbat\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 February-14 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"473401APKJSQRHHJKPQMPQGRGRVGCDPSD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-14T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-14T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm-10pm, £25, in building // Please join us for the first Young JW3 Friday Night Dinner of the new year, where we will come together as a community to partake in Jami Mental Health Shabbat 2025.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe all have mental health and it is just as important as our physical health. Starting a conversation about mental health is an excellent way to challenge the stigma and get people thinking and talking about their perceptions of mental health and mental illness. During our Shabbat dinner we will have the opportunity for introspection, sharing insights and learning about Jami's impactful work to enrich and save lives impacted by mental illness in the Jewish community.\\r\\n\\r\\n6:00pm - Doors open and welcome drinks\\r\\n6:30pm - Shabbat dinner*\\r\\n10:00pm - Carriages\\r\\n\\r\\n*Vegetarian and gluten free food available upon request. Please contact Gianina at gianina@jw3.org.uk ASAP upon booking with any other dietary requirements.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Mental Health and Wellbeing Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 January-31 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472001AVBNSGGRPHVGTBKKJVHCPMPNGDH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-31T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-31T18:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thu 05 June 2025 //\\r\\n6:30pm // \\r\\n£20 // Shake, stir, and sip your way through a lively summer social! Join us for a hands-on cocktail and mocktail masterclass, where you'll learn to craft delicious, refreshing drinks while mingling with great company. We’ll kick off the evening with a light summer dinner, then dive into the art of crafting the perfect pour— suitable for beginners and seasoned shakers alike!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Summer Cocktail Masterclass\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 June-5 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"485003APNKLNRBTNHKRTLGBCSVGQQLNCP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-05T18:30:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nini\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £15, in building // Participants meet in the restaurant, will move to LR2 for the Tai Chi // Join us for Tai Chi & Chai Tea, a unique wellness event designed to cultivate and harmonise mind and body through gentle and flowing movements. Start your Sunday morning with a warm cup of chai tea in our cosy café, then transition into a gentle Tai Chi Chaun taster session. Immerse yourself in the flowing, meditative movements of Tai Chi Chaun, an ancient Chinese art that promotes flexibility, coordination, strength, and balance. No prior experience is necessary—this session is for everyone! Our instructor, a member of the Tai Chi Union of Great Britain, will guide you through the basics in a welcoming and supportive environment. It's the perfect way to nourish both your body and mind while meeting new people.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Tai Chi & Chai Tea\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 February-23 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"478001ANQNMSNHPTQJTQMHTGGMNLKVJRC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-23T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-02-23T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Shira Klasmer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thu 29 May 2025 //\\r\\n6:45pm // \\r\\n£20 // Join us for a glow-in-the-dark painting experience where we'll explore the meaning of dreams through the lens of the Talmud, Rebbe Nachman, and Carl Jung. After discussing these dream concepts, we’ll mind map and visualise our own personal dreamscapes as inspiration for creating expressive UV glowing artwork with phosphorescent colours.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":165,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: The Dream Project: Glow in the Dark Painting Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 May-29 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"486802ARGRNNVTMJJPGQNTJDGTCTMNMGJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T18:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-29T18:45:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Elliott Leigh\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £15 // For those in their 20s, 30s, and 40s // Join us for a laid-back morning filled with classic board games and exciting new ones. You'll have the chance to try different games, make new friends, and enjoy light breakfast refreshments—all in a relaxed, friendly atmosphere. It's the perfect way to kick back and enjoy a summer Sunday!\\r\\n\\r\\nBring your friends, bring your competitive spirit, and we’ll see you there!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3+ Board Games & Breakfast\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 July-20 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"505201AQDHLHJJNHCCKJNDRKVKTSMSGQD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-20T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-07-20T11:00:00\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"}]"
          },
