ita Lasker-Wallfisch, the last living survivor from the camp orchestras, whose testimony frames this powerful documentary. The film examines the SS&#039;s perverse relationship with music—forcing prisoners to perform for their entertainment and accompany slave labourers, turning art into another form of torture.\" />\n<meta name=\"abstract\" content=\"https://www.jw3.org.uk/whats-on/last-musician-auschwitz\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"JW3\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.jw3.org.uk/whats-on/last-musician-auschwitz\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The Last Musician of Auschwitz\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"How can there be music in the worst place in the world? The Last Musician of Auschwitz reveals how music became a lifeline and form of resistance amid the Holocaust&#039;s horrors.\nAt its center is 99-year-old cellist Anita Lasker-Wallfisch, the last living survivor from the camp orchestras, whose testimony frames this powerful documentary. The film examines the SS&#039;s perverse relationship with music—forcing prisoners to perform for their entertainment and accompany slave labourers, turning art into another form of torture.\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://www.jw3.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/meta_facebook/public/images/The%20Last%20Musician%20of%20Auschwitz%201.jpg?itok=Dm2aMadP\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\" />\n<meta property=\"og:updated_time\" content=\"2025-04-23T17:35:40+01:00\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@JW3London\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"The Last Musician of Auschwitz | JW3\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.jw3.org.uk/whats-on/last-musician-auschwitz\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:image:height\" content=\"500\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:image:width\" content=\"1500\" />\n<met